window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":5801,"title":"Chapter 5801: Chapter 5800: No Immensity! II","paragraphs":["The severed Root lay in the snow where Minerva had fallen, green and broken and faintly smoking, and the frost crept across it from the broken end.","No Progeny stirred on the golden clouds. No Keeper stepped forward. Above, on their ring of floating thrones, the Immense Ones sat as still as the statues on the mountain’s flanks, and not one of them spoke.","Only the snow moved!","And then, very slowly, it began to change!","It thickened first. The steady fall that had covered the Legacy since THE Long Night began grew heavier, and heavier still, flakes crowding the air until the far thrones blurred and the edge of the Plain vanished into white. Thicker than anyone on the mountain had ever seen it. Thicker than anyone in the Legacy had ever seen it!","Then the wind came!","It came out of nowhere. There had been no wind on THE Firmament Mountain in all the time Noah had stood there, only the quiet fall, and now there was a wind that howled! It tore across the Plain in a single screaming gust and the snowfall became a blizzard, whipping sideways, stinging, roaring over the golden clouds and the thrones and away across the Legacy.","Noah felt it spread. Across every Elsedimension Mountain in every direction, the black glass peaks and the green ones and the one that burned sullen red, the blizzard came howling down. It tore acros the purple-gold rivers on the Legacy’s floor and whipped them into white-capped waves. It shook the thousands of domains hanging in the sky like lanterns in a storm!","All around the Plain, the Keepers moved at once. Authority rose off them, and Dimensionality with it, spreading out in shields over the clouds of the beings they served. Verys stood behind Noah with one webbed hand raised, and the blizzard broke through.","Conduit Lifeforms scattered from the pillars in bright, frightened flocks, chiming in alarm, and vanished into the white! The golden clouds rocked on the wind.","And then existence began to speak!","There was no voice. There was no cognizance with a name above it, no speaker at all. The knowledge simply arrived, in Noah and in every being on the Plain at the same instant, as cold arrives in the bones on a winter night. Nobody told it to you. You simply knew it, all at once, and could not stop knowing it.","| THE FIRST FROST HAS FALLEN.|","|No new Immensity shall arise.|","|Any Root that attempts to complete itself shall undergo IMMENSE SEVERING.|","|THE COUNTING HAS BEGUN. Existence now counts every Root. Each Root makes the cold heavier upon every other Root, and upon all others besides.|","...!","Every being on the Plain went still inside the howling storm!","On the golden clouds, Progeny and Provenance Lifeforms went pale. The water-woman’s glowing fish went dark all at once. The stag’s bells stopped ringing. Batiatus, who had not stopped talking since he arrived, sat with his mouth open and nothing coming out of it!","Dravos, still being tended at the edge of the Plain, lifted his broken helm toward the sky. More than one of them pressed a hand flat against their chest, over the place where their Root sat, as if they could hold it still.","Above, the thrones perceived it too! Noah felt them take it in, all of them, the vast presences flickering behind the storm. On the throne of black glass, the embers went out entirely. The hollowed star dimmed. Even the hazes, which no one could see, seemed to draw in on themselves, as though something very large had just felt a draft of coldness.","Noah looked at his hands as he...only he did not feel the cold as terrifying as all others did.","But a weight arrived even for him.","It settled onto his Root without any fuss at all. It was there, a pressure that had not existed a heartbeat ago, sitting on the turning mobius at the center of him like snow gathring on a roof. And as he felt it land, he understood with a cold, clean certainty that it would only ever get heavier.","Noah’s expression grew heavy.","Beside him, on the next cloud, Achilles had gritted his teeth. The frost on his lashes thickened as the blizzard poured past him, and inside him Noah could feel the new Root, barely a day old, flicker under the added weight.","Noah sat very still on his cloud, and thought.","Only days ago, he had sat down with THE Writer of Mythos and begun writing a Narrative together. A small thing, it had seemed. One thread pulled, and then another, until Vakochev had been called forth, and an Immense One had died, and waves of cold had poured out of the corpse, and a Hollow Night Lifeform wearing Lucy’s face had risen out of it.","It had only gotten colder since!","And now this. He had come to a Convocation of Roots meaning only to watch and learn. A Progeny of an Immense One had singled him out, fought him, tried to become Immense to prove him wrong, and failed. And because she failed, here was a harder winter than any before it!","No new Immensity, ever. And a cold that grew heavier with every single Root that dared to exist.","All these fucking things kept happening!","He knew he had not caused them. Not really. The Writer had written; Vakochev had come; Minerva had chosen her own gamble. But every time he moved, the winter seemed to grow teeth.","Did he simply need to not fucking do anything? Sit in his Existential Root Domain and never come out? Because it felt, sitting here in the howling snow, that the more he moved, the more everything around him deteriorated!","And then there was the other thing!","It came to him slowly, as he turned the information over, and he did not like it at all.","The Counting did not only press on Roots. Upon every other Root, and upon all others besides, existence had said. All others. Even the Immense Ones would be heavily affected, then. Even the thrones above him would feel the cold grow heavier with every Root that existed.","Which meant that anyone who wanted the cold to ease on themselves now had a very simple way to do it.","Fewer Roots!","If you were an Immense One, and the winter sat heavier on you for every young Root counted beneath you, then every Root that stopped existing would make your own winter a little lighter. Just a little. Just enough to be worth thinking about.","Noah’s expression grew heavier still!","He lifted his head and looked up through the blizzard at the ring of floating thrones.","The snow was so thick now that he could barely see them. Only shapes. The black glass. The bone. The living leaf, empty now. The hollowed star. The hazes. Great vague presences sitting in the storm above the Plain, looking down at the golden clouds where every being with a Root of Immensity sat pale and still.","And it felt, suddenly, as though he were looking up at countless pairs of eyes.","Chilly eyes. Calm eyes. Eyes that had just been handed a very simple sum, and were looking down at him, and at Achilles, and at every other Root on the mountain, and quietly beginning to count!"]},{"number":5802,"title":"Chapter 5802: Chapter 5801: Difficult! I","paragraphs":["For a long time, the only sound on THE Firmament Mountain was the blizzard.","Then Sir Moriarty rose from his throne of instruments!","There was no slow, pleased rising this time. He simply stood and when he spoke his voice cut through the howling wind as cleanly as a blade through cloth.","\" The Convocation is ended.\"","The Plain went still inside the storm!","\" Every one of you will return to their mountain with their Keeper. Now. \" His spectacles were white with frost. \" There will be no Favors granted. There will be no closing rite. Go.\"","There was no warmth in it at all. None of the dry amusement, none of the scholar’s delight, nothing but precision, each word set down exactly where it was needed and not one word more.","Nobody argued!","Noah looked out across the Plain, at the blizzard tearing sideways over the golden clouds, white and endless and roaring. He could feel it stretching away past the edge of the mountain, past the Legacy, past anything he could perceive.","It was not only here. He was nearly certain of it. Across every Dimension and every Observable Existence, the same storm was likely raging right now.","Above, one after another, the thrones began to empty!","The pressure of the Immense Ones’ gazes lifted from the Plain like a hand taken off a chest. First the black glass. Then the hollowed star, the bone, the living throne in leaf that had already stood empty. The hazes thinned and vanished. Moriarty was gone. Poona lingered a moment longer than the rest, her bright eyes sweeping once across the golden clouds below, and then she was gone too.","The ring of thrones hung empty in the storm, filling slowly with snow!","On the Plain, the Progeny and Provenance Lifeforms began to disperse.","They did it quietly. The water-woman stepped off her cloud with her fish still dark inside her and let her Keeper lead her away. The stag followed his, antlers bowed, bells silent.","Batiatus went without a word. Keepers led their charges to the edge of the mountain one pair after another, onto the glowing Conduits, and away into the white, until the golden clouds stood mostly empty and the Plain of Accord was only snow.","Noah stayed where he was!","He stood at the edge of his cloud and looked at the place where Minerva had fallen. The snow had nearly buried it already.","\" Wow ,\" said a voice beside him. \" What a crazy thing your actions had a hand in propagating.\"","...!","Ling was standing in the snow beside his cloud!","He had not seen her come, and he had not felt her come, which was a great deal more unsettling! One moment the snow beside him was empty, and the next she was simply there, looking up at him.","Her round face was somber for once, the smile gone quiet. But her eyes were bright. They were full of something that was not sorrow at all, a sharp, curious light, like someone who knows a great deal more.","Noah did not turn to look at her.","\"I did not have a hand in propagating anything,\" he said.","Ling held out her hand, palm up. Snow gathered on it at once, piling up fast, a small white heap in the middle of her palm.","She was dressed for a summer afternoon, not a blizzard at the end of existence. The same blue silk dress embroidered with gold, cut high at both sides, her thick powerful thighs and strong calves bare to the storm but for the white wrap-bands at her ankles.","No coat, no cloak, no fur. The wind tore at her ribons and whipped her spiraled buns and she did not so much as shiver. She stood in the howling white looking perfectly, entirely at ease.","She smiled!","And her voice arrived in his mind, for him alone.","\" Every time you take a step, authority shifts beneath you. Every time you open your mouth, the air changes. You make a choice, and existence answers. Cause and effect. It’s that simple.\"","She tipped her palm, and the little heap of snow slid off it.","\" Some people love to cry about bad luck. They point at their ruined existence and call it an accident. A twist of fate. A coincidence. But nothing in this life is coincidental. Whether you want to admit it or hide behind it, causality is inescapable. Every choice you ever made has an effect.\"","Her eyes went to the buried green glow in the snow.","\" Minerva did what she did of her own will. But you were among the things that came together to make it happen as it happened. Is it bad luck that she had to be the first one to try to become Immense, only to fail? That the new conditions of existence were revealed through her, and the cold got colder?\"","She hummed. \" Hmm. We just said luck is something people cry about. There’s no fate. There’s no luck. There’s only us. What we are, and what we choose to do, Big Boy.\"","The snow poured down around them.","\" And I’ve made a choice. It’ll have its own causality, same as everything. I’m inviting you to my mountain.\"","...!","An invitation to her mountain? Now? In the middle of all this?","Noah turned his head, finally, and looked at her!","\" Whatever for?\" he sent back, for her alone.","Ling blinked at him. Then she smiled brilliantly.","\" Why ,\" she said, \" to put your head between my thighs and see if I can crack it.\"","...!","Noah said nothing!","Ling laughed!","\" Kidding .\" She tilted her head, and for a moment the brightness in her eyes went very focused. \" I’ve made a choice, and so has the Immense One behind me. Someone a great deal more powerful than Sir Moriarty, and a great deal more mysterious, wants to have a talk with you.\"","She held out her hand, palm up again, empty this time. \" Walk with me?\"","Noah looked around!","The Plain of Accord was nearly empty now, a white field under a white sky, the blizzard howling across it and the empty thrones hanging overhead full of snow.","A few golden clouds still held figures. On the nearest one, Achilles had drawn Rose close against his side, one arm around her, frost thick on both of them, his solemn eyes on the storm. Rose’s face was pressed into his shoulder. Neither of them was looking at anything but each other.","Noah looked back at the girl who was a Root, entirely, from her skin to her core.","A mysterious Immense One. More powerful than Moriarty.","He needed time to think anyway. Maybe an Immense One would be illuminating.","He nodded!","Ling grinned. She flicked one foot against the snow, a light, careless little motion, and her hand snaked out and closed around his. Her grip was warm.","She flicked her foot again.","And the two of them were gone!","In the place where they had stood, the snow crashed down harder than before, filling in their footprnts in an instant, as though the blizzard had been waiting for them to leave.","---","Ling’s mountain was unlike any other in the Legacy.","It rose alone out of the blizzard, wrapped from root to hidden peak in a trembling golden-violet haze. That haze was the light of an Immensity, burning steadily and deliberately all the way around, and where the storm struck it, the snow simply stopped. The blizzard screamed and whipped against it and could not get through. Like a massive coat of Immensity wrapped around an entire mountain!","Ling let go of his hand and went ahead up the slope.","Inside the haze there was no snow, and yet the mountain was cold! Its slopes were dull grey-black stone, the air still and heavy. Gnarled trees with bark like old iron lined the way, their branches bent back on themselves, and every one of them was shivering in the windless air, as if they remembered the cold even with it kept out.","Ahead, a cave swelled out of the mountainside like a great stone throat, twisted trees crowding its mouth and pale smoke drifting out of it.","Ling went in without slowing. Noah followed, and at the stone lip, his sight bloomed.","| You are entering the periphery of an Existential Immense Domain.|","|The Immense One who controls it holds absolute authority within it.|","|Although, to be clear, it would hardly matter whether they wished you harm here or anywhere else.|","...!","Noah stopped!","A little way into the misty tunnel, Ling turned her head, the smoke curling around her face. For a moment she did not look like a cheerful girl who had run late up a Conduit. She looked like something that lived in a place like this.","\"I don’t bite ,\" she said. \" Neither will the owner of this place. Come on.\"","Noah did not do afraid. And even if he had, curiosity had always won that argument in him. He stepped in!","The tunnel was long and close and warm, its walls damp under his fingertips, so thick with mist he could barely see her blue silk ahead of him. The smell of incense grew stronger with every step.","Then it opened into a cavern!","Its ceiling was lost in the dark and mist filled all of it, grey banks rolling slow across the floor. It felt enormous, and occupied, like a room where someone sits very still in a corner.","Ling stopped at the edge of the mist and stretched, arms high, then bending one leg and the other, her powerful thighs flexing and loosening under the silk.","For a moment she simply stood there with her eyes closed, the mist curling around her ankles, as if listening for something only she could hear. She breathed out.","And then...she danced!","It began slow: one step, her arms sweeping a wide, flowing arc, drawing a circle on the air. Her body turned with it and the arc continued unbroken, circles within circles, every motion flowing into the next with no seam between them. Her face had gone calm and far away. She was a priestess at a rite, and the rite was her.","Then her feet struck the stone!","DUM!","Heel, then ball, a hard stamp that rolled through the cavern like a drum. Another. A rhythm rising, older than words. Her palms struck her own thighs and chest in time, call and answer, skin answering stone. Her hips moved loose and grounded, her body sinking low toward the earth and rising again, arms flung wide.","With every turn, the mist drew back from her in rings!","And as it cleared, flames appeared! Purple torches set in the cavern walls kindled one after another as the mist fell away from them, two, then six, then a great ring of dozens burning deep, steady violet, throwing long trembling shadows across the stone and across the dancing girl at the center of it all.","The rhythm quickened. Her turns tightened, and the violet light caught on her and trailed behind her hands like ribbons of flame. Twelve turnings, Noah counted, each one different, and on the twelfth she spun so fast the purple light wrapped her entirely!","| You are witnessing a NARRATIVE INSCRIPTION RITUAL DANCE: THE Kindled Circle.|","|It is not performed. It is written, with the body, onto the domain.|","|Each turning draws the dancer closer to their own Root of Immensity, attuning existence and Root to one another.|","|Performed to its Truest Essence, the distance between the two closes entirely. The dancer and their Root become one.|","...!","Noah went very still!","Become one with their Root? He looked at the girl spinning in the violet light, at the panel of 1s he had read on the Plain, at the being whose Root did not sit inside her but was her, from her skin to her core.","So that was how! Somewhere, at some point, she had danced this until there was nothing left between her and her Root at all, and whatever she had been before that, she had stopped being it.","The last haze thinned at the far end of the cavern, where the ring of torches met, and lifted. Behind it lay an old, faded prayer mat.","And on it sat an Immense One!","Noah could not quite see it. Its Dimensionality ran so deep that his sight kept sliding off its edges. But he saw enough to know he would never forget it.","It sat, vast as a mountain range drawn down into the shape of a giant. Enormous prayer beads, each the size of a boulder, dark and polished by some unimaginable span of handling, hung around its hands and thick forearms on a cord older than many. Its eyes were open, pale and pupil-less, and slow tears ran from them down a broad, solemn face, hissing faintly where they met the violet fire at its jaw.","And yet the mouth beneath was set in a wide, fierce line, almost a smile, burning with terrible cheerful certainty. Its hair rose from its brow like a mane of fire, and the fire was purple, wreathing its shoulders and beads and knees in slow, deep violet.","It wept, and it smiled, and it burned!","Unmoving and silent, it sat on its prayer mat, and its weight filled the whole mountain!","Ling’s dance wound down to stillness directly in front of Noah. She rose tall, lifted her arms once toward the ceiling, and let out one long breath, the purple light sliding off her like water.","Then she sat cross-legged on a second mat laid before the prayer mat, patted the empty space beside her, and looked back over her shoulder.","\" Come .\"","...!","Noah stood a moment longer, looking at the weeping, smiling, burning thing!","This was what an Immense One felt like. Poona waving from a golden throne, Moriarty adjusting his spectacles over a corpse, those had been Immense Ones choosing to look like something he could stand beside.","This one chose nothing. It simply was, and the air pressed on him so heavily that he had to decide, deliberately, to keep breathing it.","Why would a being like this call him here?","The answer was not his yet. He wanted it!","So he crossed the cavern floor between the purple torches, sat down on the mat beside Ling, and looked up at the Immense One."]},{"number":5803,"title":"Chapter 5803: Chapter 5802: Difficult! II","paragraphs":["Noah watched the Immense One on the prayer mat, and in the next moment, it spoke!","| THE THINKER AT THE END OF EXISTENCE welcomes you.|","...!","The voice rose out of the stone and the purple torches and the thin mist lingering in the corners, deep enough to rumble in Noah’s ribs like a great drum struck softly. There was no cruelty in it. There was courtesy, and patience, and underneath both a distance so vast that every word seemed to fall from very far above.","The beads around its forearms shifted, click by heavy click, though its hands never moved.","|\" Existence will only grow harder from here. The winter will be colder, and a great many will die in it. That is simply what existence is now, as we walk into an age that very few are ready for.\"|","|\"In time, even the Immense will be fighting over warmth.\"|","The beads clicked again.","|\" But set all of that aside. Tell me something. In all of existence, at this very hour, who would you say carries the hardest adversity?\"|","...!","Noah listened with everything he had!","Every word from this being was heavy. Heavy, like a word carried for a very long time before it was finally set down. And the manner of it was old, older than any voice he had heard, measured and unhurried.","But the question itself was simple.","\" Those who have formed their Roots ,\" Noah said calmly.","|\" Yes .\"|","The tears kept running from those pale, pupil-less eyes, hissing where they met the violet fire at its jaw.","|\"You cannot advance. And now you may be hunted besides, your Roots cut away so the cold sits a little lighter on everyone else. And yet it was in this very cold that the newly risen Immense were meant to open the door. They were to be the Key to THE Great Becoming. And now not one of them can become Immense at all.\"|","A long, rumbling sigh moved through the cavern.","|\"A conundrum, isn’t it?\"|","The purple flames around its shoulders rose, slow, and settled.","|\" The air is growing thinner. With the coming of THE Long Night, existence will grow colder and colder from here. The frost is not going to thaw, and it is not going to take pity on anyone. Those who became Immense before this fell upon us do not hold the key. Even I do not hold it, as I...\"|","It stopped.","Then, slowly, the Immense One turned on its prayer mat!","The beads dragged across the stone. The great kneeling shape shifted, vast as a mountain range turning in its sleep, until THE THINKER AT THE END OF EXISTENCE had its back to them. And Noah saw.","A gash ran down it!","It began at the crown of its head and ran the whole length of its back, a single enormous wound, deep and ragged and wide enough to lose a Dimension in. The edges were torn. Its purple fire could not close over it; the flames reached for the edges and sputtered and fell back. And the wound was full of frost!","Thick white rime packed into it and spiling over its lips, cold so dense it steamed against the heat of the flames, and through the frost, faintly, a light was leaking. Immensity. The Thinker’s own Immensity, seeping out of it in thin pale threads, drifting up into the cavern air and fading.","Gory, and heavy, and wrong. It looked like something that should have killed whatever carried it a long time ago!","Beside Noah, Ling was on her feet.","She had risen so suddenly that her mat skidded on the stone, and her face had gone the color of old ash. The cheer was gone from it entirely. Her eyes were wide and fixed on the wound, and her hands had come up in front of her as though she could reach across the cavern and hold it shut.","\" Father ...\" Her voice cracked. \" What is this?! When did this happen?! What the fucking fuck?!\"","...!","Father.","Slowly, the Thinker turned back around to face them. The fierce almost-smile had not changed. The tears had not stopped.","It looked at Ling. Then at Noah.","|\"I am dying.\"|","BOOM!","...!","An Immense One was dying!","Noah sat very still on his mat. An Immense One, one of the beings at the top of all existence, was dying in front of him, and its wound was made of cold.","His eyes flickered. He thought of a frost-visage wearing Lucy’s face, rising out of the snow of the Vasiliou Elsedimension to strike down THE UNPAID COLLECTOR, and of how he had held his wife in the snow and called that Immense One a bum until it came down to die.","He thought of the Overseeing One above the frozen forest. And now here was a third, kneeling on a prayer mat with the winter packed into its back.","Beside him, Ling sat down.","She did not so much sit as collapse, all at once, as though whatever had been holding her up had simply let go. She sat on her mat with her powerful legs tucked beneath her and her hands limp in her lap, and her eyes were ashen and empty, staring at nothing. It was as though the bright cheerful soul Noah had watched laugh through a bloody bout had simply gone out of her.","The Thinker looked at Noah.","|\" The winter is brutal on us all. I tried to find answers by going into the winter itself. And this was the result.\"|","The faint threads of Immensity kept rising from behind it, fading into the dark.","|\" My Immensity was too bright. It drew in things that were brighter still, and far more terrible.\"|","Noah raised his head.","\" Where exactly did you go?\"","He had to ask. He had an inkling, and he did not like it.","The fierce line of the Thinker’s mouth widened, very slightly, into something that was almost a smile.","|\"I went where you have gone. That is why I brought you here.\"|","...!","|\" Any Immense One who goes there meets a certain death. A few of us, the more reckless ones, studied the cold as soon as it came. We took it into our own bodies. We learned where it leads. And yet when we went into that place, the answer that came back at us was so very heavy.\"|","The pale eyes held him.","|\" Why do you suppose that is?\"|","The Cold Place!","Noah’s eyes were bright. He did not answer.","There was no need. He knew the frozen seas and the seated dead and the rivers of cold that poured out of the dark and away across existence. He had knelt in them, and drunk them, and walked back out again, every time.","|\" Wherever the opposition is greatest,\"| the Thinker went on, mild as ever, |\" that is where the answers are. The answers to this winter lie past that place. Past that doorway of endless cold.\"|","...!","\"A doorway ?\" Noah said. \" The Cold Place is a doorway?\"","|\"Is that what you call it?\" | A small, dry sound, very nearly a laugh. |\" Its true name is THE Undersnow. And the first place you arrive when you go down is only its doorway.\"|","The beads clicked, slowly.","|\" The Long Night was meant to be hard. It was never meant to be obscene, or impossible. When I began to die, even my Teacher was surprised, and she reached out to me. The Long Night has been tainted, she said. The adversity of it, the turning of the great cycles of existence, has been interfered with. And not even an Immense One should have the power to do such a thing.\"|","The flames sank low around its shoulders.","|\" As things stand, it will only grow colder. Even the common masses, even the lifeforms that hold no authority at all and were never meant to freeze in this Night, even they will become blocks of ice. And the conditions laid upon the Immense are heavy. They were made so that we cannot even come close to the answer.\"|","The pale, weeping gaze settled on Noah and stayed there.","|\" But others can come close. Others can enter THE Undersnow and come back alive.\"|","|\"Others like you.\"|","BOOM!","...!","Noah’s gaze flickered, and his eyes grew heavy!","The Thinker watched him a moment longer. Then, slowly, tenderly, it rose.","It leaned forward from its prayer mat, vast and burning, the frost-packed wound shifting on its back, and reached out its enormous hands, the great beads swinging and clicking from its forearms, and gathered Ling up off her mat as gently as someone lifting a sleeping child, and drew her into its lap, and held her there.","Ling did not resist. She curled against it, small against the great burning chest, her ashen eyes wet.","The Thinker stroked her hed. Its enormous hand moved over her spiraled buns and her loose white ribbons, slow and careful, the purple fire parting around her so it would not touch her.","|\"I have lived a very long time. I do not care much about dying.\"|","Its hand kept moving over her hair.","|\" But I want my Progeny to live fruitful lives. I do not want them to freeze into nothing.\"|","It looked up at Noah over the top of Ling’s head.","|\" There is a prophecy going around. It speaks of THE Long Night, and of three key figures who might be its answer. Moriarty and a few others believe you may be one of them, since yours was the first Root formed after the Night began.\"|","| \"I think it is a smoke screen. A trick. There are no chosen ones in existence. Much less some tidy, neat set of instructions for surviving the Long Night.\"|","The beads clicked.","|\"I think a bill that went unpaid for a very long time has finally come due. Things were done in the past. My Teacher, THE ACHARYA OF IMMENSITY, did things in the past. Good things. Bad things. The First Sundering was one of them, and a great deal of what came after is connected to it.\"|","|\" There are no chosen ones who will come to save everyone. But there is cause and effect. Every deed calls back its answer, measure for measure. And sometimes the answer that comes back is far larger than the deed, and far more terrible. That is THE Long Night.\"|","Its hand paused on Ling’s hair.","|\" But its coming also leaves ways for existence to adapt. Something, for example, that can take the cold of that Night into itself and not come apart. Something that can enter its gateway and walk into whatever secrets lie beneath it. Or, for example, a whole lifeform whose entire existence is a Root.\"|","It looked down at the girl in its lap, and back up.","|\" Existence finds a way. So no. You are not chosen. You were favored by probability, lucky enough to have access, and strong enough to survive it. That is all. It is also a great deal.\"|","The pale eyes did not leave him.","|\" Tell me. Do you have family? Attachments?\"|","...!","The question boomed out through the cavern.","Noah raised his head, somber, and looked at this vast dying being with its daughter in its lap. The Thinker did not wait for his answer.","| \"THE Long Night will strip a great many families of every scrap of warmth and love they have. We need to find out what happened. And we need to change the course of things.\"|","The flames rose, slow and steady.","|\"I am sure I am not the only one. You may not be the only one either. A great many lives across existence will move, each trying to find their own answer. Legacies will believe they have found the chosen beings who will save them, and perhaps they have. Who knows? But none of us can sit back and wait, and hope that someone else finds the answer first.\"|","It looked down at its wound, then back at Noah.","|\" So I am here, though I am dying. I have thought through a great many probabilities, and I am THE THINKER AT THE END OF EXISTENCE. My distinction has made me grand even in the face of all this.\"|","The beads went still.","|\" Dreamer. It is going to be brutal. But may I back you, as you seek answers in the places the Immense cannot reach?\"|","The fierce almost-smile widened.","|\"I am dying. But I can die for a long time. After all, I am THE THINKER AT THE END OF EXISTENCE.\"|","HUUM!"]},{"number":5804,"title":"Chapter 5804: Chapter 5803: THE Undersnow I","paragraphs":["A dying Immense One wanted to back him.","Noah sat on the mat with that thought. He was being offered protection to go and uncover mysteries he could not even begin to fathom yet. The cold that had grown teeth. The door that had shut in Minerva’s face. A Night that was never supposed to be obscene, tainted by something no Immense One should have had the power to touch.","And he had his own questions too.","Every second that passed, his attributes grew heavier. THE Osmontian Inscription of THE Dreaming Hour pressed and pressed at him, one passing second worth an entire day, compressing his Provenance down tighter and tighter, and he was climbing. He could feel it. He was walking toward Immensity one packed second at a time!","And existence had just made it perfectly clear that nothing was allowed to become Immense.","He wanted to understand that. He wanted to understand it very badly!","But more than that, under all of it, he thought of his mother, his son, his daughter. Of his women, and every life sleeping in THE Infiniverse, dreaming their long dreams on a golden shore. He did not want those dreams frozen solid. If things were only going to grow colder, and harder, as time passed, then he needed to know why. And if it could be put right, he needed to put it right.","It would have been easy to call this a natural cycle of existence. But THE THINKER had said the Night was tainted. He had said it was a bill, coming due for something the Immense had done a very long time ago.","What had they even done?","There were so many things he wanted to know. But first things first.","\" You said you want to back me ,\" Noah said. \" How?\"","The beads clicked. The tears kept falling. In THE Thinker’s lap, Ling lay curled and silent, her ashen eyes open.","|\" The existence that is now taking shape will give very different priorities to different lives,\"| THE Thinker said.","|\"The lives of those who might change things will matter more than ever. And the ones the Immense believe to be among the three will be the most critical of all. To be watched. To be guarded. They are the only answer many of the Immense believe in. The only way through the cold that still opens the door, so that they need no longer be merely Those Who Remain.\"|","A long, rumbling breath echoed.","|\"I do not believe in chosen ones, as I have told you. But you are still a figure who will need protecting while you do what you must. Because I do not believe it, but others do. Moriarty believes it. And it is very hard to say what believers will do, given enough time and enough cold.\"|","The purple flames settled lower.","|\" There is more. A friend of mine, in another Legacy, has told me that they hold someone they have affirmed as one of the three. They have held that belief for a very long time. THE Sealed One.\"|","...!","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","| \"And among the things he has discovered is your name. It has gotten out, you see. The first Root to form after THE Long Night began.\"|","The Thinker’s voice stayed mild. | \"Though he is no longer sealed, so I suppose he is simply Riven now. THE Riven. He is being groomed as one who can reach the answer and find the key. And among the many things he has said he wants is you.\"|","The beads clicked, once, very slowly.","|\" So I expect Immense Ones will move at his word to obtain what he wants. Out of their own belief. Because they want him to be the key. Because they want the door opened, so that they are no longer only Those Who Remain.\"|","|\"Existence has become so brutal and so ridiculous that it is reaching a point where lesser beings merely wave their hands and give commands, and the Immense move to fulfill them.\"|","The pale, weeping eyes held him.","|\" Until I die, I can be your backer. That much I can promise.\"|","Noah thought about that for a long moment.","The fucking Sealed One. Riven!","He had dragged himself into a position like that, the favored candidate of an entire Legacy of Immense Ones, with Immense Ones ready to move at his word? And he was still gunning for him?","Of course he was!","Noah’s eyes flashed with decisiveness. He nodded.","\" Very well. I will go and confirm things regarding the Cold Place....THE Undersnow, for now.\"","THE Thinker’s weeping eyes shone!","For the first time, they did not look distant at all. They blazed, bright and resplendent, as though something very old had just been given a reason to keep going a little longer. The great hands moved in its lap. Tenderly, it lifted its daughter, and turned her round to face Noah.","|\" Take her as well. Remember, it will be brutal, and hard, and you cannot do this alone. Little Ling is one of my greatest accomplishments. She will not slow you down.\"|","Ling’s eyes had changed.","The ash was gone from them. In its place was fire, bright and furious. She wiped her tears away with the back of her wrist, hard, and turned her head to look up at her father.","\" Something in there did this to you. Yes?\"","The Thinker did not answer.","\" Then I’ll just have to fuck it up myself ,\" Ling said. She turned back to Noah, and her face was fierce and burning and very young. \" Hey, Big Boy. Let’s go.\"","...!","Her eyes burned with a furious light!","Noah lifted his hand. Rivers of his Provenance slid out of him, blue and gold, and wound around her wrist, binding her existence to his for the crossing. Then, still sitting on the mat, he closed his eyes and turned his thoughts downward. To the Cold Place. To THE Undersnow.","His Root pulsed. It held the weavings of THE Long Night inside it, packed into every quark he owned, and those weavings answered.","He felt himself begin to sink.","Down, out of the purple-lit cavern and the kneeling burning giant, down through the stone and the snow and the dark, his existence sliding toward that unfathomable place!","—","He opened his eyes in the Cold Place.","The frozen seas stretched away to every horizon, blue and white and shining, as they always had. Drifting crystals hung in the air, and the rivers of cold still rolled out of the dark.","But the Hollow Night Lifeforms were gone!","Every one of them. The countless seated dead, the ranks upon ranks of blank-eyed things in their turning pillars of cold, the beasts and giants and lions with wrong heads, all of them gone. The rivers ran over nothing, and the great frozen expanse lay empty as far as he could see.","And the place where the Caretaker had always stood, her pages turning around her in the air, was empty too.","Noah stood very still.","Beside him, the air shivered, and Ling appeared.","She landed in a crouch on the frozen sea, then sprang up and turned in a full circle, looking everywhere at once. Her face was ferocious. It was also, somehow, still a little cute, round-cheeked and fierce, a small furious thing glaring at an entire frozen underworld as if it had personally insulted her family, which, as far as she was concerned, it had.","She finished her circle and looked at him, and her voice was earnest.","\" You didn’t have to agree to anything. So thank you in advance. For moving on this, and looking into it .\" She planted her hands on her hips.","\" My father can say he’s dying all he likes. But his Immensity is exactly that... immense. He’s THE Thinker at the End of Existence. Just think how well that name fits these times. \" Her eyes sharpened. \"If you make any headway into all this, I’ll reward you too.\"","Her words were sharp and her eyes were sharper.","Noah listened while he looked around. The empty seas, the empty place where the Caretaker should have been, the rivers of cold pouring on over nothing.","His gaze grew firm. He rose, and looked out across the endless frozen seas.","\" Let’s go.\"","He dove!","Straight down, into the sea of cold, and it closed over his head like a lid. Ling hit the water a heartbeat behind him, and followed.","The sea was colder than anything he had ever touched. Colder than the rivers he had drunk in the frozen underworld, colder than the Collector’s gaze, a cold so deep it seemed to have a weight of its own, pressing in from every side. It was white-blue and faintly luminous, and the deeper they went the darker and denser it grew, until it was less like water and more like diving through the frozen heart of a glacier.","Noah’s body drank it.","The cold poured into him through his skin and ran straight down into his Root, and his Root took it and refined it, pressing it down into the packed quarks alongside his Provenance and the Long Night already waiting there. Every stroke deeper, he grew a little denser. A little colder. A little more himself.","Beside him, Ling swam down through the freezing dark as though it were a warm pond in summer. The cold did not touch her at all. It slid off her bare arms and her powerful legs and her fluttering white ribbons and found nothing to take hold of. She was a Root, all the way through, with a unique quality!","Down. Further down. The light above them dimmed to nothing. The pressure mounted. Down past anything Noah had ever reached in the Cold Place, past anything he had even known was there!","And after a long while...","POP!","They passed through something. A barrier, thin and taut as the skin on a drum, and it burst around them. The sea’s pressure vanished all at once, and instead of sinking further they were rising, carried upward, breaking out through the surface of a white-blue sea into open air.","Noah surfaced, and looked around, and went still.","It was terrible, and it was wondrous!","Radiant frozen landmasses floated all around them, vast islands of blue-white ice glowing faintly from within, drifting slowly through a dim, endless sky. Trees grew on them, towering trees taller than mountains, their trunks and branches filled with cold, rimed so thick they glittered like frozen lightning. And everywhere, hanging in the air between the floating islands in their thousands, were Dimensions and Observable Existences.","Broken ones.","Every single one of them was shattered. Ripped in half, some of them, cleanly, as though something enormous had taken each one in its hands and torn it apart. Others were cracked through like dropped plates, their broken halves drifting slowly apart with seas and continents and dead frozen cities spilling out of the tears. Thousands upon thousands of them, a whole sky full of torn realities, hanging frozen in the dark.","Ruination’s prompts came fast. She was reading every thread of information she could reach, as quickly as she could reach it, and her words came clipped and urgent.","| Master. You have arrived at THE BASAL FLOOR of THE Undersnow.|","|Multiple dangerous lifeforms sensed nearby. Designation: EMPOWERED HOLLOW NIGHT LIFEFORMS.|","|Each one appears to hold a LESSER KRYOS EXISTENTIAL CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN within its existence.|","...!","Noah let out a long, heavy breath.","There truly was more to the Cold Place than he had ever known. A whole existence under the ice, and he had been standing on its doorstep all along. Would the answers be here, somewhere, among the broken realities and the frozen islands? Would anything here be willing to give them up?","Before he could even settle his thoughts...","KAAA!","A cry split the frozen sky!","Something came down out of the dark and landed on the edge of a floating island directly above them, and the whole island dipped under its weight.","It was a crow.","It was the size of a mountain range, and it was wrong in evry way a crow could be wrong. Its feathers were long jagged shards of black ice, layered and overlapping and chiming faintly against each other whenever it moved, and through the gaps between them Noah could see its ribs, white and bare, glazed in frost.","Its beak was a great curving tower of dark rime, cracked along its length, long enough to impale a Dimension, and its talons hooked over the edge of the island like iron grapnels, and where they gripped, the ice spread in white veins.","It had many eyes. They ran in rows down both sides of its head, a dozen or more, each one a pale cold blue and each one fixed on him. And on its head sat a crown. A tall, jagged crown of frozen spikes, branching like the antlers of some dead king, glittering with a light that was colder than light had any right to be.","Tattered banners of snow trailed from its wings. A halo of drifting frost circled it slowly, like a ring of dust around a dying star.","It looked down at Noah with every one of its eyes, and the weight of it came down on him!","It was suffocating. Not Immense. Not quite. But heavy, crushing, a presure that pressed on his Root and on the Counting’s weight already sitting there, and made both of them heavier.","| You are not allowed here.|","|Return.|","Noah’s gaze grew heavy.","\" What if I do not wish to return?\" he said. \" What if I want answers?\"","The crow looked down at him, cold and unblinking, and slowly spread its great wings. Rivers of snow streamed from them in the dark.","| There are no answers.|","|There is only THE Long Night.|","...!","Noah breathed out.","He rolled his shoulders. He stretched, loosening his arms, his back, his neck. And golden clouds began to spill from him, soft and bright, drifting out across the white-blue sea.","Beside him, Ling had gone utterly still, and then not still at all. Her thighs were trembling with readiness. Her whole body hummed with it, every muscle drawn tight, her powerful legs vibrating faintly beneath her, as though her entire existence had become a single coiled weapon waiting for someone to let it loose!","Noah looked up at the crow again.","\"In this epoch, I intend to be supreme ,\" he said. \" And it seems I will have to become more dominating than I have ever been. Existence wants to be brutal? Okay!\"","His eyes shone. \" Then I will be more brutal. I will be unfair.\"","\"I can be very unfair!\"","HUUM!","An infinite pillar of dreams erupted out of him!","It tore up from the white-blue sea in a column of golden light that did not end, stretching up past the floating islands and the broken Dimensions and away into the dark. And out of it, wreathed in it, a fiendish creature made of dreams, Noah shot upward toward the frozen crown!"]},{"number":5805,"title":"Chapter 5805: Chapter 5804: The Undersnow II","paragraphs":["When Noah thought back across his whole existence, there had been times he could only be called a bully.","He had been terrifying with his power. Overpowered, grand, tyrannical, a being who walked into a war and ended it with a single drop of his blood or mana while armies wept at the edge of his shadow. He did not regret it. It had been who he was, and what the moment needed.","But the higher he climbed, the more complicated existence became. The beings grew stranger. The rules grew deeper. And it grew harder and harder to simply overpower anything, even with everything that made him unique.","Harder. Not impossible.","And through all of it, in every one of those moments when he had stood over something that should have crushed him, there had been one answer to his terrible immensity. One thing underneath all the others.","His Infinity.","So.","He looked at the crow ahead, and his sight opened it!","| EMPOWERED HOLLOW NIGHT LIFEFORM.|","|VERITAS: 999 (+100). PROVENANCE: 999 (+100). POTENTIA: 999 (+100). PONDUS: 999 (+100).|","...!","Nine hundred and ninety-nine, and a hundred more on top of each line!","Noah’s eyes narrowed as he flew. The base alone matched Minerva, the very ceiling she had hit and broken herself against. And then a hundred more in everything, sitting on top of it like a borrowed coat. Where did that come from? The Basal Floor? The cold itself, feeding the things that lived in it? Or something the crow carried inside it, a stolen heart of true Immensity pushing it past a limit it could not reach alone?","He did not know. It did not matter yet. What mattered was that it was stronger than him on paper, in every line!","And yet his numbers were packed and its numbers were hollow. He had learned that much in the snow. Digits were only what existence could be bothered to count. They were never the whole of a thing.","He raised his hand.","\"I AM.\"","HUUM!","He was.","But he was what?","With those two words he pulled every ounce of his Provenance and every scrap of his power together into a single point, and it came out of him as an aurora of dreams. Blue and gold, incandescent, drawn out long and thin and sharp into the shape of a blade, and it shot across the frozen sky toward the crow with a sound like the largest bell in existence being struck once and cut off!","It hit the crow full on!","The crow lowered its head and met it with its beak.","BOOM!","The blade of dreams struck the cracked tower of rime and broke apart against it, scattering into drifting golden sparks. At most, the crow’s head rocked back a fraction, and a thin line of frost cracked along the edge of its beak. That was all.","Little damage. Almost none!","But...","\" THE MORTAL COIL.\"","HUUM!","Golden clouds descended. They came down out of the frozen dark all around the crow, settling over the snow and the floating islands and the torn Dimensions, soft and bright and silent, and wherever they touched, borrowed things began, quietly, to be disallowed. The crow’s hundred extra points flickered. The cold in its feathers wavered.","Every eye it had narrowed! A low sound rattled in its throat, the first sound it had made since it told him there were no answers. It had felt the Coil land, and it did not like it.","\"I AM !\"","HUUM!","A second aurora of dreams tore out of him, brighter, sharper, a blade of blue-gold light shearing through the air. It hit the crow across the breast, and this time something gave. Black-ice feathers sheared away in a spray, a handful of them, spinning off into the dark as glittering shards!","Out of nowhere, Ling appeared beside the crow’s head.","She had not flown there. She was simply there, one leg already rising, and it came down in a single swing. Her thigh pulsed with a physicality so terrifying that the air around it bent. It hit the crow in the side of the skul, and the whole mountain-range bulk of it was knocked sideways off its island, sent hurtling through the frozen sky straight at Noah!","KAAAA!","The crow screamed as it tumbled, and the storm of its cold howled after it, black feathers and blue-white frost streaming off it like smoke off a comet.","He bellowed it again.","\"I AM!\"","Another blade tore out of him, and another, every repetition of the words a new eruption of dreams, each one carving across the tumbling crow. His own body began to glisten. Light ran along his crystalline skin in bright veins, blue and gold, and he rushed forward to meet the crow in the air.","His hand met its beak as...","The impact broke him in half!","Half his body simply went, shattered from the shoulder down to the hip in an explosion of crystal and light, and before he could even feel it, the crow’s wing swept around. The rime-banners along its edge had gone sharp as a blade of frost, and they took his other half clean off.","He Root and Existence pulsed as it was overwhelmed and decimated as effectively...","He died!","Ling stopped in the air, one leg still half-raised. Her fierce face went blank with shock, and for one heartbeat she simply hung there in the frozen dark, staring at the empty place where he had been.","...!","A moment later, golden clouds began to gather.","They drew together out of the frozen dark where he had been, bright and slow, and in the heart of them, something took shape again. Then the clouds opened, and Noah came out of them.","| Your existence has ended.|","|Your Dream has not.|","|Your Dream is Infinite. Even death will not stop it.|","He came out cold. He came out dominant!","There was no armament on him. No garment of Provenance, no crystal plate, nothing at all. Only his skin, smooth and shining and unbroken, and the dense packed muscle of a body that had been pressed and refined by the Lived Hour a second at a time into something harder than anything the Basal Floor had ever seen.","He hung in the frozen air entirely naked, a long and heavy thing between his legs, swinging freely as he turned, utterly unconcerned with it. Golden-blue light rolled off his shoulders. His eyes were very calm.","He looked at the crow, and the crow, for the first time, looked back at him warily!","\"I am Human ,\" Noah said.","The clouds around him began to churn.","\"I am THE Protagonist .\"","The churning gathered, tightened, took shape.","\"I am Quintessential .\"","All around him, the clouds of dream broke apart into Dimensions!","Small ones at first, each one no larger than a fisst, unstable and flickering, blue-gold bubbles of existence that trembled and pulsed as though they could barely hold themselves together. Thousands of them, blooming out of the clouds in every direction. Then tens of thousands. Then hundreds of thousands, still more of them coming, filling the frozen sky around him until he hung in the heart of a vast, trembling clusters of his own unstable dreams!","One after another, they began to surge toward the crow.","\" My dream is fucking infinite, \" Noah said. \" What about yours?!\"","BOOM!","He surged forward to meet it!","And as he went, his Dream began, subtly, to change. Infinity threaded into it, more and more, until the two could not be told apart. His Root began to spin inside him, faster and faster, turning like an engine that had just been given all the fuel it had ever wanted. And both of his Inscriptions burned!"]},{"number":5806,"title":"Chapter 5806: Chapter 5805: I Dream Your End!","paragraphs":["Noah felt like an engine!","THE Osmontian Inscription of THE Dreaming Hour churned inside him, pressing a day into every second. His Root spun at the center of his chest, faster and faster, the mobius turning like a wheel that had finally been given a road. And through all of it, through every packed quark and every current of Provenance, the idea of Infinity was spreading. Seeping in. Soaking into his Dream until he could no longer tell where one ended and the other began.","He raised his hands.","The crow roared!","It was a maddened sound, stripped of any grace it had carried before, and with it came a wave. A glacial wave of cold rolled out of its body in every direction, white and total, and everything it touched froze. Drifting islands, torn Dimensions, the white-blue sea below and the frozen air above, gigaparsecs of it in every direction, all of it locked solid in a single instant, as though this region had become a gem with the three of them sealed inside it!","Ling froze mid-leap.","Noah froze mid-reach.","For one breath, nothing moved at all.","Then, around Ling, the ice began to melt. It ran off her in streams and sheeted away from her skin, because there was nothing in her for it to hold. And around Noah, the ice began to dream. It softened. It blurred at its edges into drifting golden haze, slow and drowsy, until he was simply moving through it as though it had never frozen at all.","He lowered his hands, and spoke.","\"My Tongue is young, \" Noah said. \" Undeveloped. I dream of it growing, and it will. I have Letters. I have Words. All of them built on my own Root and my own foundations.\"","His eyes held the crow.","\" So I will make a sentence. One built for nothing but destruction.\"","He breathed in.","\"I DREAM OF YOUR END.\"","HUUM!","|THE OSMONTIAN TONGUE: A SENTENCE has been composed.|","|I DREAM OF YOUR END.|","|Your Root, your foundations, and your Provenance are gathered to a single purpose: to dream, simply and purely, the end of what you behold.|","|While you hold the target in your gaze, its existence is dreamed toward its conclusion. What is dreamed away does not vanish. It returns to the dreamer.|","|The more certain the Dream, the faster the ending.|","...!","The edges of the crow began to glow!","A thin line of gold ran along the rims of its great wings, along the tips of its talons, along the cracked edge of its beak. It shone for a moment, soft and warm and wrong against all that black ice. Then the glowing edges began to flake away. Tiny golden flakes, drifting loose from the crow like ash from a burning page, and they did not fall. They flowed. Across the frozen sky in slow shining streams, all of them drifting toward Noah, sinking into his skin, and he felt each one arrive as a small warm weight in his chest!","The crow screamed and lookd at its own wing.","Then its crown rang.","It was a terrible sound as around the crown, shapes began to form. Rendered shapes, many-faced and vast, turning slowly in the frozen air. A colossal orange one, facet upon facet, so intricate Noah’s eyes pulsed trying to follow it. And inside that, a violet one, and inside that, another orange. Shrink. Push. Shrink again. The three of them spun together around the crown and then drove at Noah as one, a single rendered weapon built to crush everything it touched down into a point smaller than a quark and then scatter the point across existence!","Noah looked at it coming.","He composed another sentence.","\"I DREAM OF HEALING INFINITELY.\"","HUUM!","|A second SENTENCE has been composed.|","|I DREAM OF HEALING INFINITELY.|","|While it holds, whatever of you is broken is dreamed whole again before your existence can come apart.|","|It does not prevent the blow. It refuses the wound.|","The rendered weapon hit him.","BOOM!","It crushed his left arm down to nothing, pushed his ribs out through his back, and condensed half his skull into a point and flung the point away. And golden clouds bloomed on every wound in the same instant, and his arm was there again, and his ribs, and his skull, whole, whole, whole, each broken part dreamed back into place before the rest of him could even notice it was gone!","He walked through the rendered weapon as it tore him apart and remade him, over and over, and came out the other side untouched.","Then he landed on the crow’s back!","He stood there among the black-ice feathers and the frosted ribs, naked and gleaming, heavy with muscle, and raised both hands over his head, and brought them down like hammers!","WAA!","The crow cried out!","Its back buckled under the blow. Golden light ran out from the point of impact in cracks, and more of it flaked away, and the flakes streamed up into him. He brought his hands down again. And again. Every strike, more of the crow came loose into dreams and drifted home to him.","\" When a dream is small, it dies with the morning ,\" Noah said, and his voice rolled out across the whole frozen region.","He struck.","\" But when a dream has enough weight, when it has enough teeth, it stops being a dream. It becomes existence.\"","He struck again.","\" My dream is not an invitation. It is an unyielding decree, moving with absolute certainty. Struggling against it is an ant cursing an avalanche. It changes nothing at all.\"","His hands came down, and the crow’s spine groaned.","\" Sit down. Stop thrashing against it. Do not fucking resist! The dream will happen, and your permission was never asked!\"","...!","ROOOAR!","The crow reared under him, screaming, thrashing, the whole mountain-range bulk of it bucking in the frozen air.","And Ling moved.","She hung in the air beside its head, and her thighs flexed. They swelled, visibly, the great muscles expanding as though something inside her had just been given room to breathe, and she began to spin. A hazy light wrapped around her, golden-violet, the same light that had burned around her father’s mountain, and her eyes changed. The pupils went out of them. They were pale and blank and white, exactly like her father’s, and she turned in the air in a slow, flowing circle, and then another.","The Kindled Circle. A piece of it. Three turnings, four, drawing her closer and closer to the Root that was her whole existence, until Noah could not tell, watching, where the girl ended and the Root began.","On the last turning, she kicked the crow’s beak.","BOOM!","It shattered in half!","The whole great cracked tower split down its length with a sound like a glacier breaking off a mountain, and the two halves tumbled away into the dark, and from the ruin of the crow’s face, gold poured out. Flakes and flakes of it, a river of them, streaming across the sky and into Noah!","Noah roared!","He threw his hands up, and the blue-gold clouds all around him gathered into them, and took shape. Spears. Long and bright and made of his own Provenance, humming with his Dream. He drove the first one down into the crow’s back. Then the second. Then a third.","The crow flipped. It rolled over in the air, trying to throw him, and its feathers came off it in a freezing storm, and they cut him open. Across the chest, the thighs, the throat. Heavy wounds, deep and cold, the kind that should have ended him. Every one of them was dreamed shut before his existence could so much as start to break apart.","He kept throwing spears.","Four. Ten. Twenty. He drove them in faster than the crow could thrash, one after another after another, until its whole back was a forest of blue-gold shafts, skewered from the base of its broken crown down to its tail.","And from behind, Ling kicked it.","She came up under its tail and drove her foot straight into its ass, with every ounce of her Root behind it, and the sound the crow made then was not a scream. It was a sound no creature should ever have to make!","The kick drove the whole beast upward onto the spears. Every one of them sank in to the haft. And the crow split.","Down the middle, spine to breast, the two halves of it tearing away from each other in the frozen dark!","Noah’s sentence grew grander.","Now he could see it. Truly see it, the end of this thing, as clearly as he could see his own hands, and the more certain he was of it, the faster the Dream moved. The crow’s halves glared at him with every eye they had left, furious, hating. Golden clouds closed around them. And all at once, the whole of its body turned to dream!","BOOM!","The explosion was frozen. It burst outward in a sphere of white and gold and blue, ice and dream together, and for one moment the whole region was lit by it, and then it was gone.","Noah steadied himself in the air where the crow had been.","He looked grand. Naked and gleaming, packed with muscle, gold still drifting into him from the dust of the thing he had just ended.","| Your Infinity has permeated your weavings.|","|THE PROTAGONIST and THE Tide That Owes Nothing have become interlinked, for results most geared to you.|","|Loot shall once more flow from your enemies.|","|For granting death to an extremely powerful enemy, you have obtained: LESSER KRYOS EXISTENTIAL CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN x5, and one GLACIAL RECORD OF A CRUEL CROW.|","...!","Five slivers of pale blue crystal drifted out of the settling dust, each one a snowflake grown down into itself, pulsing cold and slow. They circled him, bright against the frozen dark.","And behind them came something else. A shard of ice, thin and clear, with light moving inside it. It floated up to him on its own, touched his brow, and sank in!","He saw the Basal Floor through the crow’s eyes.","Scattered scenes, dozens of them, flickering past. Frozen islands. Torn Dimensions. Other Empowered Hollow Night Lifeforms, huge and cold, prowling the dark. And then one scene held, and would not let him go.","THE Caretaker, bound in chains!","Her pages were gone. Her frost dress was torn. Great chains of pale light were wound around her arms and her waist, and she was being led. Before her walked a figure, long and slender and humanoid, far taller than she was, and it had no face at all. Only smooth, pale blankness where a face should have been. It led her across the Basal Floor, toward a massive crack in the ice, a vast blue rift splitting the frozen dark from top to bottom.","In the memory, the faceless thing stopped.","It turned around.","It had no eyes, and it looked at him anyway. Noah felt its invisible gaze land on him, through the crow’s dead memory, across however much distance lay between them.","And...","BOOM!","His upper body exploded!","It was erased, shoulders and chest and head wiped out of existence as cleanly as a word scraped off a page. And in the same instant, the golden clouds came roaring in, and his sentence held, and he was dreamed back together, whole, gasping.","The memory was gone. Ripped out of him!","But he hung there in the frozen air, grand and heavy-eyed and whole, having just defeated something far grander than himself.","Ling floated over. She was bleedng from a dozen cuts, her ribbons long gone, her pupils back again and bright with something that looked very much like approval. She looked him up and down.","Mostly down.","She whistled.","\" Be decent and cover up when you fight, Big Boy ,\" she said, still looking at his lower half. \" You don’t want to be distracting.\"","Noah glanced down. A pair of blue-gold trousers wove themselves out of his Provenance and settled over his hips.","Then he turned his calm gaze back to the Lesser Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins, and waved his hand. Three more slid out of his keeping, the ones the Caretaker had given him, and joined the five in the air. Eight of them now, circling him in the dark.","They began to spin around each other, faster and faster.","And four of them began to fuse into one!"]},{"number":5807,"title":"Chapter 5807: Chapter 5806: Purely Educational!","paragraphs":["The eight Lesser Kryos spun faster around each other, trailing pale blue light behind them like comets chasing their own tials!","Noah watched them close. Each one was a quarter of a true Immensity’s remains, a snowflake grown inward on itself, cold and dense and pulsing with the settled weight of something that had once stood at the very top of existence. And as they spun, they began to press together. Two merged first, and then two more, and the pale blue light between them flared, and flared again.","When the light settled, only two crystals hung in the air before him where four had been.","They were larger. Brighter. Denser, each one humming with a low, steady thrum that Noah could feel in his Root, and they were no longer Lesser!","|KRYOS EXISTENTIAL CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN x2.|","|Each holds the settled weight of an Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin formed within an Immense One. Far grander than the Lesser variety.|","...!","Two genuine Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins born crom 8 Lesser Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins! At this time...","A blur of blue silk swung past his face.","Ling had flipped upside down in the frozen air, legs tucked, ribbonless hair hanging loose, and she drifted to a stop directly in front of the two Kryos with her face an arm’s length from them. Her eyes were bright with open interest, studying the crystals as a jeweler studies a stone she has not seen before.","Then those same interested eyes lifted from the Kryos and settled on Noah!","He gazed back at her. She hung there upside down, round-faced and blood-speckled and curious, and he thought about a great many things in a very short time. About the Basal Floor stretching away beneath them, cold and vast and full of things that wanted to kill them. About the fact that she was THE Thinker’s daughter, and a Root made flesh, and the only being in this place who could match him blow for blow.","About how she fought, and how she laughed, and the fierce burning look in her eyes when she had kicked the crow’s beak in half.","And about the fact that he was, at the end of all of it, still human. But he had to draw his boundaries.","\" Are you interested in me?\" Noah said.","Ling blinked!","\"I am deciding to change a certain aspect of myself,\" he went on, \"I do not wish to disappoint you with any misunderstandings.\"","Ling righted herself in the air, slowly, until she was facing him properly. Her smile was wide and warm and a little sharp at its edges.","\"I do find you interesting ,\" she said. \" But it is more curiosity than anything. There were a few lifeforms in the Legacy who caught my eye. But I didn’t even deem them worthy enough to have anything with.\"","She shrugged, and the shrug carried her whole body. \" It’s a matter of pride. I believed myself so much grander that I couldn’t possibly allow someone weaker than me to experience the wonder of my thighs.\"","...!","Noah almost laughed. Almost!","\"I have been loose with my love and my affection, \" he said. \" Multiple women. And I have not done right by them. So I came to a conclusion that I cannot do that again.\"","He looked at her directly. \" But I am still human, and humans are lustful beings. I can offer you a purely...educational relationship. We learn about each other’s weavings of existence. No emotions. No attachments. We will be working together for a while in this place, and it would do me well to understand the extent of your power. You can try to understand mine.\"","...!","Ling’s mouth fell open into a wide O!","Then she laughed, the sound ringing out across the frozen dark of the Basal Floor.","\" What an arrogant fucking guy you are! \" She wiped a tear of laughter from the corner of her eye. \" Do we even have time for such things? I can sense a distant aura out there, at least one just as powerful as that crow, if not more.\"","\" One can always dream more time ,\" Noah said. \" Come. Let us see how strong your thighs are.\" His eyes held hers. \" And remember. No emotions, and no attachments.\"","Ling tilted her head!","She looked at him for a long moment, and her smile changed. It lost none of its warmth, but something in it sharpened into a blade, the smile of a being who had just been offered a game she was very confident she could win.","\" No emotions ,\" she said. \" No attachments.\"","Her eyes glittered.","\" Okay!\"","Golden clouds bloomed around them!","Thick and warm, they poured out of Noah’s Provenance in soft, bright banks, rolling out through the frozen air and closing over both of them, and their figures vanished into the gold. Whatever sounds followed were between them, and the Basal Floor, cold and indifferent, did not care to listen!","The Basal Floor drifted on around the clouds, vast and cold and full of things that prowled in the dark.","And on the frozen island where a terrifying Hollow Night Lifeform had just been killed, atop the ruins of its shattered crown, Noah Osmont sought to understand a very unique lifeform!","---","<THE Infiniverse>","The golden shore of THE Infiniverse was quieter than ever.","Snow fell on it now! The farmland beyond the shore stretched away in long green rows, heavy with the crops his people had tended days ago, and the snow came down on all of it in soft white sheets, settling on the golden sand. It was not a blizzard here. Not yet as THE Infiniverse afforded a layer of protection.","The Counting of The Long Night pressed on everything, even inside his own Infiniverse!","Noah stood at the edge of the shore with a Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin turning slowly in his hand, pale blue and cold and humming, and he looked across the farmland at the figure sitting in the snow.","Thalia was meditating!","She sat cross-legged in the middle of a plowed field, her dark red hair loose around her shoulders, her hands resting on her knees. The snow gathered on her. It settled on her hair and on her lashes and on the tops of her bare feet, and she did not brush it off. Her eyes were closed. Her breathing was slow and even. Around her, the crops closest to her body had bent toward her, very slightly, as if she were a sun and they knew it.","Noah watched her for a while before he moved.","He had been thinking, amidst this apocalypse of snow, about the women who had helped him. There had been several. There had been more than several, and he had been loose with his affection, and he had not done right by most of them.","He had told Ling that on the Basal Floor. He had made a decision about it. No more carelessness. No more taking someone’s warmth and leaving them to wonder what it had meant.","If he was going to change that, he ought to start with the most recent one.","Thalia had come to him out of a white pool, bleeding, carrying warnings from a future. She had taught him the Sovereign Genesis. She had wept one tear when he remade his quarks, and called herself his destiny and his Provenance, and he had not yet given her much in return, except the decimation of her Lineage that was a causality from a decision they both made.","So he walked across the snow to her field, and knelt in front of her, and waited until she opened her eyes.","\" You are back ,\" Thalia said.","\"I am back.\"","She looked at the Kryos in his hand! The pale blue light of it played across her face. She did not ask what it was.","\"I brought you something ,\" Noah said. \" Two things, actually. One to show you, and one to give you.\"","He raised his free hand, and the air between them filled with a dream.","He showed her the Vasiliou Elsedimension. The white avenues, the frost-visage of Lucy, the Collector’s hazy vastness rewriting existence into a debt. He showed her the blow, the single strike that shattered everything the Collector had written, and the corpse, vast and ruined, and the mammoth of frost rising out of it.","He showed her the death of the being that had once promised to rip her in half.","Thalia watched it all with her hands still on her knees and her breathing still even. When the dream faded, she was quiet for a long moment. Then the corners of her mouth moved, just slightly, and her eyes were bright.","\" He is gone ,\" she said.","\" Mmm.\"","\"Good.\" She breathed out, and some tension Noah had never noticed in her, went out of her all at once. \" Good.\"","The snow fell on them both.","\" The second thing ,\" Noah said.","He held out the Kryos.","\"I want to help you form a Root.\" he said.","Thalia looked at the crystal, and then at him.","She held his gaze for a long time. Then she reached out, and her fingers closed around the Kryos, and the pale blue light ran up her arm and into her chest!","Her body shuddered. Her eyes widened. The Provenance within her brightened!","Noah had done this multiple times before as it was second nature now as he guided the formation of another Gonadotropin.","The Provenance within her was not swelling; the essense was focusing, each one narrowing down to a point so fine it could slip between the threads of a living thing’s existence and alter what it found there. Rewrite how a body was built. Reshape the code that made a being what it was, at the deepest level, where existence wrote its instructions.","A Root bloomed in her chest as it devoured the Kryos ECG!","It was small, and bright! And it turned with a quiet, surgical certainty that reminded Noah of her hands when she had traced a line on his chest.","|A ROOT OF IMMENSITY has been formed.|","|Bearer: THALIA VASILIOU.|","|THE GENOMIC CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN.|","|CONCEPTUAL ROOT OF IMMENSITY.|","|Nature: EXISTENTIAL GENOME ALTERATION. The bearer perceives and rewrites the foundational code of any existence she touches, including her own.|","|At its peak, nothing in existence is built in a way she cannot take apart and rebuild.|","...!","Thalia breathed in sharply, and the farmland around them bloomed!","The crops nearest her shot up a foot in an instant, their leaves spreading wide, their colors deepening from green to a rich, vivid emerald. The plowed earth beneeth the snow stirred and settled into neater rows, as though it had just been told a better way to be soil. Even the snowflakes falling on her seemed to land more carefully, each one finding its place.","She opened her eyes, and they were different. Still grand, still warm. But behind the warmth, something moved with the calm, focused precision of a surgeon who has just been given a blade sharp enough to cut anything in existence.","Noah looked at her, and felt his own Root hum in answer, and smiled!","Then the snow grew heavier!","It came down harder across the whole of THE Infiniverse, on the golden shore and the farmland and the sleeping dreamers inside them. The Counting had noticed! One more Root in existence, one more weight on every other Root, and the cold answered it at once.","Noah lifted his face to the falling snow and let it land on him!","He was doing many things at this moment as his existence was also present...elsewhere.","---","In a small, utterly unknown world.","The desert was gone.","Noah stood in the sky above the small world where an old woman had once recited THE Augury of the Long Night to him by firelight, and the desert he remembered was buried. The dunes were white, and the black tents were white.","The blizzard howled across it!","It had been snowfall when he first placed his protection here. Gentle, strange, a thing the desert people had never seen and did not have a word for. Now it was a storm, and the storm was not gentle, and the people beneath it were hurting! He could feel them! Small, warm, fragile lives huddled around their fires, burning everything they had, and the cold eating through their walls anyway.","And this was not only here!","This was happening across trillions of worlds at once. Across uncounted realms, Observable Existences, and drifting Dimensions, in places Noah had never been and never would be, the same blizzard was falling on the same fragile lives. The ambient temperature of reality itself was dropping toward nothing, and there was no one standing over most of those lives as he was standing over these.","Two figures appeared beside him in the sky!","THE Infiniverse materialized on his left, her multicolored fur coat heavy with snow, her starlit eyes grave. Ruination appeared on his right, crimson beams sweeping the horizon, her coat of crimson and gold sharp against the white. Both of them looked down at the buried desert and said nothing, because there was nothing to say that the blizzard was not already saying.","Noah looked at them, and then out across the storm, and spoke.","\" The frost is settling across countless regions at once. We did not author this winter, even if our hands are tangled somewhere in the thread. And we are not saviors walking the dark to be worshiped.\"","The snow whipped past all three of them!","\" The billions of lives shivering on those far Dimensions do not know my face, and I will never learn their names. Pulling them into our shelter buys us no strategic advantage. It leaves no debt to collect, offers no return on the investment, and does nothing to halt the turning of the Night. It is completely, utterly unnecessary.\"","He paused. The blizzard filled the silence.","\"It is merely my human sentimentality. A quiet, irrational refusal to let the frost take them all just because the sky decided to go cold.\"","He turned to them.","\" So do not hesitate. Pull upon my Infinity. Open the borders of THE Infiniverse and swallow every Dimension and Observable Existence you can reach. Bring them into our warmth. We cannot carry the whole of existence, but where our reach extends, let us save as many as we can.\"","...!","Ruination’s crimson beams were already moving!","Her Root of the Record had grown grander than ever. She could find Dimensions now as a hawk finds mice in a field, rapidly, precisely, and without mercy toward the distance between them.","And THE Infiniverse was already opening!","Her Root of Genesis answered the command at once. The borders of her existence widened, and widened again, and kept widening, a living thing stretching herself to take in countless things into the warmth of her body because her Master had told her to, and because it was unnecessary, and because he was human.","Toward his words, they had only a single answer.","|Yes, Master.|","Below them, the buried desert began, very slowly, to rise. The whole world and small Observable Existence peeled away from its place in the freezing dark and drifted upward, into the open borders of THE Infiniverse, into the warmth, and the people inside their tents did not know what had saved them.","They only knew the wind had stopped being a blizzard as only light sprinkling of snow cascaded down!"]},{"number":5808,"title":"Chapter 5808: Chapter 5807: Existence Is So Beautiful!","paragraphs":["<THE Sealed One>","THE Keepers of Existence was a Legacy that looked, from a distance, like something that should not exist during a winter.","Boundless seas of crimson gold rolled away in every direction beneath a sky that had no end, shining and warm, and rivers of the same color ran through them and above them in slow winding currents that crossed and parted and crossed again. Floating islands drifted across those seas, serene and green, some the size of small Dimensions, some no larger than a garden, and every one of them was blanketed in snow.","The blizzard reached even here. It howled across the crimson gold, and where the flakes touched the seas they hissed into threads of steam, and where they touched the islands they piled and stayed, white on green, cold settling over warmth.","It was a Legacy shared by dozens of Immense Ones, THE SLEEPLESS FIEND among them, each one a pillar holding the same roof. Those who served in it spoke its name as one speaks the name of a law, because that was what it was. THE Keepers of Existence. The ones who had kept things exactly as they were for longer than anything could remember!","At the heart of those seas, on a great dais of black iron rising from the crimson gold, THE Sealed One stood and looked at what had been brought to him.","A dozen Rare Gu hung in chains along the dais’s rim, strung up in black iron, each one a different strange and shining thing. A moth whose wings were written light, and a serpent with scales of closed eyes. Something like a jellyfish made of old brass bells. All of them silent, because the chains had been designed to keep them silent as they were filled with Immensity.","Beyond the Gu, a dozen Provenance Lifeforms knelt in a row with their heads bowed. Every one of them carried a Root of Immensity.","And at the very front, in the lightest chains of all, two figures.","THE Champion Alcaeus knelt with his broad back straight, bronze-skinned and scarred from his shouldrs to his heels, his long matted hair frozen with blood. He had been a champion. Now he did not look at THE Sealed One at all, only at the snow.","Beside him crouched THE Infinity Eater.","Behind THE Sealed One, the air split like an eyelid!","A vast dark eye looked out of it, sleepless, patient, burning with an attention that had never once blinked. Its face was barely perceptible behind the haze, but the mouth was visible, and it was smiling.","| THE SLEEPLESS FIEND regards you.|","|\"They say if you die, the door is forever lost. Existence will become harder and more brutal to live in, but many core members of this Legacy believe you are one of the core keys.\"|","|\"Others, even here, believe differently.\"|","|\"So you will be protected. Five Immense Ones on your security detail at all times. And they continue to fatten you up, like a pig.\"|","The smile widened behind the haze.","|\"Now we are even giving you our own Descendants.\"|","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND looked at THE Infinity Eater as he said this!","And the betrayal on THE Infinity Eater’s face was heavy.","It turned its great head, slowly, from the Fiend to THE Sealed One and back again, and its burning eyes held the Immense One, and there was not a single glimmer of respect in those vast dark pupils. Not a shred of decorum. Only the flat, enormous disbelief of a hound that has just been handed to the butcher by the man who raised it.","\"I live in Infinity ,\" THE Infinity Eater said, and its voice was the torrent of every voice it had ever swallowed. \" My existence is grand. I was meant to form a glorious Immensity of Infinity. How could I be sitting before another like a meal right now? How could I be discarded so simply?\"","THE Sealed One smiled!","He rose from where he sat and walked toward THE Infinity Eater, unhurried, his long dark coat trailing across the black iron. He stopped in front of it, close enough to touch, and looked up at its churning Infinity and its betrayed, burning eyes.","\" You depended on the power of another to get what you had,\" THE Sealed One said, softly. \" That is why you were discarded in the end. A rented coat always gets taken back when the cold comes. You built an entire life out of borrowed wood, and now you look surprised that the landlord kicked the door in to reclaim his timber.\"","His gold eyes held THE Infinity Eater.","\"In a way, I am just like you right now. I lean on the power of Immense Ones to find my footing. I sit in their snow, I take their craft, and I learn their ways. But the difference between us is simple. I know what the bill looks like. I know they want something from me, and I want something from them. Two strangers striking a trade across an open fire before the wood burns out. And I will not need their fire for very long.\"","The Infinity Eater strained against its chains!","\" You never understood the exchange ,\" THE Sealed One went on, still soft. \" You thought a master’s favor was love. You thought being a useful hound meant they would let you sleep by the hearth forever. But a hound that goes lame gets left behind in the brush.\"","He tilted his head. \" Maybe if you had anything left to offer, they would not have thrown you into the ditch.\"","His mouth opened.","It kept opening!","His jaw came loose from his face and went on widening, the pale skin of his cheeks stretching thin as paper, lips peeling back and back until his mouth was no longer a mouth at all but a vast black opening, wider than he was tall, wider than THE Infinity Eater itself. Inside it there was no throat. Only dark, and a pale gold glint far, far down, like something very old at the bottom of a well.","\"In existence ,\" THE Sealed One whispered from inside that impossible mouth, \" most things are discarded.\"","OOOOH!","THE Infinity Eater screamed!","It threw itself backward. The chains held. It clawed at the dais, infinity snapping, every swallowed voice howling out of it at once. THE Sealed One leaned forward, and swallowed it whole. The chains snapped like thread. The scream went down into the dark and stopped, and the jaws slid back into place, and he was a lean pale man in a long dark coat again, standing alone.","His whole body shone!","Pale gold light spread outward from his chest, bright, brighter, the Infinity of a thousand devoured beings churning through him, and his Root sat a little lighter.","Then he turned, shining, to the Champion and the Gu and the dozen Provenance Lifeforms shackled and bound before him with their flickering Roots.","He licked his lips!","Then he raised his arms, palms up, and let the snow fall on them. It settled on his open hands and on his shining coat and on his pale gold hair, and he smiled, brilliantly, the smile of a man standing in a garden he intended to eat.","\" Existence... is so beautiful, isn’t it?\""]},{"number":5809,"title":"Chapter 5809: Chapter 5808: Emotion!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","Noah’s existence was stretched across many places at once, and one of them was a dream.","It was Emotive’s dream!","He had visited a great many dreams since he built the Dream Engine. Adelaide’s snowbound capital. The Emperor Penguin’s army of robots wearing his face. Each one had been a window into what a person wanted most, rendered in whatever shape their heart could hold.","Emotive’s was different.","He arrived floating in a vast, shining expanse that took him a moment to recognize. It was THE Earliest Folds. Or rather, it was Emotive’s memory of them, reimagined and polished and made grander than they had ever truly been, the old strange spaces of his long-lost Observable Existences rebuilt in a dreamer’s hands.","Massive structures of THE Loom rose everywere through it, the great woven works that Emotive and THE Living Paradox had once built together.","They climbed and arched and spiraled away in every direction, towers of woven light, bridges of thread thick as continents.","And everywhere, in every direction, stood statues of Noah!","Hundreds of them. Thousands. Some small enough to hold in two hands, some so vast their heads were lost among the woven towers. Noah seated on a throne. Laughing, head thrown back.","Arms spread wide, painting a Dimension in his blood. Standing over a fallen titan. Every one of them was stellar, grand, carved with such devotion that each seemed to have captured the very best thing about him in a single moment and held it there forever.","He floated before one of them, and stopped.","It was made of pure Luxuria Ego Authority. The whole enormous figure shone with a deep red light, warm and heavy and intoxicating, the raw substance of desire shaped into a man. It was him with crimson hair and golden eyes, wearing a fitted red suit, standing with one hand in his pocket and the faintest knowing smile on his face.","And sitting on its shoulder was Emotive!","She wore a loose red dress that hung loose and careless off her fair figure, her white skin shining brilliantly in the red light of the statue beneath her. Her hair burned. Not with one color, but with many, all of them shifting at once, crimson and violet and electric blue and a green like poison and a gold like sunrise, every shade of every feeling a being could have, tangled together and flickering madly. And her eyes, when they found him, blazed with that same bottomless mania.","She was beautiful. She had always been beautiful!","Then those eyes found him.","And she smashed forward off the statue’s shoulder, crossed the space between them in an instant, and wrapped her whole body around his feet!","She clung there, arms locked around his ankels, cheek pressed to the top of his foot, and let out a long, deep sigh of absolute contentment!","Noah sighed too. He reached down and patted her burning hair.","\" You can just hug my body, you know, \" he said. \" Why wrap yourself around my feet?\"","She did not let go.","Sometimes her love and her fascination with him felt too extreme. Sometimes it unsettled even him. But this was who she was. This was the woman who had torn her own Heart out and given it to him, to save him from becoming an apathetic, mindless version of himself. He could put up with a great deal of strangeness from someone who had done that.","\"I like what I like!\" Emotive said into his foot. Then she lifted her face, and her manic eyes blazed up at him. \" And I can feel so many emotions coming off your existence right now. So many! How can I be of service to you, my Everything?\"","...!","Noah looked into those eyes of boundless mania, and produced a Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin.","It hung in his palm, pale blue and humming.","He reached down with his other hand and took Emotive by the neck, not gently, and lifted her up off his feet until she hung before him, her toes dangling, her burning hair spilling around her face. Her eyes went wide and bright with delight.","He was not being cruel. He knew her. She liked to be handled a little roughly, liked to feel his grip and his certainty, and in her own mad way this was how she knew she was loved. He was only speaking her language.","Then he drove the Kryos into her chest!","She gasped, and her eyes never left his face, absolute mania and absolute trust burning in them together.","Noah went to work. He reached into her existence through the Kryos and began to build a Root, and the moment he looked closely at what was in there, he was alarmed.","He had known her emotions were strong. But..","She had elevated the Seven Deadly Sins and their Virtues to heights he had never imagined. Luxuria and Castitas, Ira and Patientia, Superbius and Humilitas, every one of them and their Egos refined and deepened and stacked atop each other in her existence until they formed a structure so dense and so volatile it hummed like a storm about to break. She had been busy, in her long dream. Terrifyingly busy.","He did not change any of it. He only used what she had already built, guiding the Kryos along the paths she had carved herself, letting her Egos and her emotions shape the Root as it formed. It was hers. He was just helping it find its footing.","Minutes passed.","HUUM!","Emotive floated free of his hand.","She hung in the dreaming air before him, arms loose at her sides, her many-colored hair streaming upward as though caught in a wind that blew from her own chest. Her whole body glowed. Waves of emotion rolled off her, one after another, joy and fury and longing and grief and a madness underneath all of it, each wave carrying the weight of an Ego so heavy it bent the woven light of THE Loom’s towers around her.","|A ROOT OF IMMENSITY has been formed.|","|Bearer: EMOTIVE.|","|THE PASSIONAL CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN.|","|THE ROOT OF EMOTION.|","|PHYSICAL ROOT OF IMMENSITY.|","|Nature: Emotion made flesh. Every feeling the bearer holds is carried in her body as mass, force, and weight. The more she feels, the heavier and stronger she becomes.|","...!","Physical?","Noah stared at the prompt!","How could a Root of Emotion be Physical and not Conceptual? Emotion was the most abstract thing he could think of. It had no shape, no weight, nothing to put your hand on. Unless it did. Unless a racing heart and shaking hands and a throat gone tight with grief were not the side effects of feeling at all, but the feeling itself. Unless every emotion she had ever had lived in her body first, and she had simply never let it be anywhere else.","His eyes shone!","Before him, Emotive dropped from the air and knelt. Terrifying waves of power and Ego vibrated off her, rippling out through the whole dream, and she bowed her burning head to him.","Anyone watching would have thought he had just wasted two Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins. One on Thalia. One here. Two of the rarest treasures of the Long Night, given away, gone.","But they would have been wrong.","His Foundation, THE Tide That Owes Nothing, sat at the very forefront of his existence now, and it was no longer simply collecting the boons of his actions and filtering them. His Provenance of THE Human Dreamer had wrapped itself around the Tide, tightly, and together they were doing something new.","| THE Tide That Owes Nothing has answered your giving.|","|Given: two Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins. Aided: the formation of two Roots of Immensity.|","|Returned, as dreamed: QUINTESSENTIAL EXISTENTIAL CHORIONIC GONADOTROPIN x10.|","|Your Root buzzes with excitement at the thought of consuming them.|","...!","Ten!","Noah felt his Root hum in his chest, eager, hungry, spinning faster at the mere thought of them. Ten Quintessential ECGs, returned for two Kryos given freely. That was the Tide. That was what happened when he gave with open hands and a clear heart.","He could be magnanimous. He could give things away, and get back even grander returns. His women and his family could be spoiled, and things could be made right for all the women he had not exactly ignored, but had never quite given their proper due.","A great many things could be made right. And in doing so, he would keep living his Dream grandly, and keep making tremendous gains, and there was no contradiction in that at all.","He was still thinking it when two small arms came around him from behind.","Emotive had risen from her kneel and come up at his back, and now she wrapped herself around him, her cheek pressed between his shoulder blades, her small hands locking tight across his chest.","\"I want to end my dream soon, \" she said softly. \" So I can be by your side again.\"","Her grip tightened.","\" I’m connected to your emotions more than anyone. So I’m the most in tune with what you feel, and what you want. And you, my Everything, are voracious.\"","Her voice dropped. \"I can feel the cold you’re fighting against, and taking in. I can feel your fear. Your doubts. I can feel you wondering if you have what it takes against this Long Night, for something that seems so complex, with so many moving pieces.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed as her small hands wrapped tighter around his chest!","\" But I can feel your Tyranny too, \" Emotive went on. \" Boundless. And your Quintessence, roaring inside you, screaming that even in all this, you will reign supreme. I can feel you more than anyone else can, whether you meant it to be that way or not.\"","She pressed closer.","\" Emotion is one of the strongest things in all of existence. Every lifeform does everything it does because of how it feels. Immense Ones move by emotions, an ant moves by emotion. Your grand dreams, you enact them because of how you feel. You feel grand!\"","Her voice trembled with something between devotion and madness. \" And I want to make sure existence has no choice but to bend to your will.\"","Her burning hair spilled over his shoulder.","\" This dream you put me in let me hone my emotions and my Egos. I won’t leave it just yet. But even without leaving it, I can still feel you, and I can do many things...even If I am not awake .\"","She paused as her voice turned low and very hungry. \" I’m also unfathomably thirsty. And true to my emotions. I want to spend the next few years in this dream doing some unspeakable things to you.\"","She pressed her lips to his ear.","\" Are you ready, my Master?\"","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed with voraciousness.","So did hers.","And the grand dream went on around them, the statues of him watching from every direction, the woven structures of THE Loom arching overhead, as time in the dream stretched out long and slow and theirs!"]},{"number":5810,"title":"Chapter 5810: Chapter 5809: Compression!","paragraphs":["The snow still fell on the Basal Floor, even inside a golden dream.","Noah had raised the domain around the place where the crow had died, a sphere of soft blue-gold haze floating in the frozen dark, and inside it the air was warm and still.","The shattered Dimensions hung beyond its edge in their thousands. And the snow came down through the dream anyway, slow and fat, settling on the golden haze and melting there into small bright drops that never quite reached the ground.","Ling sat cross-legged on a drift of dream-cloud with her chin in her hands.","Cheeks pressed into her palms, elbows on her knees, she was watching him, her face flushed. The ribbons were gone, her hair loose and tangled, and she had the dazed, bright-eyed look of someone who had just learned something she had not expected to learn.","Their educational entanglement had ended a little while ago!","Now Noah was dancing!","He moved in the center of the golden domain, barefoot on the air, stripped to the waist, and he was performing THE Kindled Circle. The dance her father had passed down to her. She had shown it to him, turning by turning, somewhere in the middle of everything else, and he had learned it as he learned everything that mattered: completely.","His arms swept out in a wide, unbroken arc. His body turned with it. Circles within circles, every motion flowing into the next with no seam between them, and then his feet struck the air, heel and ball, a hard stamp that rolled through the domain like a drum!","He waved a hand in the middle of a turning.","A Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin appeared in his palm!","It was not pale blue like the Kryos. It was blue and gold, the exact colors of his own Provenance, dense and humming and shaped like nothing he had words for, a small star pressed down into itself a thousand times over. The Tide had returned it to him, and it knew him.","He swallowed it without breaking the dance.","It went down into him like a sun, and his Root drank it and spun!","Ling’s hands slid down to cover her mouth!","The second turning. His palms struck his own chest and thighs, call and answer, and a second Quintessential ECG appeared, and he swallowed that too. The third turning, and a third. With each one his body answered. The muscle across his shoulders and back thickened, dense and heavy. Tendrils of blue-gold light spread acros his bare chest and down his arms, branching and glowing just beneath the skin like rivers seen from very high, and every tendril pulsed in time with the stamping of his feet!","Four! Five!","He grew. Not taller, exactly, though he was taller. Denser. More there. His crystalline skin took on the dark sheen of polished diamond-jade, and the tendrils of light burning beneath it made him look like something cut from a mountain and set alight from within. His hair rose off his shoulders and hung in the air as though it had forgotten how to fall.","Around his head, the light gathered into a shape, a broad and jagged crown of blue-gold radiance that swept back from his brow like the horns of some ancient war-lord, and the mobius at the center of his chest spun so fast it blurred into a solid disc of light!","Six! Seven!","The Kindled Circle was drawing him closer to his Root with every turning. He could feel it happening. The distance between Noah and THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin, which had never been large, was growing smaller and smaller, the Root and the man leaning into each other as two halves of a thing lean together before they close.","Eight!","His stamping shook the whole dream. Snow fell faster outside the golden haze.","Nine!","On the twelfth turning, he spun so fast that the blue-gold light wrapped him entirely, and he stopped.","He stood in the center of the dream, bare-chested and burning, the crown of light blazing around his head, every tendril beneath his skin lit at once. He was breathing slow and deep. His eyes were very calm.","One Quintessential ECG remained, drifting at his side. Nine were inside him now.","And his existence began to change!","| THE Kindled Circle has been performed. Your Root and your existence have drawn nearer to one another than ever before.|","|Nine Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins have been consumed.|","|Your existence has been compressed and refined beyond its prior limit. What was many is becoming one.|","...!","He felt it before the prompts finished.","Everything he was, every ability and Foundation and Inscription, every trick and art and scrap of power he had gathered across an entire existence, all of it was sliding together. Pressing close. Finding the places where one thing and another thing were really the same thing wearing two names, and closing the gap.","The Dual Root at the center of him was doing it, and he was so close to his Root now that he could feel it choosing.","| Consolidation has begun.|","|THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer has absorbed THE Provenance of THE Immense Sovereign.|","|They were never two. The Sovereign’s authority to perceive and rewrite the foundational design of any existence now flows through your Dreams. What you dream of a being, you may also build into it.|","|THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer retains its Quality of Time.|","| THE Nine Foundations have become THE One Foundation.|","|THE Unkneeling Crown, THE Tide That Owes Nothing, THE Mirror That Keeps, THE Hunger That Refines, THE Unmoved Verdict, THE Pure Trajectory, THE All-Drawing Stillness, THE Remembered Truth, and THE Sovereign Existence have collapsed into a single bedrock beneath your existence.|","| THE One Foundation: Ineffable. It cannot be made to kneel, moved, compelled, deceived, or diverted. Everything drawn to you is refined without waste. Everything observed is kept. Everything given returns grander. Existence near you must conform to what you are.No weight laid upon you is ever wasted. Pressure, suppression, command, and cold do not lift from you, but where they press, they are kept and built upon, each burden hardening into more of the floor you stand on. Even THE Counting, bearing down upon your Root, now leaves behind a sliver of foundation for every moment you bear it.|","...!","Noah breathed out!","The prompts kept coming!","| Core Capability I: THE Dream Without a Far Wall.|","|Consolidated from: THE Infinite Dream; the Sentence I Dream of Healing Infinitely; Perpetual Baryogenesis; Bedrock; the Sediment-Shed.|","|Your Dream has no end, and neither do you. Death within your Dream is not death. Whatever is broken is dreamed whole before your existence can come apart. What is borrowed cannot settle on you. You do not recover; you refuse the wound. Every death you return from, you dream once more, slowly, from within. You learn the blow that killed you, and how it found you, and it can never kill you the same way twice|","| Core Capability II: THE Sovereign of the Lived Hour.|","|Consolidated from: THE Osmontian Inscription of THE Dreaming Hour (THE Lived Hour, THE Dreamt Epoch, THE Hour That Dreams); Foundational Acceleration; the Quality of Time.|","| Every second you exist, your existence is refined as though far more time had passed in your Dreams. You may enter a deep Dream and compress an Epoch of refinement into a held moment. Time that acts upon you is drawn into your Dreams, and a dreaming hour moves as you would have it move.|","| Core Capability III: THE Waking Decree.|","|Consolidated from: THE Waking Dream; the Dream Engine; Dream-steering; the passive dreaming of existence near you; the Sentence I Dream of Your End; THE Dream State of Sonder.|","|You may dream around any existence without putting it to sleep, so that it fights as one dreaming. You may enter, steer, and build within the Dreams of others. Existence near you dreams whether you will it or not. What you behold with certainty, you may dream to its end, and what is dreamed away returns to you. You see every being as the center of its own story, and are not moved by it.|","| Core Capability IV: THE Living Grammar.|","|Consolidated from: THE Osmontian Tongue (the Letters I Am, Osmont, Quintessential, Human, and Protagonist; the Words THE Mortal Coil and THE Unbound Lineage; the Sentences I Dream of Your End and I Dream of Healing Infinitely).|","|Your Tongue is no longer a list. It is a grammar. Letters may be spoken alone, joined into Words, or composed into Sentences in the moment of need, each one drawing on your whole existence. THE Mortal Coil disallows borrowed authority wherever it is spoken. THE Unbound Lineage frees a line of descent from any hand behind it. A Sentence you compose may be spoken onto another. For as long as you will it, they carry that Sentence as though it were their own, drawing on your Tongue to heal, to end, or to endure|","| Core Capability V: THE Rendered Design.|","|Consolidated from: the Rendering’s Ruling; the Sovereign’s foundational design (absorbed), the inverted-Elsedimension technique; Infinite Sanguine Cause Mortar.|","|You may render shapes that pull, push, grow, and shrink existence, partition a Root or a being along its natural seams, seal what must be quarantined inside itself, and mortar what you build with your own blood and Causes. What you design, holds.|","| Core Capability VI: THE Tide-Crowned Protagonist.|","|Consolidated from: THE Tide That Owes Nothing; the Letter Protagonist; THE Meta-Fictional Protagonist Mantle (hidden); THE Mirror That Keeps; THE Hunger That Refines.|","|The story you walk through bends its spoils toward you. Every enemy you grant death to becomes a Chapter concluded, and what it carried flows to you. Every gift you give freely returns as what can be dreamed. Any capability you witness, you may study and keep. Everything you consume is integrated without waste. You perceive, faintly, the shape of the next great adversity turning toward you, and the spoils it carries, before either arrives. It comes to you as a title without a page. This is known as THE Unwritten Page.|","| Core Capability VII: THE Unkneeling Chill.|","|Consolidated from: THE Unkneeling Crown, THE Unmoved Verdict ...THE Precept of Solipsism; THE Chill of Negative Immensity.|","|You cannot be made to kneel. Bindings and commands find no hold on you. Your committed will cannot be diverted. You see beings truly beneath every mask. What cannot perceive you cannot touch you. And a chill of Negative Immensity runs through every weaving you make, so that your authority passes through any other. The cold of THE Long Night lives in your quarks, and it no longer only obeys the winter. Frost within your reach may be turned, and set upon whatever is borrowed in another, freezing it from within while leaving what is truly theirs untouched|","| Core Capability VIII: THE Sanguine Covenant.|","|Consolidated from: the Sanguine Arts; the Blood Marks...|","|Your blood is your authority. What you mark with it becomes bound to you, its fate held apart from every framework but yours. Your Provenance may divide into its Open Hand and its Closed Crown, and either may act in your stead. Those you have marked with your blood carry a sliver of your Dream within them. Should one of them die, your Dream may catch them once at the edge of their ending, and carry them home to you.|","| Substrate: Dialetheic Infinity.|","|Beneath every capability lies a truth that is also its own opposite. You are finite, and you are infinite. Every capability above draws from it without limit.|","...!","The prompts stopped.","Noah stood in the silence after them and felt what he had become.","For so long, he had been a collection of things, a Foundation here and an Inscription there, an art bolted onto a Word bolted onto a Provenance, each one grand and each one separate. Now he reached for any one of them and found all of them answering at once, because they were no longer separate. They were one body of power, moving as one.","And the Root at the center of him was so close he could almost touch it.","His Dreamer’s sight opened, and showed him.","| Noah Osmont. THE True Human Emperor. THE Human Dreamer.|","|VERITAS: 918. PROVENANCE: 950. POTENTIA: Infinite. PONDUS: 903. OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 941.|","|Density: Consolidated. The numbers count only what existence is willing to count.|","|Root: THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin. Dual Conceptual and Physical Existential Root of Immensity. Attunement: near-union. Future path: Empyros and Fiend, at once.|","|Provenance: THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer (Sovereign-absorbed, Quality of Time).|","|Foundation: THE One Foundation. Ineffable.|","|Core Capabilities: I. THE Dream Without a Far Wall. II. THE Sovereign of the Lived Hour. III. THE Waking Decree. IV. THE Living Grammar. V. THE Rendered Design. VI. THE Tide-Crowned Protagonist. VII. THE Unkneeling Chill. VIII. THE Sanguine Covenant.|","|Substrate: Dialetheic Infinity.|","|Held: one Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin.|","...!","Nine hundred and fifty!","Not quite at Minerva’s ceiling, the very number she had broken herself against trying to become something the winter would not allow. Not quite at the crow’s base, either. But these were not the same kind of number. Every point of his had been pressed and packed and refined until it held far more than any of theirs, and he knew it now as surely as he knew his own name.","Outside the golden domain, the snow fell faster!","And the figure of Ling rose up as she clapped her hands!"]},{"number":5811,"title":"Chapter 5811: Chapter 5810: Brutality! I","paragraphs":["He wanted to test a few things of his newly elevated power, so he tested them.","He started with the frost. Snow was still drifting down through the edge of the golden dome, and he reached for one flake and asked the cold inside it to turn. It did. The flake stopped in the air, spun once, and drifted back up along its own path, against the fall of every other flake around it. He tried a second, and a third. They all answered.","Next, THE Unwritten Page.","He reached for it as he would reach for a thought at the edge of sleep, and something came. A title, faint and unfinished, hanging in his mind with nothing written under it. He could not read all of it. Enough of it was legible to know it pointed downward, deeper into the Basal Floor, toward the direction the Glacial Record had shown him. More information wss slowly coming from this as it seemed to be running in thr background for now.","Last, the Lent Clause.","He told Ling what he wanted to try something.","\" Big Boy, you have already tried many things today. What more are you planning on doing?\"","He spoke I Dream of Healing Infinitely onto her.","WUU!","It settled into her like a coat laid over her shoulders. She looked at her hands, then bit the pad of her own thumb until it bled. The cut closed before the first drop could fall.","\" Oh,\" she said. Her eyes had gone very bright, and she kept looking at her thumb as though it had told her a secret.","Results, then. The frost turned. The Page gave him a direction and was still working right now to give him results. And the Clause held on someone else.","He focused on something else.","The memory of the Caretaker being led away in chains was not the only thing the crow had carried.","Ruination spent a long while going through the rest of it! The devoured weavings of the crow had settled into Noah when its body turned to dream, and she read them as she read everything now, thread by thread, perfectly, keeping all of it.","Most of what she found was hunger. Ages of it, flat and endless, the long patrol of a thing that circled the same frozen islands and ate whatever came through the barrier. A good part of the rest was cold, simply cold, the texture of the Long Night soaking through a mind until there was nothing else in it.","But under the hunger and the cold, there were shapes. Routes. Places the crow had been told never to go. Places it had been told to guard. And other things, much larger than it, that it had been afraid of its whole existence!","Ruination passed it to him piece by piece, and Noah listened with his eyes closed.","It was not enough! It was a map drawn by something that had only ever walked one corridor.","So he reached for THE Unwritten Page to finish its work!","He pressed on it, and fed it everything Ruination had pulled from the crow, every route and every forbidden place, and let the Page make the shape of what lay ahead.","The title sharpened. And under it, for the first time, a page began to write itself!","| THE Unwritten Page turns.|","|THE Undersnow is not a single place. It is a descent.|","|THE Basal Floor is its uppermost layer. Here prowl the Guards: Empowered Hollow Night Lifeforms, each one bound to a stretch of frozen dark, each one carrying a Lesser Kryos within it. They do not live here. They keep watch here.|","|Beneath THE Basal Floor lies the second layer.|","|THE Evergrave of THE Unthawed Ages.|","...!","The name settled into him grandly.","| THE Evergrave is not a floor. It is an expanse. It holds skies, seas, frozen Dimensionalities, and lands that stretch farther than any Guard has ever wandered.|","|Its inhabitants are not Hollow as they are Night Lifeforms in truth: whole, aware, and old beyond counting. They remember, and speak, and keep customs no living thing has kept for a very long time.|","|They were not born there.|","|Every one of them unjustly died. Across the ages, and across the cycles of existence that came before this one, reaching back to before THE First Sundering. And when they died, the Night did not let them go. It kept them and has maintained their existences ever since.|","|Many of them are First Lifeforms.|","|Within THE Evergrave, lifeforms approaching Immensity, and lifeforms seated at it, are abundant.|","|Extreme caution is recommended.|","...!","Noah opened his eyes!","First Lifeforms. Provenance Lifeforms from the very beginning! Dead, all of them. Dead for longer than the Legacies had existed. And kept. Held in the cold by the Night, their existences maintained, age after age after age, and The Long Night that was abundant here...now permeated across existence.","Why?!","Why would a winter keep its dead? For what? And who had the Caretaker been, to walk among them and come above the Undersnow to give him missions, and who was the faceless thing that had chained her and led her down toward them?","He did not have the answer. He had a direction, and a name, and a warning, and a great deal more to think about than he had had an hour ago.","And he had one more thing!","Because the Page had not stopped at the Evergrave. At the very bottom of it, there was another line, shorter than the rest, and it was not about the layers below. It was about right now. About the golden bubble of dream he had raised over the place where the crow had died, and what was waiting on the other side of its walls.","He read it twice!","Then he let out a slow breath and looked at Ling.","She was still sitting on her drift of dream-cloud, watching him, but the dazed look had gone out of her face. She had seen his eyes open.","\" Hey ,\" Noah said. \" We’re going to be pressed a bit, and made to suffer. But even you shouldn’t die with my Osmontian Tongue on you. Hang in there, okay?\"","He said it simply. Then he picked the tenth Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin out of the air beside him and threw it to her.","She caught it!","Her eyes went wide!","It was the last one. She held it in her palm and stared at him as if he had tossed her his own heart. Then her existence drew it in. Greedily, all at once, the blue-gold star sinking into her palm and vanishing, and her whole body lit up from the inside. The Root that was her entire existence drank it and blazed, and she shone, her skin glowing gold-violet, her loose hair lifting, the air around her humming with a power that had not been there a heartbeat ago!","He had meant it as preparation.","Then he waved his hand.","The clouds of dream fell!","The golden haze that had held them came down all at once, sinking away into nothing, and the frozen dark of the Basal Floor rushed back in around them. Cold, first. Then the torn Dimensions drifting in their thousands, and the snow, no longer melting, falling straight onto their faces.","And the things that had been waiting in ambush that he had forseen!","There were nine of them!","They had gathered around the dream while it stood, silent, patient, ringed in a wide circle across the floating islands and the empty dark, and every one of them was as large as the crow had been. Some were larger. All of them were Empowered Hollow Night Lifeforms, and every one of them was looking at him.","A wolf with three heads, each one a different age of the same animal, pup and prime and grey-muzzled elder, frost dripping from all three jaws.","A whale that swam through the empty air, vast and slow, its ribs showing white through its frozen hide, whole drowned Dimensions trapped in the ice of its belly.","A spider with legs of clear glass, each leg taller than a mountain, and in the web it had strung between two torn Dimensions hung frozen bodies, hundreds of them, turning slowly in the cold.","A headless titan in armor of black ice, sitting astride a horse made entirely of snow.","An elk whose antlers were a chandelier of frozen light, every branch hung with small pale flames that did not melt anything.","A scorpion of blue ice as long as a mountian range, its tail curled high, its stinger dripping something colder than frost.","An owl with a hundred faces where its one face should have been, all of them human, all of them with their eyes closed.","A hydra of icicles, nine necks swaying, every head blind.","And at the center of the ring, rising up out of the dark before them, the ninth.","A Naga!","Its lower body was a serpent’s coil so long its tail vanishd somewhere among the distant islands, scaled in white and pale blue, and its upper body was a creature with the shape of a woman and none of the warmth of one. It had six arms, long and thin and jointed wrong, each hand holding a blade of rime. Its hood flared wide behind its head, and the inside of that hood was lined with frozen eyes. Its face was beautiful and fiendish and utterly cold, and it smiled at him with far too many teeth.","Noah’s panel-sight flickered across all nine, and every reading came back at the crow’s level or higher!","Okay! They saved him the time to go looking!","The Naga lowered its head toward him!","|You do not belong here.|","|But you do not listen, so...|","|Let this place where you have killed also be your grave.|","...!","---","<THE Verdant Regard>","It was always spring in the Existential Immense Domain of THE Verdant Regard.","It had been spring there since before some Legacies were founded. Endless meadows rolled away under a pale green sky, thick with flowers that bloomed and fell and bloomed again without ever wilting. Rivers of clear sap ran between them. Trees older than most Dimensions leaned ovver those rivers, their leaves whispering softly, and everything in the whole vast domain grew toward its center, toward her, as flowers turn toward the sun.","The snow had found its way in anyway!","It fell on the meadows in thin grey flakes, and wherever it landed, the flowers did not wilt. They simply stopped. Frozen mid-bloom, petals half open, waiting for a warmth that did not come.","At the center of it all, THE Verdant Regard sat on a bed of moss with her daughter in her arms.","Minerva had not woken! Her body lay limp against her mother’s chest, pale and still, the crooked crown of leaves long gone from her head. Beside them, on the moss, lay the illusory green Root that had been severed on the Plain of Accord. It was frozen now, all the way through! The frost had crept up from its broken end until there was no green left in it at all.","THE Verdant Regard looked at it, and did not move.","Something buzzed at this time.","A faint vibration at the edge of her domain, polite, asking for entry. She knew the shape of it before she even turned her attention toward it, and had known that shape for a very long time.","She let it in.","The air of the domain split open like an eyelid, and he stepped through!","THE SLEEPLESS FIEND did not come as an eye this time. He came as a figure, tall and dark and hazy at the edges, his face barely perceptible, and his presence pressed down on the spring meadows until the frozen flowers bowed. He walked toward her through the snow without hurry.","\" THE Keepers of Existence have confirmed it again,\" he said. His voice was low and warm and very reasonable. \" And again. Riven is one of the keys. Perhaps the major key. Even with the winter growing colder, everything remains on track for him.\"","He stopped a few paces from her.","\" We know none of those already Immense will find the door to THE Great Becoming. It has to be an Immensity that rises after the Long Night. And this newest change, Roots no longer able to mature into Immensity at all, only confirms that we are heading in the right direction. I came to ask you to place your cards on the right lifeform. With Riven, things are confirmed. We can all support him. And we can all gain our access.\"","The snow fell between them.","\"The first Root formed after the Long Night, Osmont, may be a key as well. Even if he is not, he is an anomaly enough that Riven feels he needs to devour what Osmont holds, to ensure his own success .\" His voice softened.","\" So I came to ask. Let us work together, as we used to. Allow us to take Osmont. I am sure there are others, even in THE Legacy of THE Acharya, who have their doubts. Let us get past this together.\"","He came around behind her!","He stood at her back, and his hand came up, slow and tender, and his fingers traced the side of her neck. Lightly. Almost lovingly. Then his hand slid down her arm, and found hers, and his fingers wove through her own.","She was looking at her daughter’s face.","\"I am sorry for our daughter, \" THE SLEEPLESS FIEND said quietly.","...!","Our daughter!","\" Through her, I sensed he was involved as well. Yes? \"","His thumb moved slowly across the back of her hand. \" Existence wraps tightly around anomalies. Even if he is not a key, he is certainly an important weaving. Can I count on you again?\"","THE Verdant Regard said nothing!","\" If you say yes, I will contact the others and make things ready. Moriarty and a few more will stay loyal to Lucy’s teachings. They will not move. \"","His fingers tightened, very slightly, around hers. \"So it may be a small war, to get Osmont. Or it may be a simple extraction, if we plan well enough.\"","...!","THE Verdant Regard looked down at the frozen Root on the moss.","She looked at it for a long time. Her eyes were heavy, full of grief so old and so deep! The snow settled on the frozen Root, and on her daughter’s still face, and on her own green hair.","Then her eyes sharpened!","She raised her head. Not toward the Fiend. Past him, past the edge of her domain, past the Legacy’s thousand mountains and the blizzard howling between them, toward a place most beings could not have seen at all. A lone dark mountain, wrapped in a trembling coat of hazy Immensity, burning steady against the storm!","Her gaze held there, sharp as a blade.","And her fingers closed tighter around the hand of THE SLEEPLESS FIEND."]},{"number":5812,"title":"Chapter 5812: Chapter 5811: Brutality! II","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","The Naga’s words had barely finished falling when all nine Guards moved at once!","They came from every direction, above and below and to every side, the ring they had formed around the dream closing like a fist. The whale dove. The wolf’s three heads howled in three different ages of the same voice, and the spider’s glass legs stabbed down through the dark.","Across the ring, the owl’s hundred faces turned toward them in perfect unison, and every one of those closed human eyes began, very slowly, to open.","Noah had perhaps half an instant to think.","Nine of them. Each one at the crow’s level or higher, and the crow alone had killed him once. Ling at his side, shining with the Quintessential ECG he had just thrown her. The Lent Clause already sitting in her like a coat. His eight Core Capabilities, untested in a real fight, all of them still more promise than proof.","As brutal and painful as this would be...it was a great test of what he had become as he welcomed it with unbound tyranny, his body erupting with golden clouds of infinite dreams!","\" You first,\" he said, looking at the Hydra.","Ling was already moving.","The hydra reached them first because it had nine heads and did not need to see where it was going. Its necks of icicle lashed out in a blind fan, and Ling went straight through the middle of them. Her leg came around in a blur of blue silk and shattered one head, then another, then a third, the ice bursting into glittering fragments as her thighs were packed with enough density to crush trillions of Dimensions!","The heads grew back before the fragments had finished falling.","That was a problem. Noah watched the regrowth once, saw where the cold of THE Long Night flowed up from the hydra’s chest to rebuild each head, and knew where to put his hand.","He had wanted to test the frost on something living. Here it was. He could also control THE Long Night!","He flew in under the fan of necks, his Provenance pressuring the creature as if he weighed infinite density, and he laid his palm flat against the hydra’s breast, and tugged on the cold inside it.","It was the easiest thing he had ever done. The Long Night’s cold lived in his quarks, and the cold inside the hydra was the same cold, borrowed, poured into it by the winter to keep it moving. He simply told that cold to face the other way.","HUUUM!","More than a hundred Provenance Essence burned in his body, but...","The cold did what he commanded it to do!","It turned inward, and froze the hydra from its heart outward, nine necks locking rigid one after another, until the whole creature hung in the air as a single sculpture of blue ice.","Ling kicked it as grandly...","It exploded into powder!","BOOM!","Result: With enough Provenance burned, the frost worked on even a Hollow Night Lifeform. It did not touch what was truly the creature’s own, and there had not been much of that in a Guard.","His new Foundation and Tide worked without him doing a thing as he stood above the corpse of another lifeform, his mouth open as blue gold lava like mist leaked from him, his eyes shooting beams of light as he looked fiendish!","|A Guard has been granted death.|","|The Chapter it carried has concluded.|","|Spoils: Lesser Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin x10. Memories of a Guard.|","...!","Ten!","Ten small snowflake crystals spun out of the drifting powder and into his hand, and behind them came the memories, a thin cold thread of them, sinking into his mind.","He did not have time for much thinking or memories as...","The wolf’s three heads came down on him from above!","The pup’s jaws closed on his left arm, the prime’s on his right shoulder, the grey elder’s on his throat. And he felt it all as their Provenance burned!","They were not biting through his body. They were biting through his time. The pup’s bite made his arm young, soft, unfinished. The elder’s made his throat old, thin, failing. Between them, the prime held him and tore.","It hurt. It hurt in a direction he had not known pain could come from!","But he had met THE First Gu of Time and had felt the death of time itself!","So fuck this motherfucker!","Noah reached for THE Sovereign of the Lived Hour, and drew the wolf’s time into his Dreams.","HUUM!","A dreaming hour moved as he wished it to move. The pup’s jaws went slack, then soft, then aged in a heartbeat into the jaws of something ancient. The elder’s jaws went the other way, back and back, until they belonged to a newborn that could not close them at all.","Suddenly all three heads were the same age: old, older, oldest, the whole creature pouring through its own lifetime in the space of a breath.","He dreamed that an infinite time ravaged across its existence!","It died of old age with its teeth still in him.","He pulled its jaws off his throat and let the corpse fall!","|A Guard has been granted death. Spoils: Lesser Kryos x10. Memories of a Guard.|","Twenty. He had twenty now Lesser Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins now!","He took eight of them, pressed them together in his palms, and felt them fuse. Four into one. Four into one. Two genuine Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins lay in his hands, cold and humming.","He did not keep them.","He sent them down through his own existence and into THE Infiniverse, into the Dream Engine, into the dreams of the people sleeping on the golden shore. One to his mother. One to Seo-yeon. He felt them land, felt each one settle into a dreaming existence like a stone dropped into a well, and felt the Tide notice at once.","| THE Tide That Owes Nothing has answered your giving.|","|Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin x5.|","Five blue-gold stars bloomed at his side.","He ate them one after another, without stopping, while the spider’s glass legs came stabbing down around him, and each one went into him like a sun and packed itself down into his Root!","The attacks did not stop even as he sought to advance!","That was how it went, after that. He stopped counting the minutes.","The scorpion caught him from behind and put its stinger through his chest. Whatever dripped from it was colder than frost, colder than the current Long Night, a cold that did not freeze but ended. He died...well, not really.","The golden clouds caught him and spat him back out, and in the instant of coming back he dreamed that death through once, slowly, from the inside. He learned the cause of the dreamed death. He learned the angle and the timing and the exact shape of the Dimensionality that had killed him.","The scorpion stung him again with its concentrated cold and Provenance, but this time...","It went nowhere. The stinger slid off him as though it had struck a wall, and the scorpion recoiled, confused, and Noah reached out and broke its tail off at the base with one hand, his Dream of it ending covering its body as a cloudy light covered it, and it began to flake off!","\" OOOOOH!\"","Not even screaming did a damn fucking thing.","Ling finished it. She came down on its back with both heels and drove it into a floating island so hard the island split in half, and she kept kicking until the scorpion stopped moving and the island stopped being an island. Its stinger stabbed Ling many times, but she was healed instantly for anything that passed through!","| Spoils: Lesser Kryos x10. Memories of a Guard.|","He fused eight. Two Kryos, down into the dreams of Henry and Adelaide.","| Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin x5.|","He ate them all.","What he was doing now almost became second nature as he killed, he gave away, and he got back even more in return!","But the brutal battle was still ongoing.","The owl opened its eyes.","All hundred faces at once, every eye in every one of them snapping open and fixing on the two of them, and the weight of that gaze came down like a mountain! It was a perception so total that it did not just see them. It held them. Ling froze mid-kick, locked in place, her mouth opening in a silent scream as a hundred human gazes crushed down on her Root.","Noah was not held.","He looked at the owl, and the owl could not quite find him. Its hundred faces kept sliding off him, searching, blinking, their eyes watering with the strain. What could not perceive him could not touch him, and even with a hundred faces, this thing could not see him properly.","He walked up the length of its gaze, into the space between its hundred faces, and dreamed its end.","He looked magisterially grand as tendeils of blue gold leaked out of him as he stared tyrannically into a monstrous beast, his Provenance beginning to flood into it.","He looked at it with total certainty, and the owl began to dream away. Its faces went first. One by one, their eyes closed again, and they flaked off into golden dust and drifted into him. Then its feathers. Then its body. Ling dropped free and caught herself in the air, gasping, as the last of the owl’s hundred faces went soft and gold and gone.","| Spoils: Lesser Kryos x10. Memories of a Guard.|","The loot was fused and sent to Barbatos. And another to Adelaide, because he could!","| Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin x5.|","He ate them.","He was getting stronger. He could feel it now, not in steps but in a steady rising pressure, as a flood rises behind a wall. Every Kryos he gave away came back to him as something grander, and everything that came back to him he swallowed, and his Root drank and drank and would not stop.","The remaining Guards had noticed as the pressure he radiated has nearly fucking doubled as it was insane.","He finally felt like he was returning to his old self!","The Empowered Hollow Night Lifeforms pulled back. The spider, the elk, the whale, the headless titan, and the Naga, all five of them drawing out of reach and circling, wary now. Four of their number were dead. They had come to bury him, and he was burying them instead!","Ling came up beside him, bleeding from both arms and the side of her head, her gold-violet light flickering where the owl’s gaze had crushed it.","Noah asked her mentally, in a few words, whether she could keep going. She told him, in fewer, exactly where he could put that question. She was smiling when she said it as her fair complexion looked extremely murderous!","He put a hand on her shoulder and turned the Lent Clause up even more.","\" Then let’s finish it ,\" he said.","The spider had spent the pause building. Its web stretched between three torn Dimensions now, thick with frozen bodies, every strand of it humming with a cold that caught and held. It flung the whole web at them at once.","Noah rendered.","A shape bloomed in the air before him, and another inside it, and another, a nested design of partition. He did not burn the web or break it. He found its seams, the natural lines where it had been woven together, and cut along all of them at once. The web fell apart into a thousand clean pieces, and the frozen bodies tumbled loose and drifted away into the dark, and the spider was left standing on its glass legs with nothing between it and him.","His golden clouds how now become a sea as they crashed down into it!","The elk lowered its chandelier antlers and every small pale flame on them flared white, and the light that came off them was a light that erased. Where it touched, things stopped having been. Noah felt it take a piece of his shoulder and leave nothing behind, not even a wound.","He spoke.","\"I Dream of Your End.\"","And while the elk’s erasing light was still pouring across him, he composed another Sentence in the moment and spoke it onto Ling. She carried it at once, the Clause settling onto her, and she flew straight through the elk’s white light untouched and kicked its antlers off its head.","BOOM!","His Provenance and her ridiculous existence imposed itself on thr creature simultaneously as it could do nothing else!","The elk dreamed away into gold.","| Spoils: Lesser Kryos x10, and again x10. Memories of two Guards.|","Four more Kryos, fused and given. His mother again. Seo-yeon again. Henry. Emotive, still dreaming in her Earliest Folds.","Well, there were Kazuhiko and Erikson and others, but their time would come.","| Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin x10.|","He ate them all!","WUU!","Simultaneously...the whale came down on them like a falling Dimension.","It was the largest of the nine, the size of a contnent, and it simply swam down onto them through the dark, meaning to crush them flat against a floating island under the whole weight of its frozen body and the drowned Dimensions inside it.","Noah did not move out of its way.","He let it land on him. All of it, the whole impossible mass pressing down, and THE One Foundation took the weight and kept it. Did not lift it. Did not resist it. Simply kept it, and built on it, and every immensity of that pressure hardened into more of the floor beneath him. He stood under the whale and felt himself grow heavier with every heartbeat it spent trying to crush him!","Then he pushed up as he looked like a fiendish dreamer bearing the weight of all of existence!","The whale rose. It was lifted, slowly, bodily, by a man standing under it, and Ling came in from the side and drove her knee into its eye as she struck like a sharp blade, piercing into it!","Noah’s Provenance added on as he dreamed it dead, and between the two of them, they broke it open along its spine. The drowned Dimensions in its belly spilled out into the dark, frozen, silent, and the whale went still.","The headless titan charged before the whale had finished falling.","It came on its horse of snow with a sword of black ice as long as a river, and its first swing caught Ling across the waist and threw her half a Gigaparsec!","Noah’s eyes flashed coldly.","He let his Provenance divide.","The Closed Crown rose out of him, arms crossed, dark gold at the edges, a smaller shape of himself burning with every scrap of his tyranny, and he did not hold it back. He stepped aside and let it act in his stead. Seas of infinite Dreams raged out and converged on it!","It met the titan’s next swing with its bare forearm and shattered the sword with boundless dreams, then took the titan’s horse by the neck and snapped it.","Last, it took the titan by the stump where its head should have been, and pulled, and the titan came apart in its hands like a doll made of frozen straw.","Across the dark, Ling got up. She wiped the blood off her mouth and looked at the Closed Crown, and then at Noah, and did not say anything at all.","| Spoils: Lesser Kryos x10, and again x10. Memories of two Guards.|","More loot was fused as this time, Kazuhiko and THE Emperor Penguin got something!","| Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin x10.|","He ate them.","And then there was only the Naga.","\"...\"","Noah stretched and cracked his neck as he breathed out lava like blue gold flames while staring ahead.","It had not fought. It had watched, coiled at the edge of the dark, six arms still and its hood of frozen eyes open wide, while every other Guard died in front of it. Now it rose up before him, its tail vanishing into the distant islands, its six blades of rime lifting together.","Its beautiful face was no longer smiling.","Noah looked at it, and he affirmed it was the strongest of the nine by a wide margin. He could feel that, and he could also feel, underneath all its composure, that it was afraid!","So he began to dance.","THE Kindled Circle, the dance Ling had taught him in the golden dream, the dance her father had passed down to her. His arms swept out in a wide, unbroken arc, and his body turned with it, and his feet struck the empty air, heel and ball, a stamp that rolled out across the whole Basal Floor like a drum!","The Naga struck at him with all six blades at once.","He turned through them. Every blade that came at him found only the arc of his turning, the flowing, seamless motion carrying him through the gaps between the strikes, and as he turned he struck back, each stamp of his feet a blow, each sweep of his arms a cut. A blade came off in his hand. Then an arm. Then another!","His Provenance of THE Human Dreamer became sharp and deadly!","Ling came in from above, and together they took the Naga apart.","He drew closer to his Root with every turning. He could feel it happening, faster now, faster than it had in the golden dream. The Root and the man, leaning into each other, the gap between them closing.","On the ninth turning, he tore the Naga’s head open, and every frozen eye inside it brust!","On the tenth, he took its last two arms.","On the eleventh, he reached into its chest, where its cold heart pulsed around its Kryos, and closed his hand.","The Naga looked at him with its beautiful, fiendish, terrified face.","On the twelfth turning, he ripped its heart out, and it died!","| The last Guard has been granted death.|","|Spoils: Lesser Kryos x10. Memories of the Naga.|","...!","And his existence caught fire!","| THE Kindled Circle has been performed to its Truest Essence.|","|The distance between you and your Root has closed entirely.|","|Your existence and your Root have become one.|","...!","It was like nothing he had ever felt. The Root at the center of him had always been his, spinning, turning, a heart of Immensity he carried. Now there was no center to carry it in.","The Root was everywhere. It was in his skin and his blood and his packed quarks, in his Provenance and his dreams and the cold of the Long Night inside him. He...did not have a Root anymore.","He was one.","His entire existence buzzed with utterly overwhelming power, a pressure so vast and so total that the snow stopped in the air around him, and the torn Dimensions drifting in the dark trembled, and across the whole Basal Floor, everything that could still feel anything felt him.","He hung in the frozen dark among the corpses of nine Guards, with Ling beside him bleeding and staring, and sensed what he had become.","And he knew, with perfect clarity, that he could not take it any further.","He could feel the door. Exactly where it should be, at the very top of everything he now was, the place where a Root became Immense. And it was shut. Simply not there to be opened, because existence had decided there would be no more Immensity, and existence had meant it!","He could not make his Root Immense. Not now. Perhaps not ever.","Noah looked up into the falling snow as it fell more and more heavily.","\" Do I...have to be Immense?\"","His voice carried across the whole dark expanse.","\"Is Immensity the only path? If existence itself makes becoming Immense impossible, does one... simply give up?\"","The snow held still around him, as if it were listening.","\"I have advanced so much since merely shooting fireballs,\" Noah said. \" Can I...not do something unfathomably Quintessential here?\"","...!"]},{"number":5813,"title":"Chapter 5813: Chapter 5812: Epiphany!","paragraphs":["Noah looked at himself with every single sight. He turned his whole perception inward and looked at what he had become, standing in the frozen dark of the Basal Floor among the corpses of nine Guards, his existence and his Root one thing now, buzzing with a power so total that the snow still hung motionless in the air around him.","And at the very top of it, where the door should have been, there was nothing!","He looked at that nothing for a long time.","If a being could not become Immense, then that was the end of the road. Wasn’t it? That was what everyone believed. Every Provenance Lifeform, every Progeny on evry golden cloud, every Immense One on every throne. Immensity was the formula. It was the shape existence had given to growth itself, the one direction every climbing thing had always climbed. And existence had just closed it.","So that was it, then. The ceiling. The end!","But...","Was it?!","He turned the thought over again, slowly, and looked at it from the other side.","Existence had shut the door. But existence did not do things for no reason. Even the Long Night, tainted as it was, even the cold that culled and the cold that closed, even the Counting pressing on every Root in existence, all of it came from somewhere and pointed somewhere. So what was a closed door pointing at?","Everyone assumed it meant no!","What if it did not?!","\" What if it is not a negative thing? \" Noah said quietly, to the frozen dark. \" What if it is existence saying... do not follow?\"","His existence buzzed!","It shook through him from his skin to his core, a single deep resonant note, as if every packed quark in his body had just heard something it agreed with. The snow around him trembled in the air. Somewhere far off, a torn Dimension drifted, and the light inside it flickered!","|A reading of existence has been made.|","|The door to Immensity is closed to all who would pass through it.|","|A closed door does not only say no. It also says: not this way.|","|Existence has not forbidden growth. It has forbidden following.|","...!","Not this way!","Noah breathed in, slow and deep, and let his Dream open.","He dreamed an infinite dream! It was not a dream of one thing. It was a dream of everything that could be, every possible path his existence could take from this exact moment, all of them at once, spread out before him in the span of a single instant.","He saw himself Immense, and saw that version of himself crushed against the closed door, severed like Minerva, weeping in the snow . He saw himself refusing to climb and freezing slowly in the Long Night with his family around him.","He saw himself as a tyrant eating whole Legacies. He saw himself as nothing. He saw himself as everything. Billions of futures and more, branching and branching, each one real for the space of the instant, each one his.","And somewhere in all of them, under all of them, a pattern!","He came out of the instant, and it had not even been an instant!","\"I see it now ,\" Noah said.","His voice had gone very calm. Very far away.","\" All of it. Every path I could take, at once. They are all happening. They have all already happened. It is strange, how simple it looks from here.\"","He looked at his own hands. \" Every one of those paths that climbs toward Immensity ends at the same shut door. Every single one. It does not matter how strong I become, or how clever. The door is the same. It was built to stop things exactly like me.\"","The snow drifted around him.","\" But the other paths do not climb. They change.\"","He was quiet for a moment. \"I watched the ones that change. Under pressure, they become something else. They always have. A creature is cornered by the cold, and its children grow fur. A creature is starved, and its children learn to eat stone. Humans were soft things once, in places that wanted them dead, and they did not become Immense. They became...human. Over and over, under every weight that was ever laid on them, they became something that had not existed before.\"","He lifted his head.","\" Existence does not want another Immense One. It has enough of those. It has shut the old road, and every being on it will keep pushing on the door and wondering why it will not open. \" A pause. \"I do not have to push. I only have to...evolve.\"","...!","| Your Infinite Dream has gazed upon boundless possibility.|","|A path has been found where no path was written.|","|Path established: THE Osmontian Culmination.|","|Your existence may evolve.|","|Not into Immensity. Into something that has never existed.|","|Everything you have ever dreamed, every memory, every emotion, every life you lived in the death of time, every battle, every gift, every loss, every experience your existence has held across its entire span, will be gathered and culminated.|","|From all of it, a new lifeform will be made. It will be the product of everything you have lived, and it will belong to no path but your own.|","|Requirement: your present existence must first be filled to its Absolute. Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins are the current best means.|","|Present saturation: 44 integrated. Estimated saturation of your present existence: 11%.|","|The road is arduous. The resources required are unfathomable.|","|Your Dream holds that it is possible.|","...!","Eleven percent!","Forty-four Quintessential ECGs, and he was barely a tenth of the way there. Hundreds more. Perhaps far more than hundreds, if the Absolute of his existence kept growing as he grew. Every one of them earned by giving, every gift paid for by killing things like the nine Guards dead around him, and all of it under a winter that grew heavier with every Root that dared to exist.","It would be the hardest road he had ever walked!","And it was his!","Not written by Those Who Remain. Not handed down by a Legacy. Not the door every Immense One in existence had passed through and every Root in existence was now pounding on in vain. A road nobody had ever walked, because nobody had ever looked at a shut door and understood that it was pointing somewhere else.","Noah looked up into the falling snow. It had begun to move again around him, drifting down across the dead Guards and the torn Dimensions and the frozen islands of the Basal Floor, and Ling hung beside him in the dark, silent, watching his face.","He smiled!","\" Fuck Immensity, \" Noah said. \" Fuck the written path.\"","His existence buzzed, and the snow scattered around him!","\" Fuck existence.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5814,"title":"Chapter 5814: Chapter 5813: Arrogance!","paragraphs":["His mind still buzzed with his proclamations!","Thirty-four Lesser Kryos still turned in the air around Noah, pale blue and cold, the last spoils of the nine Guards.","He did not intend to keep any of them!","He pressed them together four at a time. Each set flared, fused, and settled into a single genuine Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin, dense and huming, until eight whole Kryos hung before him and two Lesser ones remained, too few to make another.","Four went to Achilles. The king had swallowed the Long Night’s cold to make his day-old Root stronger, and Noah could afford to give to help him.","Noah sent the Kryos through his Legacy body, across existence, to the mountain where Achilles stood with Rose amidst the snow.","The other four went home, into THE Infiniverse and the Dream Engine, to three people. Two to Eon. One to Ul’moreth. One to Naldine, along with the last two Lesser Kryos.","He felt each one land!","And THE Tide answered!","| THE Tide That Owes Nothing has answered your giving.|","|Given: eight Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins and two Lesser Kryos, to four lives you hold dear.|","|Returned, as dreamed: Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin x22.|","...!","Twenty-two blue-gold stars bloomed around him in the frozen dark!","He took them all, one after another, and felt each one spread through the whole of him at once. His existence climbed with every one!","| Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins integrated: 66.|","|THE Osmontian Culmination. Present saturation: 16%.|","|Estimated Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins still required: 334. The estimate will rise as your existence rises.|","...!","Sixteen percent! A long road lay ahead.","Then he looked at himself.","| Noah Osmont. THE True Human Emperor. THE Human Dreamer.|","|VERITAS: 999/1. PROVENANCE: 999/1. POTENTIA: Infinite. PONDUS: 999/1. OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: 999/1.|","...!","He frowned!","The numbers would not hold still. VERITAS read nine hundred and ninety-nine, then one, then nine hundred and ninety-nine again. PROVENANCE slid from one to nine hundred and fifty to seven hundred and back. Every line on the panel shifted between one and nine hundred and ninety-nine, never landing for longer than a breath.","He understood it quickly. His Root and his existence were one now, so there was no separate thing inside him for existence to measure. It was the same reason Ling’s panel read one in every line.","So he tested it!","He chose five hundred for VERITAS. It settled there and stayed. Nine hundred and ninety-nine, and it went there. One, and it sat quietly at one.","He stopped.","The panel was his to set anywhere in that range, and others read whatever he chose. Under it, the real thing kept climbing. The door to Immensity was shut, but his foundation could still be refined and his Provenance still elevated, and the ceiling existence had built hung over a road he no longer walked.","He left the panel at one. It seemed polite.","Then he closed his eyes and went looking through the memories of the dead!","Nine Guards,. Alone, each was a narrow corridor, one route through the frozen dark walked for longer than anything should have to walk it. He laid them over one another, route on route, island on rift on torn Dimension, and they began to fit.","| The memories of nine Guards have been combined. THE Basal Floor has been mapped.|","|THE Provenance of THE Human Dreamer now extends across the whole of it. Every Empowered Hollow Night Lifeform upon this Floor dreams a little, and where it dreams, you may perceive it.|","...!","And Ruination went further!","| Master. The map is fixed, but they are not.|","|I have run their positions through my Root and recorded every probability of their movement. You now have them in real time, and where they will be for some while after.|","...!","Noah’s eyes opened, and they shone brilliantly!","He saw the whole Basal Floor at once, through his Dreams, with Ruination’s predictions laid over it like a lattice of light. Floating islands of ice by the thousands. Torn Dimensions hanging between them, and towering cold-filled trees. And moving among it all, small bright points where the Guards were dreaming.","Fifty-five of them!","He reached for each one and felt its weight. Every one was at the Naga’s level, some grander, a few a great deal grander. Fifty-five more of what had taken everything he and Ling had to kill nine.","Then he turned his perception north, and went very still.","A rift split the frozen dark there, blue and vast. The way down. He could feel it pulling at the cold in his quarks!","And coiled around its mouth, like a guard dog around a dor, was something that did not fit on the map at all.","It was colossal! The floating islands near it drifted in its shadow. He could not make out its shape. It had too many limbs, or none, or limbs made of the same frozen dark as the space around it, and a halo of stilled snow hung motionless over where its head should be.","Its aura was wrong!","It was Immense, and it was not. The weight he had felt on the Plain of Accord when the thrones filled was there, and then gone, and then there again, as though this thing had climbed toward the door of Immensity, stopped exactly halfway, and stood on that threshold for longer than anything should stand anywhere.","It was not asleep!","He refocused. He turned from the rift in the north to the fifty-five bright points scattered across the dark, and began, very calmly, to plan which one to kill first.","But...","Then he stopped planning!","\" Why one at a time? \" he said.","Ling looked at him. He was not speaking to her.","\"I see all of them. Where they are now, where they will be, every path each of them will walk for some while yet. I see them as a sky sees the ground.\"","His voice was very calm.","\" Fifty-five points. And I was about to choose among them as though I were one of them. As though I had to go to each in turn and stand before it and trade blows until one of us fell.\"","He looked out across the frozen dark.","\" That is the common sense of this place. The Guard patrols its corridor, and the one who comes to kill it walks the corridor too. I do not need to walk their corridors.\"","He raised his hand, and began to build!","Not a weapon anyone else had made. He had none, and wanted none. Instead he reached into what he now was, Core Capabilities moving as one body, and chose the pieces.","First, the shape. THE Rendered Design drew it in the dark: a great curved frame rendered out of nested pull and push, its limbs sweeping outward and back, partitioned along the seams where a bow must bend and mortared at the grip with his own blood and Teloi so that it would hold under any strain. What he designed, held.","Then the draw. THE One Foundation settled into the limbs as weight.","Then the string. THE Living Grammar spun it from a single Sentence, spoken quietly into the air and drawn taut: I Dream of Your End. Whatever the string sent forward would go already carying that decree.","Then the arrow, and that was the part that made the frozen dark itself go quiet!","He reached into THE Sovereign of the Lived Hour. Every second he existed, he was refined as though far more time had passed inside his Dreams. He had never once turned that the other way. Now he did. He opened a deep Dream and let an Epoch pour into it, and then another, and another, time without end, and he did not refine anything with it. He dreamed it decaying.","Trillions of years of wearing down, of erosion, of stone to sand and sand to dust and dust to nothing, of every bond in a thing slowly letting go of every other. And then he dreamed that decay across trillions more years, and pressed all of it, every aeon of it, down into a single point, and drew that point out along the string into the shape of an arrow.","Last, the edge. THE Unkneeling Chill ran through the arrowhead, the Negative Immensity in his weavings that let his authority pass through any other, and the Kneeling Frost with it, the Long Night’s own cold, turned to hunt whatever was borrowed in a thing.","He closed his hand around the grip!","| THE Rendered Design, THE One Foundation, THE Living Grammar, THE Sovereign of the Lived Hour, and THE Unkneeling Chill have been combined.|","|Its string is the Sentence I Dream of Your End. Everything it looses carries that decree.|","|Its arrows are Epochs of decay. Each one holds trillions of years of time’s erosion on all authority, dreamed across trillions more, compressed to a single point. What an arrow strikes, it ages through all of them at once.|","|Its edge carries the Chill of Negative Immensity and THE Kneeling Frost. Its arrows pass through authority, and turn the borrowed cold within their targets against them.|","|THE Tide-Crowned Protagonist binds the whole: what the bow grants death to, its spoils flow to you.|","|Substrate: Dialetheic Infinity. Your Dream has no far wall. Its arrows have no end.|","...!","He looked at what he had made!","The bow was blue and gold and taller than a mountain, its limbs curving back at their tips like the horns of the crown of light above his brow. The same tendrils that burned beneath his skin ran through its frame, pulsing in time with his existence. It did not look forged. It looked dreamed, because it was, and it looked alive, because it was part of him.","He set his feet on the empty air.","Bare to the waist, skin dark diamond-jade, tendrils branching over his chest and arms, hair hanging weightless around that jagged crown, the bow in his hand, he looked like a fiend out of a dream. A dream archer, drawing on the dark itself!","And both his paths moved through him when he drew. The Fiend was the weight in the limbs and the density of the body holding them. The Empyros was the decree in the string and the Epochs dreamed into the arrow. An arrow from this bow would land as a mountain, and as a sentence, and as the end of more time than anything it struck had ever lived.","He drew the string back!","The arrow formed as he drew, and kept growing. Past the length of the bow. Past the size of a floating island. By the time the string reached his ear, it stretched across gigaparsecs, a spear of compressed aeons so heavy that the torn Dimensions near it began to drift toward it!","Space around him twisted. The frozen dark bent inward toward the arrowhead in long curving lines, and the Dimensionality of the whole region strained at its seams, groaning, as the thing he held pressed on everything around it just by existing.","The snow nearest the arrow aged as it fell, going grey, then brittle, then to powder before it reached the edge of his light.","Ling had backed away several islands’ worth of distance without seeming to decide to as her thighs vibrated!","Noah looked down the arrow at all fifty-five bright points at once.","He let go!","The arrow left the string and split. One became many in a single instant, fifty-five arrows of blue-gold time tearing away in fifty-five directions, each one gigaparsecs long, each one following a line of Ruination’s lattice to exactly where its target would be when it arrived.","An instant passed. And...","HUUM!","The first one hit!","It struck a three-legged titan of hail in the far east, and the titan aged. All of it, all at once. Its ice clouded, then cracked, then crumbled, trillions of years of forced Dimensional erosion arriving in the space of a single heartbeat. Its legs went to gravel beneath it. The island it stood on wore down to sand and drifted apart, and three torn Dimensions nearby went grey and brittle and collapsed like old paper in a fire. When the light faded, half the titan was gone, simply worn away to nothing, and the half that remained was flaking into gold, dreaming toward its end!","Then the rest hit!","Across the whole Basal Floor, fifty-four more flashes bloomed, each one a sphere of blue-gold light where a Guard had been struck by more time than its whole existence had ever held. The sound came late and all at once, one vast rolling roar that shook the islands in their drift.","Most of them survived the first volley. They were each at the Naga’s level or grander. One arrow wore away limbs, heads, whole portions of their existences, but it was not enough.","Noah drew again!","\"I...can do this infinitely ,\" he said. \" My Dream has no far wall. It does not tire. It does not need to rest between one arrow and the next. So why should I not? Why walk up to each of them and trade blows, when I can stand here and draw?\"","Another arrow formed, blazing, gigaparsecs long.","\"I do not need to follow the common sense of anything else. I can do what I see fit!\"","BOOM!","The third volley landed, and the first of them died.","The titan of hail went first, its dreaming half worn away to the last grain. Then a thing like a frozen jellyfish the size of a sea, far to the south, aged into a cloud of white dust. Then a pair of frost wyrms coiled around a floating island, both of them eroding to bone and then to nothing in the same flash. One after another, across the whole Floor, bright points on Ruination’s lattice went out and did not come back.","And the spoils came.","|A Guard has been granted death. Spoils: Lesser Kryos x10. Memories of a Guard.|","Then again, and again, faster than the prompts could keep up with, until Ruination simply began to tally.","| Guards granted death: 11. Lesser Kryos received: 110.|","Noah fused as they came, without stopping his drawing arm. Four Lesser Kryos pressed together at his hip into a genuine Kryos, then the next four, the fusing happening in the back of his existence while the front of it went on loosing arrows.","Every Kryos he made, he sent away, down into THE Infiniverse, into the dreams of his people, wherever someone he held dear was sleeping.","The Tide answered each gift, and he ate every Quintessential ECG the moment it arrived. Each one spread through the whole of him, and every arrow after it came off the string a little larger and a little more certain!","| Guards granted death: 24. Lesser Kryos received: 240. Kryos fused and given: 60.|","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing notes that gifts given to enemies now considered weaker than you carry less weight than gifts given with thought. Its returns have diminished accordingly.|","| Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins integrated this battle: 41.|","...!","Diminished due to weakness? Okay!","The Guards that could still fight were fighting back now. Storms of frost came howling at him from a dozen directions. A spear of black ice the length of a Dimension. A wave of cold that froze the air solid for a thousand miles. They broke against his outline, or dreamed away into haze before they arrived, or landed on him and were kept by THE One Foundation, and every ton of that pressure went straight into the limbs of the bow and came back out behind the next arrow.","Nothing they threw slowed his drawing arm.","| Guards granted death: 38. Lesser Kryos received: 380. Kryos fused and given: 95.|","|Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins integrated this battle: 64. Total integrated: 130.|","|THE Osmontian Culmination. Present saturation: 29%.|","...!","Thirty-eight!","Seventeen bright points remained on the lattice, all of them worn and cracked and aged, several of them fleeing across the Floor as fast as their crumbling bodies could carry them. Following them would be easy. So would drawing until there were none.","He kept drawing!","But he was not looking at them.","His eyes had left the Guards some time ago. Every arrow found its target through Ruination’s lattice and his own Dreams, and he let them. His gaze was fixed somewhere else entirely.","North.","Where the blue rift split the dark, and the colossal thing lay coiled around its mouth.","It had not moved. Not once, through three volleys and thirty-eight deaths. It lay where it had always lain, the halo of stilled snow hanging over its head, its shape still too vast and too strange to resolve. Every arrow he loosed had aged the dark around it, and the dark around it had not aged at all.","It was buzzing!","He could feel it from here, a low vibration running through the frozen dark and into his quarks. Its half-present aura of Immensity was flickering fastr now, there and gone and there, as though something inside it were waking, or deciding.","Fifty-five Guards, and none of them had ever truly been his enemy. They were spoils. They were steps.","This was the only real enemy on the Basal Floor.","And even from here, with his existence packed and climbing and a bow in his hands that could empty a whole Floor of monsters, it was utterly suffocating!"]},{"number":5815,"title":"Chapter 5815: Chapter 5814: Poisonous!","paragraphs":["<Sir Moriarty>","Moriarty’s Elsedimension Mountain looked like a study that had kept growing for an Age and never once been tidied, and it could always look different.","Currently...","Shelves climbed its hollow heart in spirals, bowed under books and bones and jars of things that still twitched. Instruments of brass and glass hung from chanes overhead, some of them measuring, some of them only remembering how. Down the center of the great chamber ran a long stone table where specimens lay in careful rows, labeled in his small precise hand, and at the far end of it, under a sheet, lay the half-dissected remains of an Immense One he had been studying for a while.","The snow had reached even here. It drifted down from somewhere high in the dark and settled on the shelves, and Moriarty had given up brushing it off his books.","Poona sat cross-legged on his table, between a jar of preserved eyes and a tray of his pastries, eating the pastries!","\"You could at least pretend to have come about the Council, \" Moriarty said, without looking up from his notes.","\"I did come about the Council.\" She licked sugar off a finger. \"I just also came about the pastries.\"","He adjusted his spectacles. There was a great deal to think about before the Legacy gathered. The Convocation had ended in a severing and a voice. The Counting pressed on every Root under Lucy’s roof. And three of the thrones had stopped speaking to him in the corridors.","At this time...","The air in the chamber changed!","It grew warm, and green, and smelled suddenly of spring. Moriarty lifted his head. Poona stopped chewing.","THE Verdant Regard stepped into the study!","No door opened for her. She simply arrived, a tall figure of soft green light with a gaze like new leaves, and the snow nearest her turned to petals and fell. Her head inclined to Moriarty with perfect courtesy, and to Poona with slightly less.","Then she raised her Immensity!","It rose out of her in a slow green tide and poured up the hollow of the mountain, and closed over the whole of it like a dome. Moriarty felt it seal. Every thread of perception that ran in or out of his Elsedimension was quietly shut. Nobody outside could see in now, or hear, or sense so much as a breath. He had never once, in all the ages he had known her, seen her ask for that kind of privacy!","Poona set down her pastry!","\"Is this Osmont truly one of the three?\" THE Verdant Regard said.","Her voice was gentle, and tired, and very reasonable.","\" Will we risk our Immensity and rally around him? Because I have watched him, and it does not seem he will do anything different from any of the others. He does not show any brilliance.\"","Moriarty frowned!","He took off his spectacles and set them on the table beside his notes. Poona went very still.","\" What exactly is your point? \" he said. \" We are to gather as a Legacy in a little while to decide a direction on all of this. So why say it now, here, under a dome where no one else can hear?\"","THE Verdant Regard did not answer at once.","She walked slowly along the length of his table, past the specimens and the jars, trailing one green finger along the stone. Where she touched, small shoots came up through the snow.","\"I have begun to think differently ,\" she said. \" About a great many things. About the three, and the door, and who should and could be the one to open it. About this Legacy, and what Lucy built it for, and whether what she built it for still matters when the snow is this deep.\"","She stopped at the end of the table, by the sheeted corpse.","\"I think our weavings may no longer be aligned, Moriarty.\"","\"That is a strange thing to come and tell me.\"","\"It is.\" She turned to face him, and her gaze was sad and green and very old. \"I did it only as an assurance, you understand. I never wanted to use it. I hoped I never would.\"","She tilted her head.","\" But do you remember all that tea we drank together, over the years?\"","...!","Moriarty remembered!","He remembered it all at once, as a scholar remembers the one line in a text he read a thousand times without seeing. Ages of afternons. Her domain, spring and warm, and a cup in his hand that always tasted faintly of green. He had liked it. He had asked her once what was in it, and she had smiled and told him it was only leaves.","She waved her hand!","Green light came out of him!","It leaked from his skin, from the corners of his eyes, from under the seams of his tentacles, a poisonous glowing green that had been growing inside him quietly for longer than he could count. Rather than burning, it bloomed, spreading through his existence along every path the tea had ever taken, and wherever it bloomed, his Immensity went soft and slow and far away.","Moriarty stumbled!","He caught himself against his own table, knocking a jar of eyes to the floor, and the glass shattered, and he stared at his tentacles where green light was pouring out.For once in his long existence, he had nothing at all to say.","Poona’s face changed!","The cheer went out of it entirely. There was no shout and no laugh. Poona slid off the table, and as her feet touched the floor, her shape let go of itself. Her body went soft, translucent, and swelled outward into a vast gleaming mass of living slime, shimmering with every color at once, filling half the study and rising toward the dome of green light, and inside it, turning slowly, her one enormous bright eye fixed on THE Verdant Regard without a trace of warmth.","Then the whole mountain buzzed!","It shook from its roots to its peak, every shelf rattling, every instrument swinging on its chain. The green dome overhead flickered, not breaking, but opening, deliberately, in one place, to let something in.","The air above the long stone table split open like an eyelid!","A vast dark eye looked out of it. Sleepless. Patient. Burning with an attention that had never once blinked. It looked at Moriarty, stumbling and bleeding green light against his own table, and at Poona, vast and gleaming and silent. Last of all, it looked at THE Verdant Regard, standing at the end of the table beside the corpse, and something in it seemed almost fond.","|THE SLEEPLESS FIEND regards you.|","|\"It is a time for revolution, old friend Moriarty.\"|","...!","Outside the dome, far below on the snow-covered floor of the Legacy, the purple-gold rivers had begun to run faster. Conduits hummed in a pitch no Keeper had ever heard. On a dozen mountains at once, figures that did not belong to THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity were stepping out of the blizzard, and the snow around them was falling crimson gold.","The incursion had begun!","---","<THE Creature>","Anaximander sat on nothing.","There was no floor in the undefinition where their home had once been, only the slow obsidian foam and the snow drifting through it, but Anaximander had found a place to sit anyway. He had a book open on his knee. Where the book had come from, THE Creature did not know.","THE Creature watched him.","He had been watching him for some time. Since Anaximander had agreed to take his weavings from the future, since those weavings had come pouring back into the scholar all at once, the friend beside him had changed. His eyes were older. His hands turned the pages more slowly. And there was something in him now that THE Creature could sense clearly, sitting at the very center of his existence.","A Root!","That was what it looked like, to THE Creature’s senses. The shape of it was plain. A Root of Immensity, whole and bright, rooted in the middle of the man as surely as the fractured one was rooted in THE Creature’s own chest.","And yet Anaximander carried no authority at all, not a single thread of it, the same as always. There was no power coming off him, no weight, no pressure. A Root should hum. It should press outward on the existence around it. This one did nothing.","THE Creature looked closer, and understood.","It was no Root that Anaximander had grown. It was a hollow, exactly the shape of a Root, and existence itself had leaned in and filled it. The foam around the scholar curved toward that hollow. The snow drifting past him bent its fall very slightly inward. Existence had looked at the man, and at the space in him where a Root would go, and simply agreed that one was there.","\" You’re staring. \" Anaximander said, without looking up from his book.","\"I am, \" THE Creature said.","\" Between the two of us, I am certainly not the bigger monster though?\"","\"...\"","THE Creature said nothing. He went on looking at the hollow full of agreement in his friend’s chest, and felt, faintly, something he did not often feel.","Marvel!","Then, in the next moment, he frowned as existence distorted!","Rather than tearing, it bent all at once, the obsidian foam around them warping inward toward a single point in the undefinition, as though something very heavy had just set its foot down on a sheet of cloth. The snow stopped falling. It hung in the air, every flake of it, and trembled.","Anaximander closed his book.","A figure stepped out of the bend!","He was tall and pale, his long hair pale gold shading into white, his eyes gold and bright and very calm. He wore a long dark coat that did not move in any wind. And he was shining, faintly, from the inside, pale gold light seeping out through his skin as though he had eaten something enormous not long ago and was still digesting it.","THE Creature knew him as those eyes were unforgettable!","Everyone from their home knew him. He was the reason there was no home. He had taken their Observable Existence and left nothing behind but this foam.","\" Hello again ,\" said THE Sealed One.","His voice was warm, and courteous, and interested, the voice of a scholar greeting another scholar at a lecture.","\"It has been quite some time. And yet, not.\" He tilted his head, taking in the foam, the hanging snow, the two of them. \"I am sorry to say that I come this time bearing death.\"","...!","THE Creature and Anaximander moved closer together!","Neither of them decided to. They simply did. Anaximander rose off his seat of nothing and drifted to THE Creature’s side, and THE Creature’s white and obsidian flames rose around both of them, and their faces were grave.","THE Sealed One walked forward, unhurried, and the pressure of him arrived!","It came down on the undefinition like a sky falling. It was not Immensity. THE Creature could feel that it was not; there was no door behind it, no completion, no finished shape. But it was close. It was so close that the difference barely mattered, a weight that pressed on the foam and the snow and on THE Creature’s fractured Root until the crack across his chest began, very faintly, to glow.","\" People fear death ,\" THE Sealed One said, \" because they think it means being erased. They think the lantern goes out and the room stays cold and empty forever. But that is not what dying is.\"","He stopped a little way off, and his gold eyes rested on THE Creature.","\" Death is just an open hand tipping over a bowl, so something better can drink.\"","The snow trembled in the air between them.","\" Sometimes, death is actually a kindness. When an old tree rots in the brush, it does not curse the dirt. It feeds the ground, so a taller trunk can climb toward the sun. Nothing ever truly vanishes in existence. The weight stays. The heat and the stubborn marrow you carried simply get poured into someone else’s blood.\" His voice softened.","\" In a strange way, you do not really stop walking. You just live on through me.\"","THE Creature did not answer.","\"And look, \" THE Sealed One went on, almost apologetic. \" I do not want to be unfair. You can see the shapes standing behind my shoulder. I am not alone. I have never been alone.\"","Behind him, the undefinition shifted!","Shapes rose out of the foam at his back, vast and hazy, their Dimensionality flowing so deep that THE Creature could not see them clearly at all. Only the auras came through, pressing out from behind THE Sealed One like five suns rising behind a single hill. Five of them. Each one heavy with the unmistakable, finished weight of true Immensity!","Five Immense Ones, standing in the foam where a home had been.","\" But I never liked ganging up on a man,\" THE Sealed One said. \" It leaves a bitter taste in my mouth, like chewing on burnt gristle. So those behind me will not move. They will not lift a finger. They will not take a single step toward you.\"","He smiled.","\" They are just here to watch the wood get split. It is only you and me.\"","...!","Five Immense Ones watching. A being very nearly Immense himself walking forward. And THE Creature with a fractured Root and a friend who carried no authority at all.","It was catastrophic!","THE Sealed One’s gold eyes drifted down to THE Creature’s chest, to the crack glowing faintly there, and to what lay inside it.","\" You really should be more careful ,\" he said, \" and not hang about outside existence with a Root that bright.\"","His eyes lit with open, delighted curiosity. \" A Root of Existence? Man. That is an anomaly worth exploring.\"","...!","THE Creature looked at him.","He looked at the pale shining figure, and at the five suns rising behind it, and at the foam that had once been everything he came from. He felt the weight of all of it pressing down on him, on his fractured Root, on his friend at his side.","And he began to buzz!","It started low, deep in his vast body, a vibration running up out of the undefinition and into him. His white and obsidian flames rose higher. The colorless Provenance around him began to simmer and churn. The crack across his chest blazed, the fractured Root inside it flickering and flaring, and THE Creature stood up straighter under the weight of five Immense Ones and a devourer, and did not bend!","\" Existence ,\" THE Creature said, \" is fearless.\"","The foam around him shook.","\" Existence perseveres.\"","His flames roared up into the dark, and the hanging snow scattered.","\"I simply have to... persevere.\"","...!","THE Sealed One watched THE Creature blaze, and his smile softened into something that looked almost like respect.","\"You are a grand being ,\" he said . \"I mean that. There are very few things in existence that would stand straighter under this. \"","He glanced back at the five suns rising behind him, then returned his gold eyes to THE Creature. \" But I am afraid it is the end of the line this time. Even Osmont will be, or should already be, very preoccupied right now.\"","THE Creature’s flames did not waver. But something behind his eyes went very still at that name!","\"In existence, there are some who believe themselves invincible no matter what, \" THE Sealed One went on. \" Let us put that to the test for you today .\"","He rolled his shoulders, loosely, like a man about to lift something heavy. \" Will you somehow survive standing before me?\"","He took one step forward!","\" You never know ,\" said a voice. \" Crazy myths and legends get written all the time.\"","...!","It was a lazy voice. Unhurried, faintly amused, as if its owner had been leaning against a wall somewhere listening to all of this for a while and had finally gotten bored enough to join in.","THE Sealed One stopped. And his smile, instead of fading, widened!","He turned.","Something was descending through the undefinition above them. Ink came first, rivers of it, black and glittering, pouring down out of the dark and curling through the obsidian foam without spilling a drop. Then pages, thousnds of them, drifting down around the ink like white leaves. And in the middle of it all, sitting on the air with one leg crossed over the other, came a woman!","She was tall and slender, with long dark hair pinned up carelessly by a single pen driven through the knot. Her robes were the pale white of good paper and hung loose around her, and every inch of her exposed skin, her hands, her wrists, her throat, the side of her face, was covered in writing.","Fine, dense lines of script in her own neat hand, running and shifting slowly across her body as though they were still being written. Her eyes were dark, and when they moved, faint lines of text moved in them too.","Behind her, so faint it could barely be seen, something vast and patient stood among shelves that climbed out of sight. Only its brilliance showed. An immense, quiet glow of ink and parchment, watching over her shoulder, as a library watches over whoever sits reading in it.","THE MATRIARCH OF INK.","THE Writer of Mythos had arrived, and her name, THE Creature felt, written on the air behind her in letters of ink, was Calliope!","She came to a stop above THE Creature and Anaximander, a little to one side, and looked THE Sealed One up and down with open, unimpressed interest.","\"I’m taking a little detour ,\" Calliope said. \"It might be disastrous.\"","She shrugged. \" But I just can’t watch a myth come to an end, you know? It would be such a shame.\"","Her dark eyes narrowed, and the script on her skin quickened. \" And you seem to be a black hole where myths go to die.\"","...!","THE Sealed One laughed!","It was a bright, genuine, delighted laugh, and it rang out through the whole undefinition, and the five Immense suns behind him did not so much as flicker.","\" Quite the opposite, actually ,\" he said, still smiling . \"I will make all your myths live on across history. Your capabilities will be remembered. Every one of them, kept safe inside me for as long as I exist.\"","He spread his pale hands, almost welcoming. \" Now. Let us see who lives, and who dies.\"","HUUM!","Crimson brilliance erupted from him!","It tore out of his chest and his eyes and his outstretched hands, a light that was Infinity and was also somthing older, bound together and fused, pouring out of a source so far down inside him and so vast that THE Creature could not see the bottom of it.","It roared outward in every direction, through the foam and the snow and the pages drifting around Calliope, and wherever it touched, the color went out of everything else.","The obsidian foam turned red, and the falling snow with it. Rivers of ink, the white of Calliope’s robes, the white and obsidian of THE Creature’s own flames, all of it, painted crimson in an instant.","All of existence, as far as THE Creature could see, was red!"]},{"number":5816,"title":"Chapter 5816: Chapter 5815: A Big, Fat, Panda! I","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","The last seventeen Guards did not get far at all.","Noah ran them down across the Basal Floor one volley at a time, and one by one the bright points on Ruination’s lattice went out, until the lattice held nothing at all but the thing in the north. Their Lesser Kryos came to him in handfuls. He fused them as they came, four into one, and sent every Kryos away to his people until none were left to send.","Then he ate what the Tide gave back!","| All fifty-five Guards of THE Basal Floor have been granted death.|","|Lesser Kryos received: 550. Kryos Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins fused and given: 137. The two Lesser Kryos remaining have been given as well.|","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing has answered, though gifts weigh less due to power discrepancy.|","|Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins received and integrated since the first volley: 90. Total integrated: 156.|","|THE Osmontian Culmination. Present saturation: 34%.|","|Estimated Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins still required: 314.|","...!","Thirty-four percent!","He looked at his panel. It showed one in every line. The real numbers underneath flickered as they always did now, sliding between one and nine hundred and ninety-nine, telling him nothing he could hold.","But he did not need the numbers to know.","He felt it! His existence, which was his Root, which was all of him now, sat denser than it had ever sat. Packed tighter. Every Quintessential ECG had gone in and pressed the rest down, and the whole of him had settled into something so compact and so reinforced that he felt heavier standing still than he had once felt at full strength.","His diamond-jade skin had darkened a shade. The blue-gold tendrils beneath it had thickened into rivers. The crown of light above his brow burned steadier, its horns longer.","He wanted to know what that meant in practice. So he took a step.","One step, on the empty air, toward nothing in particular!","Dreams poured out of him!","Clouds of blue-gold rolled away from his foot in every direction, and behind the clouds came seas, soft shining tides of dream washing out across the frozen dark for a thousand miles. They broke over the nearest floating islands and the islands began to dream. The ice on them went hazy and slow.","The cold-filled trees on their slopes swayed as though a wind were moving through them, though there was no wind. A drifting corpse of one of the Guards, torn and aged by his arrows, rolled gently in the tide and settled, and its dead face softened into the expression of something sleeping.","Everything the dream touched, dreamed. He had not told it to. He had only moved!","So he tested the rest.","First the dreaming corpse: he chose to let its dream run forward, and it aged. Its torn edges softened, then crumbled, the whole ruined body sliding through a billion years of decay in the time it took him to breathe out, until it drifted away as dust. He turned to one of the dreaming trees and chose to run its dream backward.","The rime came off its branches. Its trunk narrowed, straightened, grew young, shrank, until a single frozen seedling hung in the air where a tree taller than a mountain had stood.","He let the seedling go, and looked at his hands.","Nothing needed to be spoken, or built, or aimed. His Provenance and his existence were one, and whatever that existence moved through fell into dream. And whatever fell into dream, he could run forward or backward, age or unmake or restore, as easily as turning a page.","It was very simple.","It was also terrifying!","Noah stretched. He rolled his shoulders, loosened his neck, flexed his hands, and felt the whole packed weight of himself move with him, and the dream-seas around him rippled with each small motion.","Then he turned to Ling.","\"I am going after the one in the north,\" he said. \" It should be Half-Immense.\"","Ling said nothing!","She hung in the air beside him with her arms crossed over her chest, looking at him, and then past him, north, toward the rift and the thing coiled around it. Her face gave nothing away. For a long moment she was completely silent.","Then she stretched. Arms high over her head, back arched, one thick powerful leg pulled up and held and released, then the other, the great muscles of her thighs flexing and loosening under the blue silk, and her whole body settled into that coiled, humming readiness he had seen before the Naga.","\"As long as I don’t die right away, \" she said. \" Let’s go, Big Boy.\"","...!","Noah took a deep breath.","A light of dreams rose around the two of them, blue and gold, closing over them like a curtain drawn around a bed.","And in the next instant, they were somewhere else!","—","The north of the Basal Floor was grand.","Everywhere else, the frozen islands floated free in the dark, turning slowly on their own. Here, they had stopped. Thousands of them lay jammed together in a vast ring, pressed edge against edge, ground and heaved and stacked into a single frozen plain that curved away around a hollow at its center.","The torn Dimensions that hung everywhere else had been pulled down here too, crushed into the ice of the plain and frozen in place, their broken seas and realms showing through the surface like things drowned under a lake. Pillars of rime rose from the plain in crooked rows. Some of them had shapes inside them. Figures. Beasts. Things that had come this way before and stopped.","At the center of the ring, the blue rift split the dark from top to bottom.","And coiled around the rift’s mouth, the thing in the north.","This close, its shape finally resolved!","It was a...panda!","A panda the size of a mountain range, and nothing about that was funny. It sat hunched at the mouth of the rift with its great round back to the dark, its fur black and white and gone hard with ages of frost, every hair of it a spine of ice. Where the white fur should have been, the ice was clear, and through it Noah could see the bones of the thing, massive and ancient and glazed in rime. Where the black fur should have been, the ice was dark as a starless sky and seemed to go down forever.","Wings rose from its shoulders. Vast, jagged, made of frost, like panes of frozen glass shattered and set back together by a hand that did not care how the pieces fit. They hung in tatters behind it, and wind that was not wind moved through them with a sound like a very old choir.","Chains of broken rime hung from its neck and its thick forearms, snapped links trailing down onto the plain, as though it had been bound here once and had simply grown too large for the binding. A mantle of frozen banners draped over its shoulders beneath the wings, stiff and cracked, each banner bearing a sigil too eroded to read. And in one enormous paw, resting across its knees, it held a great club carved from the spire of a Dimension, the stone of it still carved with the windows of the city that had once stood on it.","Over its head hung the halo of stilled snow.","Its face was the face of a panda, round, with the dark rings around its eyes. But the eyes within those rings were pale, and old, and cold beyond anything Noah had met on this Floor. Its jaw moved slowly. It was chewing on somethng. A long frozen stalk of something white that Noah realized, after a moment, was a bone.","His sight opened it, and gave him almost nothing.","| Empowered Hollow Night Lifeform.|","|VERITAS: ?????. PROVENANCE: ?????. POTENTIA: ?????. PONDUS: ?????.|","|Immensity: halfway.|","...!","Halfway!","The aura came off it and went back into it, there and gone and there, the finished weight of Immensity pressing down on the whole frozen plain and then lifting and then pressing again. Every time it pressed, the rime pillars groaned. Every time it lifted, the air felt strangely empty.","The panda looked at him!","No rising, no spreading of wings, no lifting of the club. The panda simply turned its great round head, slowly, still chewing on its bone, and fixed its pale ringed eyes on the small figure hanging in the air at the edge of its plain.","There was no anger in that look. There was nothing in it but a deep and total boredom, the look of something vast glancing down at a bug on the arm of its chair and deciding, without much interest, whether it was worth the effort of lifting a hand.","Noah looked back at it.","He hung in the frozen air above its plain, bare-chested, dark diamond-jade, tendrils of blue-gold burning beneath his skin and a jagged crown of light above his brow. The dream-seas he had raised were still rolling off him in slow shining tides, lapping at the edge of the frozen ring. His eyes were very calm.","He did not look away.","Neither did it!"]},{"number":5817,"title":"Chapter 5817: Chapter 5816: A Big, Fat, Panda! II","paragraphs":["The panda only looked at him, and its gaze came down on Noah like a hand the size of a sky!","It struck his existence, all of it at once, and pressed him back hard enough that the dream-seas rolling off him caved in on themselves and the air behind him cracked. He slid backward across the frozen dark a full mile before he stopped himself, his diamond-jade skin groaning, his crown of light flickering at its tips.","One look, and it was still chewing!","| Designation: THE Warden Who Does Not Rise.|","|Empowered Hollow Night Lifeform. Keeper of the Northern Descent.|","|VERITAS: ?????. PROVENANCE: ?????. POTENTIA: ?????. PONDUS: ?????.|","|Immensity: halfway.|","The Warden Who Does Not Rise. Noah turned the name over. It had sat here since before anyone thought to write a name down. In every branch he could see where he turned back, it went on sitting here, forever, chewing its bone.","He left those branches where they lay.","| Leave, young thing.|","The voice was deep and slow and utterly unbothered, and it came from everywhere on the frozen plain at once.","| You cannot even touch me, much less get past me. And even if you did, those grander than me lie behind here.|","|This is not playtime.|","Noah rolled his neck.","Then he walked forward!","One step, and the dream-seas poured out of him again, a thousand miles of blue-gold tide rolling across the jammed islands and the rime pillars and the drowned Dimensions under the ice. Everything it touched began to dream. The pillars went soft at their edges, and the frozen figures inside them stirred in their sleep.","Then the tide reached the Warden, and broke!","The seas washed up against its great hunched body and slid away on either side, undreaming, parting around it like water around a stone that had sat in its riverbed since the river was born. Half of it was Immense, and that half stayed as solid as bedrock.","So Noah tried the other half.","He crossed the last distance in a single stride and hit it. Everything he was, every packed quark and every Quintessential ECG he had eaten, the whole dense weight of the Fiend in him, driven into the Warden’s shoulder through one closed fist!","HUUM!","The shoulder held as still as a mountain!","The Warden turned its head, slowly, and looked at the fist resting against its fur. Then it lifted the club.","It was a slow motoin, lazy and certain. The tower of Dimensions came around in a slow, bored arc, and Noah saw it coming, and it caught him anyway.","It hit him!","BOOM!","The blow stopped him entirely. His existence came apart under it so completely that nothing was left to break, and he died on the frozen plain before the club had finished its swing.","| Your Dream is Infinite. Even death will not stop it.|","Golden clouds spat him back out a mile away.","He came back already dreaming the death through, slowly, from inside. The angle of the club. Its weight and Immensity. The exact moment it found him. By the time his feet touched the ice he had learned it, and it could never kill him that way again.","The Warden watched him get up. It went back to chewing.","| You do not know Immensity.|","Noah dusted the frost off his shoulder, and kept his answer to himself. He was thinking.","Half-Immense. That was the whole puzzle, and he had been looking at it wrong. He had been trying to hurt the half that was Immense. That half stood beyond the reach of everything he currently was. But the aura kept flickering. There and gone and there. And in the moments when it was gone, the Warden was only a Hollow Night Lifeform.","A very large, very fat, very old one, carrying something Immense in its chest and the borrowed cold of the Long Night in every hair of its fur.","Borrowed.","\" Ruination ,\" he said.","| Already done, Master. The flicker is not random. It follows a rhythm. I am marking every window where the Immense half withdraws. The next opens in four heartbeats.|","Noah went forward again!","The Warden swung. He had learned the club; it passed a hand’s width from his face. It swung again, low, a new angle, and killed him. He came back. It swung a third way and killed him again. He came back, and back, each death something he would never die to twice, and every time he returned the Warden had fewer ways left to kill him.","Four heartbeats. Three. Two.","The aura went out!","Noah laid his palm on the Warden’s chest and turned its cold!","THE Kneeling Frost poured into it, and the borrowed winter packed into the Warden’s fur turned inward, freezing from the inside out, spines of ice cracking and splintering across its whole flank. The Warden grunted. It was a small sound. It was the first sound it had made besides speech.","The aura came back, and flung him away across the plain.","He landed on his feet, unhurt and interested!","| Next window in six heartbeats, Master.|","He took it. And the next. The Bow of the Ending Epoch came into his hand between windows, and he aimed its arrows past the Warden, at everything it was attached to: the broken chains trailing from its neck, the mantle of frozen banners on its shoulders, the rime pillars ringing its plain. All of them were borrowed from the Night, and all of them could age. They aged to dust under his arrows, and every link and banner and pillar that crumbled was one more piece of the Warden’s winter gone.","On the ninth window, he dreamed its bone.","The frozen stalk it had been chewing since before he arrived went soft in its mouth, and aged, and crumbled into white powder between its teeth.","The Warden Who Does Not Rise stopped chewing.","...!","Then it rose!","Oh, it rose!","Mind you, this was a Half-Immense monstrosity!","It rose to its feet for the first time in more Ages than anything on the Basal Floor remembered, and the whole frozen plain groaned under it. Ice split for a hundred miles. Its shattered wings of frost spread wide behind it, vast and jagged, and the wind that moved through them was no longer an old choir. It was a roar. The halo of stilled snow above its head flared white, and everything under it stopped.","Time stopped. The dream-seas froze mid-wave. Noah’s own existence locked in place, pinned in a single instant, his thoughts sliding to a halt.","THE Sovereign of the Lived Hour drew that stillness into his Dreams, and a dreaming hour moved as he wished. He came loose. Slowly, then all at once, and he moved out from under the halo just as the Warden’s club came down where he had been and split the plain in half!","The Warden looked at him, and for the first time its eyes held attention!","| Dying is easy for a thing like you. A blow lands, your breath cuts out. The heart just quits. That part takes only an instant. It is over before you even have time to miss the warmth. It is the darkness that comes after which is not so easy. The dark has weight. In that quiet, there is no fire to borrow, no walls to lean on, and no one. You just sit there forever, alone with whatever small, cold thing you made of yourself. Do you fear that darkness? Is that why you try to come back?|","...!","Its voice had changed. It was still deep, still slow, but there was attention in it now. Weight. The aura stopped flickering. It held, half-Immense and steady, pressing down on the whole plain.","Noah didn’t reply as he looked at Ling, hanging at the edge of the frozen ring with her fists clenched and her thighs coiled, a breath away from throwing herself in.","\" Sit this one out, \" he told her.","She opened her mouth to argue. Then she looked at his face, and closed it, and stayed where she was.","Noah turned back to the Warden. He breathed in slow and deep, and let his Dream go wide.","To beat something even half Immense, he had to dream a grand dream.","He dreamed himself.","Once, at first. A second Noah stepped out of the blue-gold light at his side, diamond-jade and crowned, identical to him in every way. Then a third. Ten. A hundred, a thousand, stepping out of the dream-seas one after another, more and more, until they filled the frozen plain from edge to edge and kept going, out past the ring of jammed islands, out into the dark of the Basal Floor, versions of him stretching away in every direction without end.","| THE Waking Decree, THE Dream Without a Far Wall, and Dialetheic Infinity have been combined.|","|Formed: THE Endless Waking.|","|You dream yourself, and existence agrees that each dreamed self is you. Each one carries your full existence. Each one may die and return. Each one learns from every death any of them has ever died.|","|Their number has no end.|","...!","The Warden Who Does Not Rise looked at the infinite sea of him, and roared!","It fought. It fought with everything it had, club and wings and halo, the steady half-Immense aura crushing down on the whole plain. Its club took a thousand of him in a single swng. Its halo froze ten thousand in place, and its wings shredded whole ranks of him into golden dust.","Every one that died came back having learned.","And behind every one that fell, there were infinitely more!","They came at it from every direction at once! A million palms on its fur turned a million lines of borrowed cold against it. Arrows of dreamed decay poured into every flicker and seam. Its wings came off pane by frozen pane, and its club broke at the grip. Up its legs and its back and its shoulders they climbed, and every step they took dreamed another piece of it away!","HUUUM!","It fell!","The Warden Who Does Not Rise toppled backward onto its own frozen plain, and the whole Basal Floor shook with the impact, and the infinite versions of Noah stood back and let it lie there.","One of him walked forward.","He climbed onto its chest, where the black fur had gone dark as a starless sky, and lay down on it, as a man lies down on a warm hillside at the end of a long day. The Warden’s great ringed eyes looked up at him.","He looked at the Panda and said lightly...","\" Do not fear that endless darkness.\"","HUUM!","\"Rage.\"","WAA!","\"Rage.\"","BOOM!","Noah pressed his arms down into its chest!","They sank in. Through fur and ice and ancient bone, into the dark at the center of it, where its dream and its existence lived. He took hold of both. And pulled.","| THE Warden Who Does Not Rise has been granted death.|","|Taken: its Dream. Taken: its existence.|","|The Half-Immense core it carried is yours.|","...!","The Warden breathed out, once, long and slow, like something very old finally being allowed to sleep.","Around them, infinite versions of Noah Osmont stood across the frozen dark, and one by one, gently, they dreamed themselves away as the one plunged into the existence of a massive Panda trembled!","The Warden lay on its back across its frozen plain, and the whole of it was treasure.","Noah could feel that from where he stood on its chest. Every spine of frozen fur carried ages of the Long Night’s cold, packed dense. Every bone under the clear ice was old enough to have watched the Basal Floor fill with Guards one by one. Its broken wings still held the shapes of stopped moments in their panes. A corpse of a Half-Immense Lifeform was worth more than a hundred beings who merely carried Roots.","He knelt, and reached further inside it!","His arms sank through fur and ice and bone, down into the dark at the center of the great chest, and found what lay waiting there.","A singularity!","It hung in the dark of the Warden’s chest, and his sight could only take half of it. One half was there, plain, a point of pale blue light so dense it bent the frozen dark around it. The other half slid away from his perception every time he reached for it, present and absent at once, flickering at the edge of seeing exactly as the Warden’s aura had flickered while it lived.","Around it, thick as the walls of a fortress, coiled weavings of Immensity.","His hand closed toward the singularity and met them. They were solid as the door he had felt at the top of his own existence. His fingers pressed and met solid Immensity at every point.","And the weavings spoke, in the voice of the panda!","| You cannot grasp Immensity if you have no Immensity.|","...!","Noah stayed kneeling on the corpse’s chest with his hand pressed flat against the weavings, and looked at them for a while.","Then he smiled, very slightly.","\" Immensity ,\" he said.","His voice was calm.","\" Everyone reaches for it. I see them. Every being that ever climbed, climbing toward the same door, as though it were the only door there is. They build their histories on the way to it. Their dreams, their hopes, all their power, poured into one shape, because they were told that shape was the top of everything.\"","He pressed a little harder, and the weavings held. \"This one sat at the door for more Ages than I can count, and got halfway through, and stayed. That was all its Immensity ever gave it. A doorway to sit in.\"","He looked down at the half-seen singularity in the dark.","\"I reject it. All of it. Immensity is only one of the things they did. The key was never the door. The key is everything they lived on the way there. Their history. Their dreams. What they hoped for, sitting in the cold. That is the part that belongs to them. That is the part I can reach.\"","He let his Dream open!","Seas of it poured out of him and down into the Warden’s body. Blue-gold tides, boundless, flooding through the frozen fur and the clear ice and the ancient bones, filling every hollow of the great corpse until the whole of it glowed from inside like a lantern. The dream soaked into the Warden’s dead existence and went looking for what was still there.","It found the Warden’s dream!","Noah saw it. The whole of it, all at once, as the dream-seas carried it up to him.","\"It dreamed of rising, \" he said softly.","The corpse beneath him glowed brighter.","\" Ages at the mouth of that rift. Chained there, then too large for the chains, then too still to remember why it stayed. Guarding the way down for those grander than itself. And every Age of that watch, it dreamed of standing up and walking away, down into the dark, or out into the light, anywhere but here. It dreamed of rising for so long that the dream grew heavier than the rest of it.\" He breathed out. \" THE Vigil That Wished to Rise.\"","...!","Behind him, something began to form!","It gathered out of the blue-gold seas pouring off his shoulders, dream-stuff drawing together, taking shape. A panda. Vast, nearly the size of the Warden itself, made entirely of golden-blue light, its fur shimmering in slow drifting waves, its great round eyes ringed with gold instead of black. Wings spread from its shoulders, whole ones, unbroken, pane after pane of clear shining dream set together as neatly as the Warden’s had once been set by a careless hand. Its body was free of chains, mantle, and club alike.","It rose up behind Noah to its full height, standing tall on the frozen plain, and moved when he moved.","He lifted his hand. The dream-panda lifted its paw!","He reached forward, and it reached with him, its great shining paw sinking down past his arms into the Warden’s chest, down through the dark, to the coiled weavings of Immensity and the singularity inside them.","The weavings let it through!","They parted around the dream-panda’s paw as a mother’s arms open for her own child. It was the Warden’s dream. It was the accumulation of everything the Warden had lived and wanted across every Age of its watch. The Immensity recognized it, and gave way.","The golden paw closed around the singularity, and drew it out!","| THE Vigil That Wished to Rise has been dreamed into form.|","|The Dream of a Half-Immense Lifeform is the accumulation of its existence. What guards its Immensity recognizes its own Dream, and yields to it.|","|Loot obtained: THE Stillborn Singularity of THE Warden’s Immensity.|","|A singularity of Immensity, half-perceivable and half not, holding within it a failed Immensity: an ascent that reached the threshold and never passed through.|","|Its properties are sealed. They may be studied.|","...!","Noah took it from the dream-panda’s paw and held it tightly.","It was cold, and heavy past anything its size had a right to be, and it flickered in his grip, there and gone and there. He could feel the whole failed ascent inside it, an Immensity that had climbed halfway through the door and frozen on the threshold. A thing that almost was. He closed his fingers around it until the flicker steadied against his palm, and put it away, deep inside himself, where nothing could reach it but him.","Then he stood, and looked down at the corpse.","The dream-panda behind him lowered its head, and sank into him.","It poured back into his shoulders in a slow golden flood, and he felt it settle somewhere deep, kept, ready to be dreamed again. The Warden’s Dream was his now. Its body was another matter.","He looked it over as a collector looks over the finest piece he has ever found. The frozen fur, every spine of it packed with the Long Night’s cold. The clear ice over ancient bones. The broken wings still full of stopped moments. All of it, whole, the corpse of a being that had sat halfway to Immensity for longer than anything on this Floor could remember.","He could swallow it right now. He could feel his existence leaning toward it, hungry, eager to press every Age of that watch into his quarks.","He kept it whole instead.","Blue-gold dream closed over the great body in a slow tide, sealing it from fur to bone, until the Warden lay wrapped in a shell of shining dream on its frozen plain. Then the shell drew inward, smaller and smaller, and the whole vast corpse went with it, down into the depths of his Dream, where it settled beside the Stillborn Singularity. Kept. Untouched.","| Consumed: the Dream of THE Warden Who Does Not Rise. THE Vigil That Wished to Rise has been kept, and may be dreamed again at your will.|","|Stored within your Dream: the corpse of THE Warden Who Does Not Rise, a Half-Immense Lifeform.|","|Held: THE Stillborn Singularity of THE Warden’s Immensity.|","|THE reach of your Dream has expanded.|","...!","Noah stood on the frozen plain where a Half-Immense guardian had sat, alone now except for Ling watching wide-eyed at the edge of the ring and the blue rift splitting the dark before him.","A hundred deaths had brought him here. The rift behind the Warden opened downward into cold that pulled at every quark he owned, toward those grander than the Warden, waiting below.","He was hungry for them already. But first, he had to make proper use of the loot of the big, fat panda to ensure he obtained the grandest returns. Which meant giving it all away. The singularity of Immensity, and the whole Half-Immense corpse along with it, so that his Tide could give him back something even grander!","He wanted to see if that would be enough...to trigger an evolution!"]},{"number":5818,"title":"Chapter 5818: Chapter 5817: Glory! I","paragraphs":["Barbatos’s dream smelled of glorious death.","Noah stepped into it through the Dream Engine and found her where he always did, at the heart of a necropolis that went on forever. Tombs rose in endless terrraces under a violet sky, each one carved with names, and between them walked the dead she had raised. She sat on the steps of the tallest tomb with a book open across her knees and a thread of pale green necromancy spinning lazily between her fingers as it passed through dozens of dead Dimensions.","She looked up, saw him, and smiled.","He spared her the speech and opened his hand.","The corpse of THE Warden Who Does Not Rise came out of his Dream and settled onto the terraces of her necropolis. It filled the sky. Its frozen fur blotted out the violet light, its broken wings of stopped moments hung over whole districts of tombs, its great ringed face lay turned toward her, eyes closed, as though it had simply lain down among her dead to sleep.","Every skeleton in the necropolis stopped walking and looked at it!","Barbatos set down her book.","She asked him what it was. He told her: a Half-Immense guardian, dead, whole, carrying Ages of the Long Night’s cold in every spine of its fur. She asked him what he wanted her to do with it. He told her whatever she liked.","She walked up to it slowly and laid her palm flat against its frozen side.","\" Oh ,\" Barbatos said quietly. \" Oh, you gorgeous fucking thing!\"","She was talking to the corpse as he left her to it.","| Given: the corpse of THE Warden Who Does Not Rise, a Half-Immense Lifeform, to Barbatos.|","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing has noted your giving. A gift of this weight, given with thought to one you hold dear, will be answered.|","...!","He moved on!","—","Emotive’s dream was exactly as he had left it: THE Earliest Folds reimagined in a madwoman’s hands, woven towers of THE Loom arching overhead, and statues of him everywhere, each one carved with the devotion of someone who had never once considered being ashamed of it.","She saw him and came flying. He caught her before she could wrap herself around his feet this time.","While she clung to his chest, laughing, he thought about why he had come to her with this.","He had many people with potential. His Son. Seo-yeon. Thalia with her Root of genome alteration. Barbatos, just now, with a Half-Immense corpse to raise. Every one of them could grow into something grand.","But Emotive’s potential was the one that frightened him a little!","Her Root was Emotion, and it was Physical. Every feeling she held, she carried in her body as mass, and force, and weight. The more she felt, the heavier and stronger she became.","That alone would have been enough. It was only the beginning.","Every lifeform in existence did what it did because of how it felt. Pride built empires. Fear toppled them. Love had moved him across more domains than he could count. Emotion was the engine underneath every other engine, and Emotive’s Root was built out of that engine directly.","And emotion was always one’s own. It came from inside, every time! The Long Night froze whatever a being had taken from somewhere else, and it could find nothing in a feeling to freeze. Under the Counting, under the Sealed Door, under a winter that choked every borrowed power in existence, her Root would keep generating, because a heart that feels needs nothing from anyone.","Then there were the Seven Sins and their Virtues. She had refined them in her dream to heights that had alarmed him, stacked and packed and volatile, storm upon storm of Ego. Her Root had simply swallowed all of it and turned it into weight.","And last, the thing only she had. The link. She was tied to his emotions in an unfathomable way. Every feeling that moved through him reached her too. As he grew, she grew. As he climbed, some part of her climbed with him.","A Root that fed on the one thing in existence that could never run dry, fed further by him.","Yes. She was the one!","He set her down in front of him, and let his Dream open.","Behind him, the golden-blue panda rose!","THE Vigil That Wished to Rise gathered out of his Dream, vast and shining, its gold-ringed eyes calm, its whole unbroken wings spread wide over the woven towers. Emotive’s manic eyes went round and bright as she looked up at it. The dream-panda reached into the depths of Noah’s Dream with one great paw, and drew out THE Stillborn Singularity of THE Warden’s Immensity, half-perceivable and flickering, and lowered it gently into Emotive’s open hands.","She held it, and her hair burned in every color at once!","\" For me? \" she whispered.","\" For you.\"","She stared at it, then at him, and her eyes blazed with a love so total it was very nearly frightening. Instead of asking what it was, she held it against her chest, over her Root, and he watched her existence lean toward it.","| Given: THE Stillborn Singularity of THE Warden’s Immensity, to Emotive.|","|Given this hour: a Half-Immense corpse and a singularity of failed Immensity, to two you hold dear, with thought.|","|THE Tide That Owes Nothing has answered.|","HUUM!","At this time, Emotive’s figure also began to shine as an utterly euphoric blast of emotions erupted from her!","And...","| THE Tide has been made euphoric with its brilliance. The quality of your return has further increased.|","...!","The dream around them shuddered!","| Returned, as dreamed:|","|Loot I: the corpse of an Immense One. Whole. Its Immensity settled within it, unscattered.|","|Loot II: an Immense Ergosphere. A sphere of turning Immensity, holding within it Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins. Number: unknown.|","...!","They came out of the Tide into Emotive’s dream, and the dream strained under them at once!","The corpse came first! It hung in the sky above the woven towers, and it was vaster than the Warden had been, vaster than anything Noah had yet seen lying still. A figure like a colossal robed sovereign, its face serene and sealed, its hands crossed over its chest, a crown of pale fire still resting on its brow long after the fire had stopped burning.","Its Immensity had stayed whole through death. It sat inside the body, whole and settled and heavy, and the weight of it pressed down on the dream until the statues of Noah began to crack at their bases!","Oh!","Oh!!!","Then the Ergosphere!","It bloomed beside the corpse, a sphere of Immensity turning around a dark core, and the turning never slowed. Currents of pale gold light swept around it in bnds, faster at its equator, slower at its poles, dragging the dream-air around with them.","Inside, glimpsed through the turning bands, lay shapes. Many shapes. Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins, dozens, hundreds, more, suspended in the dark at the center, and every time Noah tried to count them, the turning carried the count away.","...!","Emotive’s dream began to come apart!","The woven towers of THE Loom groaned and bent. Cracks raced across the sky. The statues of Noah toppled one after another, and the ground of THE Earliest Folds buckled under the weight of two things that had never been made to sit inside someone’s dream!","Noah moved at once!","He wrapped his Dream around the corpse and the Ergosphere together, sealed them in blue-gold, and pulled. The whole enormous weight of both came away out of Emotive’s dream in a single rush and went down, through him, through the Dream Engine, into THE Existential Root Domain, where there was room enough to hold them.","Emotive’s dream steadied. The cracks in the sky closed!","---","In THE Existential Root Domain, one part of Noah stood before a dead Immense One and a turning sphere, and looked.","The corpse lay across the blue-gold hills like a fallen range of mountains, robed and crowned, its hands crossed over its chest. Its Immensity sat inside it whole, and the weight of that pressed a shallow valley into the Domain’s soil around it. Beside it, the Immense Ergosphere turned and turned.","He was about to grasp them when his gaze changed.","Another part of him had felt something!"]},{"number":5819,"title":"Chapter 5819: Chapter 5818: Glory! II","paragraphs":["Far away, in the Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity, inside a cavern of purple torches on a lone dark mountain, a sliver of Noah still sat cross-legged on a mat. He had sent the a part of himself and all of Ling down into THE Undersnow.","And now that part felt the sky come down.","Auras of Immensity pressed on the mountain from above. Several of them, heavy and foreign and moving, bearing down through the blizzard toward the Thinker’s coat of burning light. The purple torches along the cavern walls leaned sideways in their brackets as though a great wind were blowing through the stone! The cavern floor hummed.","Noah looked across at the only other being in the cavern.","THE THINKER AT THE END OF EXISTENCE sat on his prayer mat, vast and kneeling, the frost-packed gash still leaking faint threads of Immensity down his back. His great beads clicked, one by one. His pale, pupil-less eyes lifted toward the cavern ceiling and moved slowly around it, as though he could see straight through the stone to the sky beyond.","|\" Adversity is always grand, and always relentless.\"|","His voice was calm and deep and faintly interested, the voice of a scholar noting that it had begun to rain.","|\" Waves of Immensity are crashing into THE Legacy of THE Acharya. It is rare for Legacies to attack one another. But in times like these, anything is possible.\"|","The beads clicked. |\"I have had a long time to think. And I believe I can guess what their target is, from where most of the attacking force has gathered now.\"|","Noah’s gaze sharpened.","\" And where would that be?\"","The Thinker smiled. The fierce line of his mouth widened, very slightly, beneath the weeping eyes.","|\" Why, here, of course. Toward this mountain.\"| A slow rumble of breath. | \"Which leads me to believe that their target, among other things, is you.\"|","The torches guttered. Somewhere far above, something heavy settled against the Thinker’s coat of Immensity, and the whole mountain shivered.","|\" Have you made progress in THE Undersnow? Or in yourself?\" | The Thinker tilted his great head. |\"I ask because I would rather you did not worry about this end too much.\"|","\"I made some progress ,\" Noah said. \" And I will make more.\"","He looked up at the humming ceiling. \" But why should I not worry?\"","|\"THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity is extremely old. \"|","The Thinker’s voice held no hurry at all. |\"We may have poisonous snakes among us. That is the only way anyone could have gotten in. But we are still grand. Lucy built this, after all. And Lucy is grand.\"|","His beads went still.","|\" We have some time, for now. Let us see how things unfold.\"|","...!","Noah lifted his head.","He could feel existence trembling. Beyond the stone of the mountain, beyond the Thinker’s burning coat, beyond the blizzard, something enormous was happening to the whole Legacy at once. What truly was going on out there?","He sent his perception up through the mountain to look.","—","The sky over THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity was broken.","Cracks ran across it from horizon to horizon, jagged and white, and through them the blizzard poured in thicker than ever. Snow buried the Elsedimension Mountains to their shoulders. The purple-gold rivers on the Legacy’s floor ran fast and dark, churning, and the Existential Conduits rising from them hummed at a pitch that set one’s teeth on edge.","And through that broken sky moved the invaders!","To his perception they looked like suns. Brilliant golden spheres, dozens of them, each one an Immensity foreign to this place, sliding through the storm in slow, deliberate lines. Some circled the mountains of the Protectors, pinning them. Some hung over the Firmament Mountain, where the Plain of Accord lay buried under snow. And the greatest number of them, a slow gathering tide of gold, were drifting toward a single lone mountain wrapped in a coat of hazy purple Immensity.","Toward the Thinker. Toward him!","Crimson gold snow fell wherever they passed.","Then the sky went dark!","It happened all at once. Across the whole broken width of the Legacy’s sky, from every horizon, a shape bloomed out of the cracks, so vast that for a moment it read as the sky itself. Obsidian, veined with gold, spreading and spreading until it covered everything above the snow.","It was a visage!","An illusory face the size of the Legacy itself, hanging over all of it. Its great head was the head of an octopus, a vast swollen mantle of obsidian skin shot through with rivers of burning gold, rising up into the broken sky past sight. Below it, where a chin should have been, hung a beard of tentacles, thousands of them, each one longer than a mountain range, coiling and uncoiling slowly in the storm.","Its skin was ridged and scaled in places, ancient, crusted with growths like coral that had been gathering since before the first Legacy was raised. Behind its head, half-seen, dark shapes that might have been vast vestigial wings stirred in the dark between the cracks.","And its eyes!","Two of them, each larger than the Firmament Mountain, burning crimson. They were enraged. They looked down at the Legacy, and at every golden sphere moving through it, with a fury so old and so total that the blizzard itself faltered under their gaze.","Somewhere in all that vastness, very small against the obsidian brow, something glinted. A pair of round lenses, perched on nothing, catching the light.","The tentacles spread!","They fell from the visage’s face and unfurled across the entire Legacy, thousands of them reaching down through the snow, curling around mountains, draping across rivers, laying themselves over every Conduit and every peak from one horizon to the other. Where they touched, the air went still.","And every golden sphere in the Legacy stopped.","All of them, from the ones circling the Protectors’ mountains to the ones over the Firmament to the great gathering tide drifting toward the Thinker’s mountain. Every foreign Immensity froze in place amid the boundless snow, pinned where it hung, as the tentacles settled over the Legacy like a net over a pond.","The visage spoke!","| This is the motherfucking Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity.|","|You all seem to forget that, so let me remind you.|","|There are levels to this shit.|","|THERE! ARE! LEVELS!|","BOOM!","Obsidian gold brilliance raged down out of the broken sky!","It poured from the visage and from every tentacle at once, black and gold and blinding, flooding the whole Legacy from its highest peak to the bottom of its rivers. Snow burned away in the light of it. The cracks in the sky filled with it. And behind it, rising out of the obsidian and the gold, came Immensity.","Unfathomable Immensity!","Noah felt it land on the Legacy, and on the frozen golden spheres, and on the mountain where he sat, and on him. It was the weight of a being who had stood at the top of existence for longer than most of existence had existed. It was the weight of a scholar who had been poisoned in his own study, and was done being polite about it.","In the purple-lit cavern, THE Thinker at the End of Existence looked up at the trembling ceiling, and his fierce almost-smile widened.","|\" Ah ,\"| he said mildly. |\" There he is.\"|"]},{"number":5820,"title":"Chapter 5820: Chapter 5819: Glory! III","paragraphs":["The tentacles had barely settled over the Legacy when the Existential Conduits began to rise.","Noah watched it happen through the sliver of himself on the Thinker’s mountain. All across the Legacy, the vast pillars of flowing authority that climbed out of the purple-gold rivers tore loose from their beds and lifted. They rose higher, and higher, until they stood like the columns of some impossible hall, and then they moved, spreading apart, drawing lines across the whole snowbound expanse, pillar beside pillar beside pillar, until the Legacy was carved into separate domains, each one walled off from the others by rings of rising light!","Golden spheres of foreign Immensity found themselves caught inside those rings, cut off, each one alone in its own partition.","Then the mist came down!","It poured out of the obsidian visage in the sky, black and gold and billowing, boundless as the blizzard and far heavier, rushing down over every carved domain at once. Mountains vanished into it, then the rivers and the Conduit walls and the frozen golden spheres pinned inside them. Everything it touched became obscure, unseeable, lost in a churning dark shot through with veins of gold.","|If you didn’t know, you’re about to know.|","|Put some respect on her name.|","|Put some respect on THE Acharya!|","BOOM!","The mists closed over the whole Legacy!","Noah’s perception went into them and came back with nothing but chaos. Immensity colliding with Immensity somewhere in the obscurity. Domains shaking. Roars that could have been anything, or anyone. The weight of beings who had stood at the top of existence for longer than most of existence had existed, all of them at war at once, hidden behind a curtain of gold and black.","His expression grew heavy!","Among all these titans, he truly fell short of every one. They held Immensity. Every one of them, the invaders and the defenders and the monstrous visage spreading its tentacles across the sky. They had walked through the door long ago, before existence shut it, and whatever they were fighting over now, they were fighting over it from a height above him.","That height was closed to him forever. Existence had made sure of that.","Yet he had something they lacked! A future away from Immensity, glorious and unwritten, that existence had denied him the old road to and so forced him to find his own.","So.","He drew his gaze back down out of the storm, and closed his eyes on the prayer mat, and turned his whole attention to the part of him standing in THE Existential Root Domain.","—","The dead Immense One lay across the blue-gold hills, robed and crowned, its hands crossed over its chest, its settled Immensity pressing the soil down around it into a shallow valley. Beside it, the Immense Ergosphere turned and turned, gold light sweeping around its dark core.","Ruination stood a little behind him, her crimson beams resting quietly on the corpse, reading it, keeping every detail. THE Infiniverse stood beside her in her heavy coat of many colors, still and watchful. Both of them were silent. They had come to watch their Master, and they would watch.","Noah looked at the corpse, and at the Ergosphere, for a long while.","\"I generated both of you ,\" he said.","His voice was calm and far away, and the Domain seemed to lean in to hear it.","\" From my own weavings, and from what I found in existence. A Half-Immense guardian’s body. A singularity of failed Immensity. I gave them to people I love, and the Tide gave you back to me in their place. You exist because I gave.\" He looked at the dead sovereign’s serene face. \" Now I will swallow you, to see if it will all be enough.\"","...!","He opened his mouth.","Inside it lay blue-gold brilliance, endless, infinite, a light that went down and down without reaching any bottom, and at the heart of it, turning, countless points of perfect dark. Event horizons. Thousands of them. Millions. Every one of them a place where something could fall in and stay fallen.","He pulled!","The corpse moved!","It lifted off the blue-gold hills, slowly at first, the whole vast robed body of an Immense One rising from the vally it had pressed into the soil, and drifted toward him. The Ergosphere came with it, its bands of light stretching, smearing, its turning drawn out into long spirals as it fell toward his open mouth. Both of them gravitated to him as everything gravitates toward an event horizon, faster and faster, stretching as they came, the sovereign’s crown of pale fire drawing out into a long thread of light, the Ergosphere unwinding into ribbons of gold.","THE Infiniverse took a step back. Ruination’s beams flared.","The corpse reached him first, and went in!","It poured into the brilliance of his mouth in a long, stretched river of robe and flesh and crown, and fell into the countless event horizons, and his Infinite Dream took hold of it.","| Devouring: the corpse of an Immense One.|","His Dream broke it down, all of it, layer by layer, as a fire breaks down a log. The robes went first, woven of authority so old it had forgotten its own name. Then the flesh, dense beyond anything he had eaten, every cell of it saturated with settled Immensity. Then the bones, then the crown, then the serene sealed face. His Dream took each piece apart, refined it to its purest essence, and pressed that essence down into him.","His body shook!","The diamond-jade of his skin darkened, and darkened again, until it was nearly black, the tendrils of blue-gold beneath it blazing so bright they lit the Domain’s hills. His crown of light flared. His muscles locked and swelled and locked again as the Immensity of a dead sovereign packed itself into every quark of him.","| Records of an Immense One acquired. Its name has worn away. Its memories have been kept.|","|Fragment acquired: Settled Bearing. The calm of a being that stood at the top of existence has been absorbed into THE One Foundation.|","|Integrated value: equivalent to 404 Quintessential Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins.|","|THE Osmontian Culmination. Present saturation: 72%.|","...!","Seventy-two percent!","The Ergosphere came next!","It fell into his mouth in long gold ribbons, and as its turning broke apart inside his Dream, the thing it had been hiding finally held still long enough to be counted.","| The Immense Ergosphere has been opened.|","|Contained: Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins x333.|","...!","Three hundred and thirty-three!","They poured out of the broken Ergosphere into his Dream like a river of stars, every one of them a genuine Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin, the true thing that Lesser Kryos were only a quarter of, and his Infinite Dream took them in one after another after another. Each one went down into him and broke apart and filled him. He could feel the space inside his existence closing, every hollow packing tight, every last gap between his quarks filling with the essense of Immensity that would stay unborn.","|Devouring: Existential Chorionic Gonadotropins.|","|Present saturation: 79%.|","|81%.|","|90%.|","|96%.|","|99%.|","His existence was screaming.","It was the scream of fullness, of a vessel filled to its brim. He was packed so dense that the Domain around him had begun to bend toward him, its blue-gold hills tilting, its river of light curving in toward where he stood, as though he had become the center of everything inside it. Ruination’s beams had gone still. THE Infiniverse’s eyes were wide.","The last Existential Chorionic Gonadotropin went down.","| 100%.|","...!","Everything stopped!","The Domain held still around him. His Dream held still. His Root, his existence, all of him, packed to the absolute limit of what his present form could hold, held perfectly, silently still, like a breath drawn in and kept.","And then the prompts came, slow and grand, one after another.","| THE Osmontian Culmination has reached complete saturation.|","|The Absolute of your present existence has been filled.|","|Everything that made you has been gathered: your Dreams, your Records, your Actions, your Memories, every life you lived in the death of time, every gift you gave, every death you granted, every emotion you held and every one you cast out. All of it has culminated.|","|An evolutionary pathway uniquely your own has formed.|","|But your existence, your Dreams, and your history are too vast to culminate in a single shape.|","|Three pathways have formed.|","...!","| PATHWAY I: THE Dreaming Origin.|","|A lifeform whose existence is a Dream that existence must dream along with. Your Empyros and Fiend halves carried to their end.|","|What you dream becomes true, first near you, then across Dimensions, then across whatever you can perceive. Existence itself becomes a thing you dream, and dream again, and dream differently.|","|You would stand at the source of things rather than among them. Every being you meet would be, in part, a dream you are having.|","|Born from: THE Human Dreamer, THE Waking Decree, THE Sovereign of the Lived Hour, every dream you have ever entered.|","|Cost: the farther you dream, the farther you stand from what you dream. The risk of becoming the author of a story you can no longer step inside.|","|PATHWAY II: THE Unsated Sovereign.|","|A lifeform of absolute weight and endless appetite. Your Fiend half carried to its end.|","|Your body becomes denser than any law existence can write. You devour and stay hungry. Everything you consume becomes you, and everything you become, you consume further. Even Immensity, eaten, would only make you heavier.|","|You would grow without ceiling by eating the grandest things in existence, one after another, forever.|","|Born from: THE One Foundation, THE Tide-Crowned Protagonist, THE Rendered Design, every Guard, every corpse, every Kryos you have swallowed.|","|Cost: a hunger with no end has no rest. The risk of becoming a thing that existence fears more than it can love.|","|PATHWAY III: THE Quintessential Human.|","|A lifeform that is human, entirely and infinitely. The first Letter you ever spoke carried to its end: I Am... Human.|","|You keep everything human: fear and love, doubt and hunger, the capacity to be wrong and to learn from it. And all of it becomes infinite. Your emotions generate without end. Your gifts return without end. Your people grow as you grow.|","|You would rise by what you feel and what you give, and carry everyone you hold dear upward with you.|","|Born from: THE Living Grammar, THE Sanguine Covenant, the Letter Human, every life you sheltered, every gift you gave freely, every death you refused to stay dead.|","|Cost: you would remain vulnerable in every way a human is vulnerable. Only, infinitely so.|","...!","The last prompt came slowly.","| Every Lifeform that has ever evolved has stood where you stand now, at the edge of what it was.|","|Most chose without ever knowing they were choosing. Existence chose through them, by hunger and cold and the pressure of their days.|","|You know.|","|Three roads lie before you, and each is truly yours. Your Existence has offered them. Walking them is yours alone.|","|What you become will be decided by neither your power, nor your history, nor any prophecy of three.|","|It will be decided by a single choice. Yours.|","|Choose.|","...!","Noah stood in the stillness of THE Existential Root Domain, packed full to the edge of everything he had ever been, and looked at the three roads.","Behind him, Ruination and THE Infiniverse waited without a sound!"]},{"number":5821,"title":"Chapter 5821: Chapter 5820: THE Dreaming Human Origin!","paragraphs":["Noah looked at the three roads.","THE Dreaming Origin, where existence would dream along with him. THE Unsated Sovereign, where he would grow heavier with everything he ate, forever. THE Quintessential Human, where everything human in him would become infinite. Each one hung before him in the stillness of THE Existential Root Domain, complete and real and waiting for him to step onto it.","He looked at them for a long time.","Then he laughed, very quietly.","\"All of these are a part of me ,\" he said.","His voice was calm.","\"I am a human. I have been a human through everything, through the casting out and the death of time and every door that ever shut in my face. I am a dreamer. Everything I have built, I dreamed first. And I am a sovereign. I rule what is mine, and I take what I need, and I have yet to apologize for it once.\"","He looked from one road to the next. \" Each of you is me. So why the hell do I have to choose?\"","The stillness of the Domain trembled around him.","\"I want it all ,\" Noah said.","His voice rose.","\"I WANT IT ALL!\"","BOOM!","His existence shook!","It shook from the center out, every packed quark in him vibrating at once, his saturated existence lurching toward all three roads at the same time. The roads answered. They bent toward him, and toward each other, and began to bleed together, the Dreaming Origin’s gold running into the Unsated Sovereign’s dark into the Quintessential Human’s warm and living light. Something began to bloom in him!","Something enormous. His skin split along the tendrils of light and blazed. His crown of radiance flared so bright it lit the whole Domain white.","The transformation had begun!","And above him, the sky of THE Existential Root Domain split open.","It cracked from horizon to horizon in a single jagged line, and through the crack poured light that belonged nowhere in his Domain.","Obsidian gold. Black and gold together, like the mists over the Legacy, but colder. Older. It came down out of the crack in great falling shapes, and each shape was a piece of existence itself given weight and aimed at him.","He could feel what they were as they fell!","A Provenance of Ending. A Provenance of Order. A Provenance of Stillness, a Provenance of the Counted, a Provenance of the Door.","Aspects of existence, concepts as old as anything that had ever been, crashing down toward the one being in the Domain who had just tried to become something existence had forbidden!","|How dare you.|","...!","The first one hit him!","It struck like the fall of countless Dimensons, and the blue-gold hills around him flattened into glass in a ring a hundred miles wide. The light of it was so bright that for an instant he saw nothing at all, only white, only the weight.","| How dare you.|","A heavy voice boomed out!","The second hit him. The third. They came down out of the crack one after another, an endless cascade, Ending and Order and Stillness and the Counted, each one a judgment, each one heavy enough to unmake even a certain big fat panda per strike, and every one of them aimed at him.","He raised his hands, furious, and met them!","The blasts landed on his palms, his arms, his chest, and burst. Their residue sprayed outward across the Domain in waves of obsidian gold, and where it touched, things stopped being what they had been. The river of light froze into a ribbon of crystal. The orchards went still and clear. And at the edge of the flattened ring, the residue washed over Ruination and THE Infiniverse.","Their bodies began to turn to glass!","It crept up Ruination’s legs, clear and hard, freezing her mid-step. It climbed THE Infiniverse’s coat of many colors, turning fur to frozen crystal. They roared, both of them, a sound Noah was hearing from either of them for the first time, and the glass cracked across their arms as they fought it, and kept climbing.","| Source of this Judgment: ?????.|","|A portion of existence objects to your becoming.|","|You were never meant to find this road.|","|Return to what was counted.|","...!","A portion of existence, then. Some part of it, old and obsidian and gold, reaching down through the crack in his own Domain to stop him from becoming what he was becoming. Who? What?","The blasts kept coming.","And Noah began to take them.","He felt it happen the moment he understood it. Every blast that landed on him was a Provenance. Ending, Order, Stillness, the Counted, each one a piece of existence’s own foundation, raw and pure and pouring down on him without end. THE One Foundation kept every ounce of their weight and built it into floor. His Hunger refined them as they struck, breaking them down without waste. Every judgment existence threw at him, he swallowed, and every one he swallowed made the transformation burn hotter!","| Warning: the Judgment is being consumed.|","|Provenance of Ending: integrated.|","|Provenance of Order: integrated.|","|Provenance of Stillness: integrated.|","|Your evolution is accelerating.|","The crack in the sky widened. Faster and heavier the blasts came, the obsidian gold pouring down in torrents now, enough to bury many things, while the glass crept up Ruination’s chest and THE Infiniverse’s throat, and the whole Domain groaned under it.","Noah threw his head back and bellowed.","\" This is my Domain!\"","His voice tore through the falling light.","\" MY DOMAIN! MOVE!\"","BOOM!","Dream erupted out of him!","Boundless waves of it, blue and gold and infinite, roaring up from his body in every direction at once. They hit the falling Provenances and swallowed them, and washed the residue away, and swept over Ruination and THE Infiniverse, and the glass on their bodies dreamed itself back into flesh and fur and crimson coat. And then they rose to the crack in the sky, and closed it.","The crack sealed shut with a sound like a great door slamming!","The last obsidian gold light vanished, and the Domain went quiet. His dream-seas settled over every hill and river, closed off from everything above, his and his alone.","He had withstood it.","| The Judgment has been withstood.|","|Your Domain has been sealed from within.|","|The three roads have joined.|","|Evolution: THE Osmontian, THE Dreaming Human Origin.|","|Human. Dreamer. Sovereign. All three, and more.|","...!","Then his existence shook one final time, and Noah fell asleep!","He went down into the dream like a man sinking into deep water, slow, and easy, and complete.","Around him, everything that had ever made him rose. His Provenance came first, blue and gold, wrapping around him in long slow bands. Then his Dream, soft and endless, layer over layer, and his Infinity winding through both, the finite and the infinite at once, and through all of it, the Long Night’s cold he had carried, and the Provenances of existence he had just devoured. Every memory, every life he had lived, every death, all of it wrapped around him, tighter and tighter, until he hung in the center of the Domain inside a cocoon of everything he had ever been, and began to change.","The Domain changed with him!","Its blue-gold hills rose and rolled into new shapes, valleys deepening, ridges sharpening. The frozen river thawed and ran again, wider now, brighter, its star-pools multiplying until they spread like a second sky along its bed. Orchards bloomed with fruit that glowed.","Overhead, a single unmoving star above the Domain split into many, then hundreds, a whole new heaven of stars opening across a sky that had once held only one. Time ran differently along the edges of the Domain now, slower in some places, faster in others, a living hour breathing in and out.","Ruination and THE Infiniverse stood where his dream had freed them, and watched.","And they felt it.","A suffocation, rising out of the cocoon at the center of the Domain, so heavy and so total that the air turned thick in their throats. It pressed on them. More than the Warden’s gaze!","Oh!","And it made them happy!","Ruination’s crimson beams trembled. THE Infiniverse pressed a hand to her chest. They looked at each other, and then at the cocoon, and something lit in both their faces that was very close to joy.","Was their Master truly this strong?!","HUUM!","The cocoon opened.","It came apart slowly, bands of Provenance unwinding, Dream peeling away layer by layer, and the figure inside floated free.","He was tall. Taller than before, and leaner in some places and broader in others, his proportions shifted just past what a human body could have held.","His skin was the deep dark of a sky at night, and beneath it, slow-drifting rivers of blue-gold light moved like constellations wheeling across that sky, so that looking at him felt like looking up on a clear night far from any city. His hair hung weightless around his head, long and white-gold, drifting as though he stood underwaterr.","The crown of light had become part of him: two great curving horns of blue-gold radiance swept back from his brow, rooted in his skull. Behind his shoulders, faint and half-real, a slow ring of light turned, a halo made of time, ticking.","He was almost alien. He was also, unmistakably, grand.","Noah opened his eyes.","They were pure gold. Every part of them, white and iris alike, a single unbroken gold, with no pupils at all. They shone softly in the dark of his face, calm and bottomless and very old.","He looked down at himself.","| Evolution complete.|","|Lifeform: THE Osmontian, THE Dreaming Human Origin.|","|The first of its kind. A lifeform that exists by its own design, apart from Immensity and beyond the bounds of a Root.|","|Evolution count: 1.|","| From the Human: your emotions generate without end. Those you hold dear grow as you grow. You keep the capacity to fear, to love, to be wrong, and to learn; all of it is now infinite.|","|From the Dreamer: what you dream near you becomes true, and the reach of that truth grows as you grow. Existence near you dreams, and you hold the dream.|","|From the Sovereign: you devour without end and grow from all you devour. There is no ceiling on what you may consume or become.|","|And more: the Provenances of Ending, Order, and Stillness, taken from the Judgment, are now your own.|","| VERITAS: Uncounted. PROVENANCE: Uncounted. POTENTIA: Infinite. PONDUS: Uncounted. OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: Uncounted.|","|Existence no longer measures you in numbers it can write.|","|Eyes: THE Gold Without Pupils. You see a thing as it truly is, all of it at once.|","|Next evolution: Saturation 0%. The Absolute of your new existence is beyond present estimate.|","|Immensity: ?????|","...!","Noah read it all.","Then he read the last line again.","Immensity. A string of question marks, where every other line had an answer.","He had taken a different road, leaving Immensity ungrasped, its door unpassed, its thrones to others. Walking away from all of it, he had become something that door had no power to stop.","So what was he now?","He looked up through his new gold eyes at the sealed sky of his Domain, and wondered, compared to the Immense Ones out there in the storm, exactly what he had become!"]},{"number":5822,"title":"Chapter 5822: Chapter 5821: Kin! I","paragraphs":["Noah touched his chest.","He did it without thinking, as a man touches the place where something has changed inside him, and the moment his fingers rested over the center of himself, he felt it.","A tree!","It stood inside his existence, where his Root had always been, grown past anything a Root could be. A trunk of blue-gold light rose up out of the deepest place in him, broad and straight and huming, and it went up. And up!","And up, past the reach of his gold eyes and his Dream and his Infinity, climbing into an endless height he could sense, its end somewhere far beyond his sight. Branches waited in the dark above. A canopy, perhaps. He could feel the weight of it hanging up there.","Only the very base of the trunk was glowing!","He had lit it. Barely! A thin band of blue-gold light around the bottom of a tree that went on forever, and everything above that band dark, waiting.","THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin had become this. His Root, the spinning mobius he had carried since the Convocation, had taken everything poured into it, every Quintessential ECG, every Kryos, a dead Immense One and grown into something measured by a different scale entirely.","He stood very still with his hand on his chest, and the prompts came.","| THE Osmontian Chorionic Gonadotropin has grown.|","|It is now THE Budding Dreaming Human Origin Tree.|","|Your evolution has lit its First Ring. The trunk above waits in the dark.|","...!","Then the Tree laid its workings open to him, one by one!","| The Tree has unlocked your Core Weaving of THE Feast That Seals. Its details are below.|","|Predation. Devour grand beings, and your Tree drinks them. What it drinks rises through the trunk as Sap. The Tree remembers the nature of all it drinks, and may grant you an Ability, a Provenance, or an Authority born of that nature. The grander the meal, the richer the Sap and the greater the yield.|","|Auto-Fusion. Whatever the Tree holds of a kind will fuse on its own into something higher. Abilities with Abilities. Provenances with Provenances. Authorities with Authorities. And, where their natures agree, across all three.|","|Giving. What you give with thought returns through THE Tide, and what returns feeds the Tree.|","|Judgment. Grow beyond what existence allows, and existence will judge you. Survive grand Judgments of your existence, and the Tree grows a Branch. Every Branch bears a Seal or an Unsealing.|","|Kin. Those you mark with your blood, or name as your own or grant kinship in unique ways, rise when your Tree rises.|","|Rings lit: 1.|","|Sap risen toward the First Bough: 0%.|","|When the Sap reaches the First Bough, your Tree will flower, and you will advance.|","|Judgment Debt: 1. Existence will remember.|","...!","Noah almost laughed. He had devoured a dead Immense One and an Ergosphere and survived a Judgment from existence itself, and evolved into a lifeform no record held a name for, and the Tree looked down at him from its endless height and showed him one lit ring and an empty measure of Sap.","Fair enough. He had barely lit the base!","Then the last prompt came, larger than the others!","| Your Tree has grown its first Branch.|","|You devoured the Provenances of Ending, Order, and Stillness while existence struck you with them. They were the substance of the Severing. Your Tree has drunk them.|","|THE First Unsealing: THE Door of Immensity.|","|You may open the closed door for a being who holds a Root.|","|When they reach for Immensity, the Severing will come for them. You may stand within it beside them, and hold their Root together while it tries to cut them apart.|","|If they endure, they may establish their Immensity.|","|Existence will judge every such attempt. You must fight that Judgment each time.|","|Each attempt adds to your Judgment Debt.|","...!","Noah went still!","Low on the trunk of the endless tree inside him, just above the thin lit band at its base, he felt it. A single Branch, newly grown, reaching out from the blue-gold wood, heavy with something that hummed in the same pitch as the closed door at the top of his old existence.","Behind him, Ruination’s crimson beams had locked onto the prompt and stopped scrolling. THE Infiniverse had taken a single step forward.","He read it again.","Minerva, on the Plain of Accord, reaching for Immensity with everything she had. The door shutting in her face. Her Root splitting down the middle with a sound like a great tree breaking, green light pouring out of her like blood, while a stranger’s voice spoke through her mouth and swore no new Immensity would rise.","He could have stood beside her in that!","He could have held her Root together while the Severing tried to cut it apart, and fought whatever came down from above, and given her a chance to stand up on the other side of the door.","His thoughts ran, fast and clear.","Thalia, with her Root of genome alteration, who could unmake and rebuild the code of anything she touched. Emotive, with a Physical Root of Emotion and a singularity of failed Immensity in her hands. Ling, who was a Root from her skin to her core. Every one of his people with Kryos sitting in their dreams right now, slowly seeding Roots of their own.","Every one of them, someday, might reach for the door.","And when they did, he could reach with them. They were Kin. When they rose, his Tree would rise with them.","Oh!","Noah breathed out slowly, his hand still resting over the endless tree in his chest.","Then he smiled!","It was a small smile, and a far from gentle one.","Noah looked at the line about Kin again.","Those you mark with your blood, or name as your own...","His Tree had risen. He could feel it inside him, the endless blue-gold trunk with its single lit ring and its first Branch humming in the dark. He had been dreamed into a new lifeform, devoured an Immense One, survived the Judgment of existence itself.","And around him, everything sat exactly as before.","Ruination stood where she had stood. THE Infiniverse stood beside her. Far away in THE Infiniverse, the Dream Engine hummed on as it always had, his people sleeping and dreaming on the golden shore.","His hand closed into a fist!","Instead of waiting for the Tree, he dreamed it.","He dreamed his family rising. All of them, every life he held dear, every person sleeping in the Dream Engine with a Kryos seeded in their dreams, every one of them climbing with him as the Tree had promised. He poured that dream down into the trunk inside his chest with everything he had, and the whole Domain trembled with it.","\"I have had my transformation ,\" Noah said.","His voice was low, and very hard.","\"It is my dream to elevate my family alongside me. So why hasn’t it begun?\"","...!","The Tree answered!","| Kin recognized.|","|Your Dream has been heard. THE Feast That Seals carries it down every thread that binds you to your own.|","|Kin Evolution has begun.|","...!","Light bloomed behind him!","Hazy cocoons of blue and gold were rising arround Ruination and THE Infiniverse, soft and shining, wrapping them in slow bands of light. Ruination’s crimson beams flickered and went quiet as the haze closed over her face. THE Infiniverse’s coat of many colors vanished into the gold. Both of them welcomed it. Both of them turned their eyes to Noah as the cocoons sealed shut, and the last thing he saw of their faces before the light swallowed them was joy.","And across THE Infiniverse, the Dream Engine began to glow!","He felt it through the threads. His people, dreaming on the golden shore, every one of them carrying a Kryos he had sent into their dreams. One after another, the light found them. His mother, sleeping beneath her blankets, wrapped in a cocoon of soft blue. Seo-yeon, curled small, glowing gold. Henry. Adelaide. Barbatos, deep in her necropolis with the Warden’s corpse beside her, cocooned in green-tinged gold while her raised dead stood around her in silent watch.","Eon. Naldine. Ul’moreth. Thalia.","And Emotive!","Her cocoon was the brightest of all!","It rose around her in the reimagined Earliest Folds, among the broken statues of him she still had yet to let him fix, and it shone in every color. Every color there was, shifting and burning at once, crimson rage and violet longing and gold joy and a deep, endless, bottomless blue of grief, all of it pouring out of her in waves as the cocoon closed.","Her Physical Root of Emotion drank in the Kin light, and the Stillborn Singularity she still held against her chest flickered in answer, there and gone and there. Her whole dream shook with the weight of what she fellt. The towers of THE Loom bent toward her. The statues of him turned their stone heads!","She was laughing as the cocoon closed. Laughing, and crying!","His fist slowly opened.","—","Far below, on the frozen plain at the edge of the northern rift of THE Undersnow, Ling had kept her eyes on him the whole time.","She hung in the dark beside the body of Noah that had stayed in THE Undersnow, the body that had fought the Warden and lain on its chest and taken its Dream. And she had watched that body change.","It had happened while he stood still. His diamond-jade skin had darkened to the deep black of a sky at night, constellations of blue-gold drifting slow beneath it. His hair had gone white-gold and weightless. Two great horns of radiance had swept back from his brow, rooted in his skull, and a faint ring of light had begun turning behind his shoulders. And when he had opened his eyes, they had been gold. Pure gold, all the way through, empty of pupils.","Ling had gone very quiet, watching! Her hands rested on her knees. Her mouth was a little open.","Then her existence pulsed!","It came from the very center of her, from the Root that was her whole being, a single deep throb that shook her from her skin to her core. She gasped. Her hand flew to her chest.","And in front of Noah’s gold eyes, the prompts rose.","| Among your Kin, only one has a foundation already established and ready to take a step toward Immensity.|","|Ling has been loosely designated as part of your Kin, due to your seed that remains within her.|","|Her existence is already saturated.|","|Her own evolution is beginning.|","...!"]},{"number":5823,"title":"Chapter 5823: Chapter 5822: Kin! II","paragraphs":["Ling’s hand was still pressed to her chest when her existence began to reach.","All of her, every part of the Root that was her whole being, had begun to stretch upward, toward something far above both of them in the frozen dark. Threads of her lifted off her skin, pale and shining, rising like steam off warm water in wintter. Her ribbons, long lost in the battles, seemed to drift back into being around her wrists out of nothing. The air around her went thin and bright and very cold.","She was reaching for Immensity.","And she knew it!","Her face went white. She clutched at her chest with both hands as though she could hold herself down, and the threads kept rising regardless, pulling at her, drawing her upward toward the door she had watched slam shut on the Plain of Accord.","In a rush of half-sentences, she told him what she was feeling. Terror, first!","The door was shut. Everyone knew it was shut. She had watched Minerva’s Root break in half on the snow, watched the green light pour out of her like blood. And now her own existence was reaching for that same door, by itself, without asking her, and she was helpless to stop it!","\" I’m not doing this ,\" Ling said. Her voice was heavy! \" I’m not, it’s just, it’s going on its own, and if it reaches the door I’m going to, I’ll be just like her, I’ll be...\"","Noah floated down to her.","He put a hand on her shoulder. His fingers rested on the blue silk, and through them she could feel the weight of him.","\" It’s okay ,\" he said.","She stared at him.","\" Your existence is reaching because it is ready. Reach. When the door comes for you, I will be standing in it with you.\"","She looked at him for a long, trembling moment.","Then the fear in them changed.","It hardened. Her hands came away from her chest and closed into fists, and her powerful thighs coiled under her, and her whole body began to hum!","WUU!","\" Fine ,\" Ling said.","She threw back her head and roared.","\" Fine! FINE! You want to cut me apart? You want to tell me no? Fuck you! Fuck the door, fuck the cold, fuck every voice that ever said no new Immensity! Come and get me, then!\"","BOOM!","And she gathered herself!","Every thread of her that had been drifting upward, she took hold of. She pulled them in, wound them tight, drew every scrap of her existence into a single burning point at the center of her body, and then she flung it all upward at once. Toward Immensity. Toward everything that had been shut against her.","The Basal Floor went white!","Far above them, in the frozen dark, a hazy door appeared.","It hung above Ling, vast and pale and sealed, and as she reached for it, the cold came down.","It fell from the door like a blade of blue-white winter, long and thin and absolute, the same color as the eyes that had looked out of Minerva’s face. It came down straight toward the center of Ling’s Root, meaning to split her in two, exactly as it had split the Progeny on the Plain of Accord.","Noah rose to meet it.","The Branch on his Tree hummed!","| THE First Unsealing: THE Door of Immensity.|","|A Kin reaches for Immensity. You may stand within the Severing beside her.|","...!","He stood above Ling, between her and the falling blade, and opened his hand.","The Severing struck his palm!","It cut. It was made to cut Roots, and it found the Tree that stood where his Root had been, and it bit into him like the edge of the whole Long Night at once. Pain went through him from his hand to his core. His skin split along his palm and blue-gold light poured out. But his hand held its place, and the blade stayed above Ling.","Below him, she kept reaching. Her existence was climbing, burning, pulling upward toward the door, and the Severing kept trying to find a way past him to her Root, and every time it slid, he moved, and every time it pressed, he held.","He reached down with his other hand, past the blade, and laid it over the center of her Root.","He held it together.","The Severing pressed down on her Root through his hand, trying to find the seam that would let it split her, and he gave it none. His Dream poured into her Root and wrapped it, held it, pressed every part of it close, until the only thing left for the blade to cut was him!","And then the Judgment came!","Obsidian gold. It tore open the sky above the door, the same cold old light that had crashed into his Domain, and it fell on him with all its weight.","| HOW DARE YOU.|","...!","It landed on his shoulders like a mountain range. His knees bent. His crown of radiance flared. The obsidian gold pressed down on him from above while the Severing pressed up against his palm from below, and between the two of them, his whole existence groaned.","It smashed down with the same Provenances he had devoured before!","He held on!","Below his hands, Ling reached the door.","It opened in silence!","And Noah did something new under the whole of existence. He let her go through it inside his Dream.","Blue-gold light poured down out of his hand into the center of her, out of the endless Tree in his chest, out of every dream he had ever dreamed. Its source was him; the door merely stood open above them. Ling passed through it wrapped entirely in his Dream, and on the other side of it, what took shape in her was something the door had given no one before her.","Immensity, dreamed.","It came into her slowly, solemnly, like something sacred being set into place. Her Root, already her whole existence, began to unfurl. It grew in depth rather than size. Layer upon layer of her opened, each one revealing another beneath it, and each layer filled with blue-gold dream and kept it.","Threads ran from the deepest of those layers up into Noah’s hand, and through his hand to the Tree in his chest, binding her new Immensity to the place it had been dreamed from. Her existence stretched outward from the small round-faced girl in blue silk into something vast, something that pressed against the frozen dark of the Basal Floor and kept pressing, until the dark gave way.","She rose.","Her silk dress darkened into the deep blue of the sky at dusk, embroidered now with burning lines of light in place of gold thread, lines that ran and shifted across it. Loose from its buns, her hair spread around her in a great dark cloud, and through it wound ribbons of white flame, long and slow and living. Her powerful legs blazed with blue-gold dream-light from hip to heel, every line of muscle lit from within, so bright they were hard to look at. Behind her, purple fire bloomed, the same deep violet as the torches in her father’s cavern, wreathing her shoulders in a slow, steady burn.","And her eyes opened.","They were white. Pure white, all the way through, without a pupil anywhere in them. Exactly like her father’s.","The Severing shattered against Noah’s palm!","It broke into a thousand blue-white shards and faded into nothing. Above him, the obsidian gold Judgment shuddered, and pressed down one last time, and withdrew into the sky, and the sky closed behind it.","| The Severing has been withstood.|","|The Judgment has been withstood.|","|Judgment Debt: 2. Existence will remember.|","|Kin Evolution: Ling has established a Dream Immensity.|","|A Dream Immensity is formed within your Dream, and rooted in it. It is Immensity, true and whole, yet it answers to the Dream that bore it rather than to the door.|","|It grows as your Tree grows. Its threads are bound to you.|","|Your Tree drinks from the rising of its Kin.|","|Sap risen toward the First Bough: 14%.|","...!","The door above them faded. The Basal Floor’s frozen dark rushed back in around them, and Ling hung in the middle of it, vast and shining, her white eyes fixed on Noah.","She spoke, and existence carried it.","|I am THE Dancer in the Boundless Dream.|","|I am lucky enough to attain Immensity when I had absolutely no reason to.|","|I am...grateful.|","A pause, and her white eyes narrowed with something very like her old cheerful grin.","|So let me thank you properly, Big Boy.|","...!","She moved!","With no wind-up at all, one moment she hung before him, and the next her leg was already swinging, thick and powerful and blazing with dreamed Immensity, coming at him with the whole weight of something newly risen behind it!","Noah raised his hand.","That was all. One open hand, lifted calmly into the path of her kick.","Boundless dream unfurled from it!","Blue-gold light poured out of his palm in an endless tide, wave after wave of it, soft and infinite, rolling out to meet her leg. Her Immensity crashed into it. And the dream took it. All of it. The whole weight of a kick carrying Dream Immensity, absorbed into a tide of dream with no far wall, held in his single open hand.","Her leg stopped a hand’s width from his palm.","The force of it went on.","BOOOOM!","Out around them it went, in every direction at once, a ring of pure released Immensity tearing out across the Basal Floor, and everything it touched broke. Floating islands cracked in half and spun away. Torn Dimensions shattered like dropped glass. The jammed frozen plain around the northern rift split into a thousand peices and fell apart into the dark, and the cold-filled trees snapped and toppled, and the crack ran on and on, out past anything One’s eyes could follow, until half of the Basal Floor lay in ruin around them, broken and drifting, destroyed by a single kick that had stopped short of its target.","And in the middle of all of it, Noah stood with his hand raised and his gold eyes calm, holding back the leg of a Dream Immensity with nothing but his palm and the Dream it had risen from.","Ling looked at him over her own blazing knee.","Her white eyes went wide!","Noah held his hand where it was, open in the frozen dark, Ling’s blazing leg resting a hand’s width from his palm.","He looked at it.","His hand. The same hand that had once thrown fireballs in a dilapidated city, the hand that had killed apes and bears and turtles and dragons, the hand that had grasped Beasts and Demons and Celestials!","The hand that had shaken under the weight of a stone in a dead domain, that had held a dying Steed’s haed and pressed a cure into an ancient line of script. Night-dark now, constellations drifting under the skin, a split still healing across the palm where the Severing had bitten him.","And it had just stopped the full weight of an Immensity!","Something rose in his chest!","It came up from the part of him the evolution had kept human and made infinite. It was warm, and loud, and it shook, far removed from the cold, far-away clarity of the infinite dream where every path was already walked.","He had done it!","All those years. The apocalypses, and the fear, and the first clumsy skills. Every time he had looked up at something vast and known in his bones that it could end him with a glance. Every time he had told himself he would get there, someday, somehow.","Today, an Immense One had kicked him with everything she had.","And he had stopped it with one hand!","His eyes stung. He had gold eyes now, pupil-less, eyes that saw everything as it truly was, and they were burning at the edges like any man’s. His throat had gone tight. He was laughing, a little, under his breath! He felt like he was laughing and crying at the emotions infinitely stretching across him!","So this was it. The human side of what he had become. The part that would always feel everything, infinitely.","It felt like this as it was glorious!","Ling was still staring at him over her knee, white eyes wide.","Noah let the feeling run all the way through him. He let it rise and rise until it filled him from his crown to his heels.","Then he moved!","His hand left her leg and came up, and came down. Straight down, swung like a hammer, toward the center of Ling’s forehead!","It was fast. So fast that the frozen dark between them seemed to skip. And it carried something with it, riding on the edge of the swing, a dream he was dreaming for the first time: extinction.","Ending without remainder, without return, the dream of a thing simply ceasing to have ever been.","Ling’s entire existence buzzed!","Her new Dream Immensity screamed alarm through every layer of her at once, and her white eyes flew wider, and her body was still deciding which way to move when the hand arrived.","It stopped!","A finger’s breadth from her forehead, his palm hung perfectly still. The dream of extinction riding on it went quiet and drew back into him, tucked away, gone. The wind of the swing caught up a moment later and blew her hair back from her face in one great dark rush.","She forgot to breathe as only now did she begin heaving as if she had escaped death.","For a long moment, both of them stayed perfectly still. She stared at his hand. He stared at her face. Her lips had parted. Her white eyes were enormous.","Then his hand turned.","Slowly, gently, it moved from her forehead to the side of her face, and rested there, his palm warm against her cheek, his thumb under the curve of her jaw. She leaned into it before she seemed to know she was doign it.","He pulled her in, and kissed her!","Ling made a small, startled sound against his mouth. Then her hands found the back of his neck and gripped hard, her fingers sinking into his weightless white-gold hair, and she kissed him back with the whole fierce, cheerful, foul-mouthed force of her, a newly risen Dream Immensity wrapped around him in the ruins of half the Basal Floor.","Golden clouds bloomed around them.","They rose out of Noah on their own, soft and thick and shining, rolling up over the two of them and closing like curtains around a bed. The ruined islands vanished, and the drifting shards of shattered Dimensions, and the frozen dark. There was only gold, and warmth, and the two of them inside it.","His human side wanted much more for the sake of...research.","He let it have its way!"]},{"number":5824,"title":"Chapter 5824: Chapter 5823: Immensity! I","paragraphs":["The golden clouds thinned a long while later, and the frozen dark of the Basal Floor came back in pieces.","Noah lay on his back on a drift of dream with Ling asleep against his chest, her dark hair spread across both of them, one blazing leg hooked over his.","He might have been a bit...relentless.","Above them, half of a destroyed Floor drifted in silence. Islands split down their middles turned slowly in the cold. Shards of shattered Dimensions hung like broken windows, each one still holding a sliver of whatever sky it had once looked out on. Snow fell through all of it, unhurrid, as though nothing at all had happened here.","The Tree in his chest hummed.","He listened to it for a while. One lit ring at the base of an endless trunk. A single Branch with the Unsealing hanging from it. Sap sitting low in the wood, waiting. He had evolved into a lifeform no record held a name for, and he understood...only a little about what that meant.","That had to change!","So he began to test!","He started with the part of him that was human, and let himself worry, on purpose. He thought of the cocoons in the Dream Engine, of his mother and Seo-yeon and Henry sealed in light, of Emotive burning in every color with a stolen singularity against her chest. The worry rose, as worry does. And then it kept rising. It fed itself. It generated more of itself without end, and every bit of it poured into him as strength, a slow warm pressure filling his limbs.","He let it run for a full minute, then tried to set it down.","It went quiet when he asked, and stayed, a low warmth under everything.","Results showed that... his emotions were fuel, endless, a well that would keep giving forever. They would also keep speaking forever, under everything. He would have to carry every feeling he had for the rest of his existence, and carry it well.","Next, the Dreamer.","He turned his gold eyes on the nearest broken island, a slab of ice split clean in two with a frozen forest on each half, and dreamed it whole. The halves drifted together, and the crack sealed from the bottom up, ice knitting to ice, roots finding roots across the seam, until the forest stood! He stopped dreaming, and it stayed. It was simply an island again, real, as though the kick had passed it by.","He widened the dream. Ten islands came together around him. Then a hundred, a whole archipelgo of frozen land reassembling itself in the dark, cold-filled trees righting themselves, shattered Dimensions folding their broken skies back into frames for Gigaparsecs.","At the edge, the truth began to thin. The farthest islands held together, but loosely, their seams faint, as though they might remember being broken if anything struck them hard enough.","So...what he dreamed near him became true, and the reach grew with his attention. Spread it too far and the truth wore thin at the edges.","Then the Sovereign.","He opened his mouth, and the blue-gold brilliance inside it looked out onto the ruin, and he pulled. Everything that remained of the destruction came to him: Dimensional shards too broken to dream back, the lingering cold of the Warden soaked into the drifting ice, the faint residue of fifty-five Guards’ patrols still hanging in the dark like old footprints. It all streamed into the event horizons inside him and went down as he literally devoured nearly a forth of THE Basal Floor of THE Undersnow.","The Tree drank!","| Predation: residue of THE Basal Floor.|","|Sap risen toward the First Bough: 17%.|","|Auto-Fusion: Provenance of Stillness + the lingering cold of THE Warden Who Does Not Rise.|","|Formed: Authority of the Held Breath (Minor). Whatever you hold in your gaze, you may still for a moment.|","...!","\"...Hmm.\"","He tried it at once. He looked at a falling snowflake and held it. It stopped in the air, perfectly still, for the space of a breath. Then it fell on.","A bit useless, but okay!","Last, his eyes.","He looked down at Ling!","The Gold Without Pupils showed her as she truly was. A girl asleep, round-faced, her lips parted. And beneath that, her Dream Immensity, deep and shining, layer on layer, every layer bound by fine bright threads that ran up out of her chest and into his Tree.","She looked like a pulsing nervous system that rapidly circulated golden pulses of Immensity as her entire body buzzed.","Deep, compared to anything he had been a day ago. Shallow, compared to the depth he could feel in the Thinker even from here, a pressure at the very edge of his senses, like the pull of a sea far below a cliff.","He checked the Kin next, through the Dream Engine. Every cocoon still closed, still glowing. Ruination and THE Infiniverse in their bands of blue-gold haze in the Root Domain. His mother in soft blue. Seo-yeon curled small in gold. And Emotive’s cocoon, brightest of all, burning every color at once, the Singularity flickering against her chest like a heartbeat.","Then the sliver he had left on the Thinker’s mountain screamed at him!","The pressure on it spiked. Through it, Noah felt the purple coat of Immensity around the mountain buckle inward, as though something enormous had leaned its whole weight against it, and the coat had bent.","Ling woke!","She opened her white eyes and looked at his face, and whatever she saw there brought her upright in an instant. She asked what was wrong.","\" Some invaders into the Legacy. Something is pressing on your father’s Immensity hard enough to bend it.\"","...!","She was on her feet before he finished.","Her father’s mountain was her home!","But...","\"Don’t worry.\"","He told her calmly, his endlessly gold eyes without pupils calming her down completely!!","He gathered himself, and the Basal Floor fell away!","---","In the cavern, the sliver filled. It swelled from a thread of attention into the whole of him, night-dark and crowned, constellations drifting under his skin, his white-gold hair lifting off his shoulders.","Noah opened his gold eyes on the prayer mat.","Across from him, the Thinker’s great beads stopped clicking. The kneeling giant turned his weeping, pupil-less eyes toward him and regarded him for a long moment.","|\" You seem a bit...different,\"| the Thinker said mildly.","Noah didn’t reply to these words as he looked up through the stone of the mountain, and for the first time in his existence, he saw the Immense as they truly were.","Before, they had been hazes. Thrones on golden clouds with shapes too deep to resolve, auras that pressed and loomed and gave him nothing to hold. Now his gold eyes went through the cavern ceiling and the mountain’s peak and the torn purple coat above it, out into the sky of THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity, and the hazes were gone.","The Legacy was at war, and he could see every one of its warriors!","First, he saw Sir Moriarty!","The octopus-headed visage still hung across the sky, obsidian veined with gold, crimson eyes blazing over the walled domains. But the visage was only the part that showed. Beneath it, Noah’s eyes followed the rest of Moriarty down, and down. The great body coiled through the foundations of the Legacy itself.","Its tentacles ran through every Existential Conduit as roots run through soil, threaded under the purple-gold rivers, wrapped around the bases of the thousand mountains, braided through the snow-buried floor. Some of those tentacles were older than the mountains they held up.","The Legacy was defended by Moriarty. In places, the Legacy was Moriarty.","And all through that vast coiled body, faint and sick, ran threads of poisonous green!","Noah let his gaze move across the walled domains.","On one mountain, THE Ashen Cantor stood in a robe of grey cinders with his mouth open, singing. Each note struck a golden sphere of foreign Immensity and unwrote a piece of it, gold peeling away from the sphere in long flakes and drifting off into nothing.","On a peak to the east, THE Keeper of the Unbroken Vow stood with a chain wrapped three times around an invader, and the chain was made of oaths, every promise ever kept in the Legacy hammered link by link into iron. The invader strained against it, and every link held!","Farther off, THE Lantern of the Last Shore, a tall robed figure with no face beneath the hood, lifted a lamp whose light showed the dead where to go, and the invaders it touched turned and began to walk that way, slowly, as though they had remembered somewhere they were meant to be. And over the Firmament, THE Hollow Choir hung in a ring of hollow faces, and their silence fell on the enemies below like a crushing tide.","Every one of them was deep. Deeper than anything Noah could measure!","And every one of them was different!","He turned to the Thinker.","\" Why do some burn brighter than others?\" he asked.","The Thinker considered the question as though it were a stone he had been handed, turning it over between his great fingers.","|\" Oh? Can you actually see Immensity at this time? Hmm...Well, what makes a well deep? \"| he asked in return.","Noah waited.","|\" Immensity is depth, \"| THE Thinker said at last, |\" not height. Everyone who first reaches it believes they have climbed. They have dug. And depth is measured in what one has carried through the Ages. A young Immensity is shallow, and loud, because it has carried little and wishes everyone to know it has carried anything at all. An old one is quiet.\"|","His beads clicked once. | \"There is more to it than that. As the big guy said, there are levels to this.\"|","Noah looked back out at the war.","Now that he knew what to look for, he could see it. The invading spheres were not all alike. Some blazed and roared, gold flaring, straining loudly against their walls: young, he guessed, only a few Ages into their Immensity. Others hung almost still, dim and patient, and those seemed far too heavy.","\" A war between the depths of wells ,\" Noah said quietly.","\" Each one deeper than the last. Each one sure it holds the water that matters. And I am standing at the edge of all of them with a Tree whose roots have only just reached the water.\"","He watched a golden sphere flake apart under the Cantor’s song. \"It is a strange thing, to finally see the size of the sky and know you cannot touch it yet.\"","The Thinker said nothing to that. But his beads went still for a moment, and then resumed.","Then Noah turned his gold eyes on his host.","For a while he had sat across from THE Thinker. He had seen the kneeling giant, the boulder beads, the weeping eyes and the fierce almost-smile and the purple torches along the walls. He had felt the depth of him at the edge of his senses, as one feels the drop beyond the edge of a cliff in the dark.","Now he saw it!","The kneeling giant was a fraction, the smallest part, a single bead on a much longer string. Behind him, the mountain was him; every stone of it carried his Immensity, every vein of ore, every torch. And behind the mountain, beneath it, around it, ran a depth that went down in every direction at onec, purple fire burning along it like torches lit at intervals down a shaft whose floor lay past any sight. Noah looked, and looked, and found no bottom.","The gash on the Thinker’s back leaked Immensity in a slow, steady river. Noah had thought of it as a wound. Through his new eyes it was a river wide enough to drown the Legacy’s largest Conduit, and it was still only the trickle escaping from a sea.","That trickle held more Immensity than multiple invading sphere in the sky combined!","Holy fucking shit. These beings were actually monsters!","Noah very nearly looked away!","|THE Thinker at the End of Existence.|","|Depth: beyond perception.|","...!","The Thinker turned his great head and looked back at him, and the fierce line of his mouth softened, very slightly.","Then the Thinker’s gaze moved past Noah, to the mouth of the cavern, and beyond it, to the sky.","Noah followed it!","At the edge of the walled domain that held the mountain, Moriarty’s obsidian-gold mist had thinned. In one small place only. Something green was threading through it from the inside, fine and patient, a single living tendril finding its way along a seam in the wall that nobody else would have known was there. And it was coming straight at them!","The Thinker’s beads clicked once.","|\" You...get to see me stretch my muscles it seems.\"|","...!"]},{"number":5825,"title":"Chapter 5825: Chapter 5824: Immensity! II","paragraphs":["The green tendril reached the purple coat around the mountain, found a seam in it hidden from everyone but her, and pulled!","The coat opened like a curtain!","Snow blew in through the gap, and with the snow came the scent of spring. Wet earth, new leaves, flowers that had bloomed and fallen and bloomed again for Ages. The torches along the cavern walls leaned toward the opening, then away from it.","THE Verdant Regard stepped through!","She came as a tall figure of soft green light. The body walking into the cavern was one of several. Far away, in her ever-spring domain, the rest of her sat on a bed of moss with her daughter’s head in her lap, and this body was a branch she had sent out from that place, as a tree sends out a root toward water. Even so, its depth went down past his sight.","Green below green below green, spring after spring after spring, an Immensity built from every season that had ever ended and come back.","She knew every path in this Legacy. She had walked them as a friend for longer than most Legacies had stood.","Three more came through behind her!","The first was a woman, tall and stooped, her body corroded bronze from crown to heel, her robe a single sheet of flaking verdicts that rustled when she moved. Where she passed, the stone at the cavern’s mouth went brown and crumbled. The torchlight that touched her came away dull, aged, its color rusted out of it. She walked slowly, with the patience of something that had outlved every enemy it had ever made and expected to outlive a few more.","| THE Rusted Matriarch.|","The second was a beast. Lean and grey, the size of a range of hills pressed down into the cavern’s mouth, its shoulders hunched as it squeezed through. Its eyes were two open doorways with nothing behind them. It stopped just inside the entrance and sniffed at the air, at the walls, at the torn coat behind it, with the deep pleased interest of a hound that has found the most interesting door in existence.","| THE Hound of Thresholds.|","The third was a young man in gilded armor, handsome, golden-haired, his Immensity glittering on him like fresh gold leaf. He swept in with a smile already on his face and looked around the cavern as though he had come to inspect a property he was thinking of buying.","| THE Gilt Heir.|","Noah read them with his gold eyes, one after another. The Gilt Heir was the shallowest, and the loudest; only a few Ages deep, and still more depth than Noah could reach the bottom of. The Hound went deeper, far deeper. Deepest of the three, the Rusted Matriarch’s depth slid away from him entirely, rust on rust on rust, down into a dark beyond his following.","Then the fifth one came, and the cavern changed!","It began before he finished arriving. The purple torches along the walls flickered, and their fire turned crimson gold. The prayer mats darkened at their edges into his colors. Even the snow drifting in through the torn coat stopped in the air, every flake of it, and each one turned slowly to face the entrance.","Noah felt why. Wherever this one’s attention rested, existence began to become his, owned rather than destroyed. The torches still burned, but they burned for him now! The mats still lay on the floor, but they were his mats. He owned what he touched, and he owned a little of whatever he simply looked at.","THE Sleepless Fiend stepped into the cavern!","He came as a tall figure in dark robes, his face barely perceptible, his presence a weight that made the mountain groan. Noah could see more than that now. A great deal more. But the Fiend kept all of that turned away from him so far.","The five of them spread out around the Thinker.","The Thinker stayed on his knees. He knelt on his prayer mat exactly as he had knelt for Ages, his beads clicking slowly through his fingers, his weeping eyes half closed. Behind him, Noah sat on his own mat, his gold eyes calm.","He felt them read him!","He felt each of them look at him and see what he had let them see: a dream of a lifeform whose Root, by every account in the Legacy, had formed days ago.","The Gilt Heir laughed out loud! The Hound sniffed in his direction once and lost interest, and the Rusted Matriarch kept her eyes elsewhere entirely.","THE Sleepless Fiend smiled!","\" Old friend, \" he said to THE Thinker.","His voice was warm. Reasonable. It was the voice of a man arriving late to dinner, sorry to have kept everyone waiting.","\"It has been a very long time. I wish we were meeting over something gentler.\" He spread his hands. \"I regret the method. Truly. The coat, the Legacy, poor Moriarty. None of it was what I would have chosen. But the snow is deep, and getting deeper. The door is shut. You know what that means for all of us who still breathe. Keys must be found, and kept, and used. For the good of everyone.\"","His gaze settled on THE Thinker, gently.","\" Step aside. Let us take the boy. You will not lose anything you cannot afford.\"","THE Thinker’s beads clicked once.","|\"I have thought through a great many probabilities,\"| he said, without opening his eyes. |\" Across a great many Ages. In none of them is a gift from THE Sleepless Fiend paid for by the one who receives it.\"|","|\"I decline.\"|","The Fiend sighed.","THE Verdant Regard took a step forward.","Her soft green light dimmed as she moved, and when she spoke, her voice was nothing like the Fiend’s. It was tired, and raw, and grieving.","\" My daughter has not woken ,\" she said to the Thinker. \" Her Root lies frozen on the moss beside her. The snow falls on her face and I cannot keep it off.\"","She looked at him, and her green eyes were wet. \" You have a daughter. You know. Please. Understand.\"","The Thinker opened his weeping eyes and looked at her for a long moment.","|\"I do understand ,\"| he said gently. | \"And I am sorry. Truly.\" |","His beads stilled . |\"Understanding changes nothing though.\"|","Her face closed!","The Fiend let out a long breath, the sigh of a father over a stubborn child, and lifted one hand.","\" Then ,\" THE Sleepless Fiend said, \"we will simply take the boy.\"","HUUM!","Five depths of Immensity rose inside the cavern at once!","They rose out of the five invaders like tides coming in from five different seas. The Gilt Heir’s gold flared bright and brash. The Hound’s grey Immensity poured out low along the floor, sniffing. Rust spread from the Matriarch in a slow brown wave, aging the air itself. The Verdant Regard’s spring rolled outward, green and overwhelming, flowers bursting from the stone wherever it touched. And the Fiend’s ownership spread from him in every direction, quiet, total, claiming everything it reached.","All five came for the Thinker, and for the man behind him.","The Thinker stayed kneeling!","He opened his great hands, and the beads left them.","They rose into the air, one after another, boulders of dark stone the size of hills, and as they rose, each one caught purple fire. They began to orbit him. Slowly at first, then faster, a ring of burning moons wheeling around a kneeling giant in the heart of his mountain.","One moon swung out and met the Rusted Matriarch’s rust. The corrosion washed against it, and the bead’s purple fire held it, rust and fire grinding against each other in a slow, endless push. Another swung out against the Gilt Heir’s gold and stopped it dead, the young lord’s Immensity flaring and straining and going nowhere. A third met the Verdant Regard’s spring, flowers blooming and withering against its burning surface. A fourth swung out to the Fiend, and the Fiend’s ownership spread across it, and the bead stayed the Thinker’s own.","Four Immense Ones. Four beads. The Thinker held all of them at once without rising from his mat.","The cavern should have collapsed!","Noah could feel the weight in it, five depths of Immensity grinding against one another in a space of stone. The mountain stood because the Thinker had decided it would stand. His weeping eyes stayed half closed. His fierce almost-smile held perfectly still.","This was what depth looked like when it chose to act!","And the Hound found the gap!","It slipped between the orbiting moons at the one instant when two of them crossed, low and grey and quick, its doorway eyes fixed on Noah. Its Immensity poured toward him in a rush.","Out of that rush, a hand formed.","Vast and grey, woven out of the Hound’s Immensity, large enough to close around a mountain. It came down over Noah where he sat on his prayer mat and wrapped around him, fingers curling, and began to close.","The pressure was beyond anything in his life!","The Warden’s half-Immensity had been heavy, flickering, half there. This was whole. Finished. Deep. The grasp of a being that had pased through the door Ages ago and carried every Age since.","It pressed on every part of him at once, and the Tree in his chest shuddred under it, and for an instant he felt how small he was inside that hand.","Then his body answered!","The constellations under his night-dark skin began to move outward. Off his chest, off his arms, off his face, drifting into the air around him, spreading until he sat inside a moving sky of his own, stars of blue and gold wheeling slowly in the space between his skin and the Hound’s closing fingers.","The halo of time behind his shoulders turned faster, ticking. His horns of radiance flared bright enough to throw shadows across the whole cavern.","And his Dreaming Origin side surged forward.","Inside the reach of his dream, things became what he dreamed them to be. And he dreamed that the hand closing on him was closing on a dream of him.","The Hound’s fingers closed, gripping, squeezing with all the weight of an established Immensity.","They were holding a sky!","Noah stood up inside it.","He lifted his own hand, slowly, laid his palm flat against the inside of the Hound’s grey fingers, and pushed.","The Immensity moved!","...!","It moved away from him a hand’s width. Then an arm’s length. The grey fingers bent back, and opened, and the Hound’s whole Immensity slid back from him across the cavern floor like a tide going out, and Noah stood alone on his prayer mat inside his sky of drifting stars with his hand still raised.","...!","|...!|","\"...!\"","The cavern went silent!","Every Immense One in it was looking at him.","The Gilt Heir’s smile had gone, and the Hound had frozen mid-step, its doorway eyes narrowed to slits, and the Rusted Matriarch had finally turned her head, and her rusted face held something that might have been interest. Even THE Verdant Regard had gone still, her green light flickering.","The Gilt Heir spoke first, and his voice cracked on it.","\" The fuck?\"","How...could something so unfathomably weak rebuff an Immensity? This was the singular question orbiting all beings here!","The Thinker’s orbiting beads paused for exactly one heartbeat.","Then they moved on!","| An Immense grasp has been rebuffed.|","|Predation: residue of an Immense One’s reach.|","|Sap risen toward the First Bough: 20%.|","...!","Noah lowered his hand.","His arms were trembling, he noticed. Faintly. The push had cost him: the lit ring at the base of his Tree had dimmed a shade, and it would take a few nanoseconds to burn bright again.","The enemy’s Immensity was many times more powerful than Ling!","Inside his dream, an Immense grasp became a grasp on a dream of him, and he could open it. Holding one off for long would drain him. Holding off two at once, he had no wish to test yet.","And THE Sleepless Fiend, for the first time since he had entered the cavern, turned and looked directly at him.","Every torch in the mountain burned crimson gold at once!"]},{"number":5826,"title":"Chapter 5826: Chapter 5825: Immensity! III","paragraphs":["The Fiend’s gaze rested on Noah for a long, quiet moment.","He smiled a little, and turned back to the Thinker’s burning bead, as though he had decided to save Noah for later.","The Hound had decided otherwise!","It came again, harder, and this time the Gilt Heir tore himself free of the Thinker’s bead and came with it, gold blazing, sword drawn, a young lord’s face twisted with the humiliaton of having laughed too soon. Two Immense Ones, coming for Noah at once!","Noah opened his dream.","Ling came out of it!","She burst from the blue-gold light like a thrown spear, white eyes blazing, legs lit from hip to heel with dream-light, purple fire roaring off her shoulders. The Gilt Heir saw her a heartbeat too late.","Her kick took him across the chest!","BOOM!","He flew across the cavern and slammed into the far wall, and the wall held, because it was the Thinker’s wall. The Gilt Heir peeled himself off it, gold armor dented, his face white with calm shock.","\"You ...\" he said. \" You’re the old man’s brat?\"","\" And you’re a dumb motherfucker, \" Ling said. She rolled her neck. \" Come here.\"","He came. She met him!","Newly risen against a somewhat established Immensity, gold against dream, his sword against her legs, and every exchange shook the mountain!","Oh!","She was shallower than he was, a Dream Immensity only an hour old against a few Ages of gold, and she held him anyway, laughing and cursing and kicking until his armor rang like a struck bell. He fought like a man more surprised than serious.","Which left Noah, and the Hound!","It came at him across the cavern floor, and Noah decided to experiment. He let himself be afraid.","The fear rose and fed itself and poured into him as strength. Anger followed, hot and steady: at the Fiend for walking into his host’s home, at the Verdant Regard for her betrayal, at all of them for coming to take him like a parcel. It fed itself too. The more he felt, the more of him there was!","That was the Human in him!","The Hound’s jaws came down where he stood, and closed on an echo.","Noah had dreamed the space around himself into his own. Inside it, the Hound’s lunge arrived already spent, its jaws snapping shut on the place he had been a dream ago. Its paw landed slow and dull, its force bleeding away into the dream. Its Immensity tried to close on him again, and slid off a sky.","That was the Dreamer!","And every blow that broke against his dream shed fine grey residue, like sparks off a whetstone. Noah opened his mouth and drank it.","That was the Sovereign!","| Predation: residue of THE Hound of Thresholds.|","|Sap risen toward the First Bough: 26%.|","|Auto-Fusion: Authority of the Held Breath + Provenance of Order + residue of an Immense One’s reach.|","|Formed: Authority of the Unclosing Hand. That which tries to close upon you finds itself held open.|","...!","The Hound lunged again, and its jaws locked wide open in mid-bite, held by nothing. It wrenched free and backed away, its eyes narow.","Noah decided to test something else.","The Bow of the Ending Epoch dreamed itself into his hand. He drew, an arrow of compressed Epochs forming along the string, and loosed it into the Hound’s grey chest from ten paces.","It went in!","The hide around the wound withered, cracked, wore toward bone through a thousand Ages in an instant.","Then the Hound’s Immensity swallowed the Ages whole, as a calm sea swallows a stone. The hide filled back in, the scratch closed, and the Hound shook itself once and smiled with marvel!","|\" Wow! He might be the real deal! He is a bit weak, but this is definitely Immensity! How the hell is he displaying Immensity? I see why we want to kidnap him!\"|","...!","The words were heavy.","Noah lowered the bow. Killing it lay beyond him, for today.","\"It seems that Immensity is deep, \" he said. His voice boomed out grandly. \"I can see how deep. My eyes go down through you, Age after Age, and I can see that your bottom is very far, and that I cannot reach it.\"","He let the bow fade from his hand.","\"I do not need to reach it today. I only need you to understand that you cannot reach me either. And someday, your bottom will be in reach.\"","The Hound of Thresholds, which had hunted every opening in existence for longer than Noah’s whole species had existed, pulsed with wonder.","The Fiend stepped off the Thinker’s bead.","Immensity raged as the Thinker was swarmed on all sides, the Hound turning its attacks on him to keep him busy, and THE Sleepless Fiend walked toward Noah. With every step, the stone under his feet darkened into crimson gold, and the air he passed through grew warm and faintly sweet, as air does in a room that belongs to someone else.","Across the cavern, Ling and the Gilt Heir broke apart to watch.","Noah looked at the Fiend with his gold eyes, and this time, he looked all the way!","The tall figure in dark robes was only a skin on something enormous. Beneath it, the Fiend went down and out in every direction, a vastnes built entirely of eyes that had stayed open since their making. Each one watched a different place the Fiend had touched once and so owned forever: a city, a sea, a Dimension, a child asleep in a cot.","From the vastness ran threads, hundreds of thousands of them, each one down a lineage the Fiend had sired across the Ages, Descendants hanging from them like fruit from a vine. One ran toward the Krazhor-Nul. One had been cut, recently, its end hanging loose and bleeding.","Around his head rested a crown of chains, every link a promise someone had made to him and was bound to keep.","And everything near him, stone and air and light, was being rewritten into what he wished it to be, all the way down to what each thing was!","| THE Sleepless Fiend.|","|Profundity: Unknown.|","...!","The Fiend stopped an arm’s length away.","\" Osmont ,\" he said. \" That is what they call you, yes?\"","His voice was warm and pleased.","\" That was very well done. I may even change the course of plans and mission we were given here today.\"","He clasped his hands behind his back.","\" The Keepers of Existence have a seat open. I would like you to take it. You would have protection beyond anything this Legacy can offer, beyond anything the old man there can offer, dying as he is. You would have resources. Teachers. Every Gu and every Immense corpse you could wish to eat. And when the one who will open the door finally stands before it, you would stand at his side.\"","His countless eyes all turned toward Noah at once. \" You would be valued. Kept. Fed. You would be made grand. You may just have to...offer your heart.\"","...!","Noah looked at him.","\" No ,\" he said.","That was all.","The Fiend’s smile warmed.","\" Of course,\" he said.","He lifted a single finger and laid it, almost gently, on the edge of Noah’s dream.","Ownership flowed out of it!","Crimson gold bloomed outward from that one point like ink in still water. Star after star in Noah’s dream changed color, and he felt each one stop being his. The sky that had held the Hound’s hand and dreamed islands back together was becoming someone else’s, one light at a time!","HUUM!","Noah poured everything he had into that single point!","The Tree in his chest blazed, every ring and Branch and drop of Sap lit at once, and dream rushed out of him to meet the Fiend’s finger, tide against tide. A crimson gold star went blue-gold again. Another went crimson. Then back.","It was terrifying. He felt he could slip at any moment!","He held for an instant. Just an instant. Any longer, and he knew he would be crushed, and face his first death since his evolution!","A bead of purple fire slid between them!","It drifted into the space between the Fiend’s finger and Noah’s dream, burning steadily. The Thinker had still not risen. His eyes were still closed. One of his moons had simply decided to be there.","The Fiend withdrew his finger, unhurried, and regarded the bead with mild amusement, then the old man on his mat, then Noah.","The crimson gold drained out of the stars, and every one of them went blue-gold again.","Noah stood inside his dream, chest heaving, infinite emotions burning all through him.","He looked into the Fiend’s countless eyes, every one of them watchng him.","And he smiled!","It was an affirmation he wanted to make, that he could at leasy defend himself! Even if only for an instant!","At this time, far above them, through the mountain and the torn coat and Moriarty’s mist, the whole Legacy began to hum, and a brilliant light began heading their way!","The Thinker opened his weeping eyes and breathed out a calm sigh.","Finally, the help would be arriving!"]},{"number":5827,"title":"Chapter 5827: Chapter 5826: Immensity! IV","paragraphs":["The note rose, and rose, and THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity woke.","Noah felt it through the soles of his feet first. A deep vibration climbing up out of the mountain’s roots, out of the rivers below, out of the snow-buried floor of the whole Legacy. Then his gold eyes caught it, and he saw what Lucy had built.","It was a single thing!","The purple-gold rivers and the Existential Conduits rising out of them, the thousand Elsedimension Mountains with their monasteries and thrones and caverns, the Plain of Accord, the Firmament, the Keepers’ Roads winding between the peaks, the floor of snow beneath it all.","He had always seen them as parts of a place. They were parts of one body. An Immensity, woven into the shape of a home and laid down to sleep, so long ago that even the Immense who lived inside it had forgotten it was alive.","It had slept for Ages.","Now it was awake, and Noah could see who had woken it!","Deep in the Legacy’s heart, where every river and Conduit met, Sir Moriarty coiled around the center of everything with every tentacle he had. Green poison bled from every seam of him. His spectacles were cracked. He was hurt badly, in ways an Immense One should be spared. And he had reached the heart anyway, and laid himself across it, and called the Legacy up out of its sleep.","The Legacy answered him!","Obsidian gold came down on the Thinker’s mountain!","It poured out of every Conduit in the Legacy at once, all of them turning their light toward the mountain, and it came down through the torn purple coat in a single crushing tide. And it fell only on those who were strangers here!","The Rusted Matriarch’s rust peeled off her in long brown sheets, her bronze body groaning under the weight. The Gilt Heir dropped to one knee, his gold dimming to brass, his face slack with shock. And the Hound of Thresholds was hurled backward out of the cavern entirely, out through the torn coat and into the blizzard, its doorway eyes wide.","THE Verdant Regard’s body cracked down its whole length like dry bark splitting in a frost, green light bleeding from the seam.","On Noah, it fell like warm rain!","The Legacy’s waking Immensity had looked at him and counted him among its own.","On Ling, it fell like a hand on her hair. On the Thinker, it fell and was welcomed, and the purple fire on his orbiting beads flared brighter.","The Fiend stayed exactly where he stood.","He stood in the middle of the obsidian gold tide as it crashed down on him. He studied the light pouring through the torn coat!","The pressure on him was enough to grind mountains, and yet he stood as this fucker’s immensity was unfathomable! How the hell had Noah escaped his grasp before when Poona threatened them just with the Legacy behind her?!","He had been cautious enough that the name of THE Legacy of THE Acharya made him hesitate then, but here he was among those leading in its invasion. What changed?","As he thought about this...","The thrones descended!","They came down through the torn coat one after another, out of the obsidian gold, and each took a place around the cavern without a word.","Sir Moriarty came first, in person. Well, in octupus.","The octopus-headed visage had drawn down into a body Noah had seen before: tentacles, spectacles, a long dark coat. But the coat was soaked through with green, the tentacles trailed poison in long glowing threads, and one lens of his spectacels was split clean across. He was breathng hard. His crimson eyes were steady.","THE Ashen Cantor came behind him, cinders drifting off his robe, his mouth closed for once. THE Keeper of the Unbroken Vow, the chain of oaths coiled over one shoulder. THE Lantern of the Last Shore, faceless, his lamp held low. THE Hollow Choir, their ring of hollow faces drifting into place along the cavern’s ceiling, silent.","They took their places around the five invaders.","And then, one by one, they turned and looked at Noah.","Thry had sensed or seen the power Noah had displayed to rebuff an Immense One and even not crumbled completely under THE SLEEPLESS FIEND as they had questions!","Their eyes shone!","Moriarty’s shone most of all. Behind his cracked spectacles, the crimson eyes held something new to Noah: hope... and it was enormous!","Noah understood what Moriarty thought he was seeing. They were looking at him and seeing an answer to the shut door. A key. Something beyond the winter’s grip. Every one of them was more certain of it than they had been an hour ago.","The Thinker spoke quietly, for Noah’s ears alone.","|\" They see a key ,\"| he said, |\" because they have spent a long looking for one. Long before this Winter. All of us are immense, but we remain. Ultimately, we have been waiting for things that will never arrive because we needed to save ourselves and find our own way...not find someone else to open the door for us.\"|","WAA!","His beads drifted slowly around him, burning.","|\" As grand as you seem right, I still see a man who chose. It is the larger thing. And the rarer. The choice to choose...that is existence. All Civilizations chose. All ways choose. Existence is a series of...choices.\"|","Noah looked around the circle of thrones. Moriarty, the Cantor, the Keeper, the Lantern, the Choir.","He counted them again.","Where was Poona?","He always expected her to be with Moriarty!","Moriarty’s crimson eyes moved away from his, toward the torn coat and the blizzard beyond it.","In the middle of the cavern, THE Sleepless Fiend lifted one hand to his brow in a small, courtly salute. To the Thinker first. Then to Moriarty. And last of all, unhurried, to Noah.","The Fiend lowered his hand from his brow, and smiled at the circle of thrones as though they had all just shared a good meal.","\" Well ,\" he said. \" Things did not go entirely according to plan, but I have learned a great deal that I can now report. It seems that what the great Lucy left behind...is not so untouchable as you all had everyone believe. I felt a sense of shame after this name alone made me not act not long ago, and I can be considered responsible for letting something slip past me.\"","HUUM!","He turned his face toward Moriarty. The obsidian gold was still pouring down on him, grinding, endless, and he stood in it with his robes perfectly still.","\"I will come back when the snow is deeper, old friend. It will not be long now. And when I do, I think you will be more reasonable.\"","His countless eyes, behind his face, all seemed to settle on the split lens of Moriarty’s spectacles. \"I left you something on one of your mountains. Where my daughter was broken. A small gift, for old times’ sake.\"","He paused.","\"I hope you will remember the taste of the Verdant Regard’s tea every time you look at it.\"","Moriarty’s tentacles went perfectly still.","The Fiend withdrew.","He simply stepped backward through the torn purple coat, and the cavern’s stone and air and light, one by one, went back to being what they had been. The torches lost their crimson gold and burned purple again. The prayer mats faded to their old dull color. Even the snow that had turned to face him turned away and fell.","THE Verdant Regard went with him. Her cracked body bled green as she backed toward the gap, and her eyes stayed on the Thinker to the very last, wet and furious and full of a grief that had nowhere left to go as she blamed him for the fact that they weren’t able to get Noah.","She also gazed hatefully at Noah as she sent him a message...","|\" Why the fuck do you portray Immensity now? You were simply playing along this whole time? This power could have entirely crushed my daughter- why push her to form Immensity for her to simply be severed?! Why?!\"|","...!","Noah’s eyes remained cold as he didn’t even spare this woman a reply.","How the fuck was he to blame?","He ignored her as she disappeared!","The Rusted Matriarch followed, rust trailing from her. The Gilt Heir dragged himself up off his knee, glared once at Ling, and went. Out in the blizard, the Hound of Thresholds was already loping away across the Legacy, grey and fast, without looking back.","Then they were gone alongside all Immense Ones who had invaded as if they all had received a collective order to withdraw!","The Legacy breathed out!","Noah felt it everywhere at once through his gold eyes. The walled domains came down. The Existential Conduits that had risen into pillars sank slowly back into their rivers, light dimming to its usual purple-gold.","Moriarty’s obsidian-gold mist lifted from the mountains in long drifting curtains, and the golden spheres of foreign Immensity that had been frozen inside those walls truly tore loose all at once and fled. Dozens of them, streaking up through the cracked sky and out of the Legacy like sparks leaving a fire!","The cracks in the sky remained!","Snow fell through them, heavier than before.","| The incursion into THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity has ended.|","|Immense grasps rebuffed: 2.|","|Immense residue devoured: 4.|","|Sap risen toward the First Bough: 29%.|","|Judgment Debt: 2.|","...!","Twenty-nine percent!","The Hound’s residue, the Immense grasps turned aside, the Fiend’s own finger held off at the edge of his dream: the Tree had drunk all of it and grown. He had come out of a cavern full of Immense Ones stronger than he went in!","And beside him, the Thinker was looking at the cracks in the sky with his weeping eyes open.","|\"I truly dislike the Fiend. He leaves gifts, \"| the Thinker said quietly , |\"as other beings leave footprints. Wherever he has walked, something is left behind for someone to find.\"|","His beads hung still. |\"It is never kind.\"|","Ling looked from her father to Noah and back, her white eyes narrowing. She asked what gift. The Thinker gave her no answer.","He was looking at Moriarty.","The old scholar had stood frozen since the Fiend spoke. He stood among the other thrones with his tentacles hanging limp, green poison dripping slowly from them onto the stone, and his crimson eyes fixed on the place in the coat where the Fiend had gone.","Footsteps came up the mountain path outside!","Quick, uneven, a little too fast for an old man’s knees. Verys came in through the cavern mouth with snow on his shoulders and his face grey. He bowed to the Thinker. He bowed to the thrones. Then he came straight to Noah, and Noah saw his hands were shakng.","The Keepers’ network had carried it, Verys told him.","Every servant in the Legacy had it now, passed mountain to mountain through the Conduits while the war was still going. What had happened in Moriarty’s study.","When the Fiend had opened the Verdant Regard’s dome, when the poison had come blooming out of Moriarty and the two of them had moved to finish him, Poona had stepped between them.","She had already taken her true form. The vast slime of every color, filling half the study, her one great eye open. She had put herself between Moriarty and the two oldest enemies in the room, and she had burned her own Immensity to hold them. All of it. Every Age of it.","She had poured it out into a wall of living color that neither the Fiend nor the Verdant Regard could get through, and she had held that wall while Moriarty fought the poison off and dragged himself down into the heart of the Legacy to wake it.","She had held it for exactly as long as it took.","Beside Noah, Ling had gone white. Her hands came up over her mouth, and her white eyes went to her father. The Thinker’s beads hung motionless in the air around him, every one of them dark, their purple fire banked low for the first time since the Fiend had walked into the cavern.","Verys stopped there. The rest needed no saying.","Across the cavern, Moriarty reached up with one trembling tentacle and took off his cracked spectacles.","Noah stood.","The Tree in his chest had gone very quiet. The Human in him roared!","\" Where is she? \" he asked.","Verys looked at him as he answered in a low voice.","\" The Fiend moved her corpse to The Firmament, Sir,\" he said. \" On the Plain of Accord.\""]},{"number":5828,"title":"Chapter 5828: Chapter 5827: Legacy’s Son!","paragraphs":["The Plain of Accord lay under a deep fresh fall of snow, and in its center, the snow was grey.","Noah came down onto the Firmament’s broad shoulder with Ling at his side and the Thinker’s great kneeling shape descending behind them. Golden clouds still hung in their ring above the Plain, every throne on them vacant, snow gathering on the seats.","And at the Plain’s center lay Poona.","What was left of her filled a hollow in the snow as wide as a village. The vast gleaming slime of every color that had sat on Moriarty’s table eating his pastries had been torn open, long ragged rips running through her from edge to edge, and along every one of them, crimson and violet and gold and blue had gone to grey, as though someone had dragged claws through a painting and taken the paint with them. Her one enormous eye was dimmed to the color of old ice and cracked straight down its middle.","The Fiend had taken his time over killing her!","Many had already gathered. Moriarty stood at the edge of the hollow with his cracked spectacles in one tentacle, green still bleeding from his seams, the Legacy’s Immense Ones around him. Beyond them, in widening rings, stood Progeny and Provenance Lifeforms from every mountain, Keepers in their simple robes, Achilles with Rose wrapped in his cloak and the frost on his shoulders staying frozen, and hundreds more Noah did not know, all looking at the grey thing at the center of everything.","Behind him, the Thinker set his great knees down at the edge of the Plain and bowed his head. The last time he had truly left his mountain was a long time ago. He had left it now, for this.","And in the periphery, the auras of other Immense Ones watched with heavy eyes. A few of them turned toward Noah as he came down, and a few of them were hard!","Then a voice from somewhere in the skies.","|\" Was he not their focus?\"|","Another voice. |\" The Fiend and others walked into the old man’s mountain for him. Poona was merely collateral for their plans.\"|","...!","Noah heard every word calmly.","He walked to the edge of the hollow, passing close by Moriarty, and looked down at Poona. She had saved him once before. He felt it, sharp and sentimental!","With the Gold Without Pupils, he looked at her across every branch his eyes could follow, every way the ambush in Moriarty’s study might have gone.","He dreamt!","In some, the dome held longer. In some, the poison bloomed faster. In some, Moriarty moved first, or the Fiend did, or the Verdant Regard hesitated at the last.","In every one, Poona stepped forward!","She took her true form, filled half the study, and burned her Immensity to a wall of living color. And in every single one, as the wall went up, she was smiling!","On the outside, Noah’s face stayed still. His gold eyes stayed calm. But the Human in him pulsed as anger and grief came pouring up through the crack, and kept pouring.","| You have better understood the emotion side of your humanity as with your evolution, your emotions grow infinitely as the happier, loving, angry, lustful, fearful...any extreme of emotions you experience will experience infinite growth and only further elevate your power.|","...!","Noah’s eyes pulsed as he looked closer, past the drained colors and the cracked eye, down into the deepest place in what was left of her, as he had once looked into the Warden’s chest.","Something was still there!","It was faint, almost nothing, a flicker far down in the grey. Every Age of her Immensity had been burned to hold that wall. But at the very bottom, something was still unfinished.","A dream.","Poona was dead. Her dream lingered, faint, and still alive!","Noah walked down into the hollow, past the torn grey edges of the slime, while the whole Legacy watched in silence. Moriarty lifted his head. The Thinker’s beads went still.","He knelt beside her, laid his stellar dark hand flat on the grey, torn surface, and closed his gold eyes.","Under his palm, the slime was cold, and still, and far heavier than it looked.","His dream went down first, soft and blue-gold, sinking into the grey mass as warm water sinks into snow. It found every place where her Immensity had been burned out and scorched clean. And at the very bottom, where the last flicker waited, it closed around it, gently, and drew it up.","Poona’s dream came into his hand!","A kitchen. Warm, cluttered, bright with lamplight, somewhere deep inside the Legacy in an Age long past.","Pastries cooling on every surface, on the shelves, on the windowsill, piled on plates along a table far too long for any kitchen to hold. Flour in the air. Noise everywhere. Every Immense One she had ever talked to sat around that table at once, arguing and laughing and reaching across one another for the last of the honey cakes that burned with Immensity.","Moriarty, younger, his spectacles whole, trying to read at the table and failing. The Ashen Cantor singing badly on purpose. The Keeper of the Unbroken Vow pretending not to eat. And at the head of the table, an empty chair, carved and plain, with a cup of tea set in front of it, still steaming, waiting for someone to come home and sit down.","Lucy’s chair!","That was what Poona had dreamed. All of them, at one table, fed and loud and safe, and the chair kept ready.","Noah held the dream against his chest and carried it down past his skin and his constellations of dreams, down to the Tree. He laid the kitchen at the base of the endless trunk, where the first ring glowed, and dreamed it into...Immensity. As he had dreamed Ling’s. Through his own Dream, past the door, without asking the door’s permission.","The dream began to grow. Its lamplight deepened. Its warmth went down, layer under layer, Immensity filling it from below like a well filling with water.","The sky over the Plain of Accord split open!","BOOM!","Obsidian gold poured through a crack that ran from one horizon to the other, straight through the ring of empty thrones, down onto the snow, onto Noah kneeling in the hollow with his hand on a corpse and a dream cupped against his chest.","A voice only he could hear boomed out!","| How dare you.|","|The dead are counted. The dead stay counted.|","|You would dare to dream what existence has ended?|","...!","It landed on his back like the weight of every Age at once!","His knees drove into the snow. His crown of radiance flared, guttered, flared again. The constellations of dreams under his skin blazed and dimmed and blazed, and the obsidian gold ground down on him, searching for the place where he would let go.","He held the dream!","Bent over it as a man holds a child in a burning house, his whole body a roof, he let every ounce of the Judgment fall on him, and THE One Foundation took it and built it into floor beneath him. He kept it from the kitchen. He kept it from the chair!","Around the Plain, nobody moved, for what they perceived was different from what Noah percieved!","The Judgment pressed down one last time, then withdrew, and the sky closed behind it.","| The Judgment has been withstood.|","|Judgment Debt: 3. Existence will remember.|","...!","Noah raised his head, snow settled on his white-gold hair, and laid the dream back at the bottom of the torn slime, where he had found it. It sank out of his hand and settled into the place where her Immensity had burned out.","Then he spoke to her. His voice was quiet. It carried across the whole Plain anyway!","\" Dream once more ,\" Noah said.","He kept his hand on her.","\" Under my gaze and brilliance... dream.\"","...!","The corpse buzzed!","A single deep vibration rose from the bottom, where the dream had settled, and then the color came back, one slow wave of it rolling outward through every drained stripe and every torn edge.","At the center, the great eye shudderd.","The crack down its middle sealed from the bottom up. The dull ice warmed. And the eye opened, clear and bright and fully awake, and fine glowing threads ran out of the depths behind it, across the snow, into Noah’s chest, into his Tree.","A new Immensity rose out of Poona!","It rose over the Plain, smelling faintly of honey cakes and lamplight, and every Immense One on the Plain of Accord felt it!","| Kin Evolution: Poona has established a Dream Immensity.|","|Sap risen toward the First Bough: 38%.|","...!","The slime gathered itself and shrank, until a small round shape sat in the snow in front of Noah, gleaming with every color, its one great eye blinking up at the gathered Legacy.","Moriarty and others showed extremely complex expressions as many eyes turned over and locked onto Noah!","What had he just done?! He revived...an Immensity?","Who among them could do this?!","...!","As for Poona, she turned to Noah and smiled brilliantly, and through her Dream Immensity he sensed her about to kneel to him before everyone. He quickly and sternly sent her a command not to!","She went very quiet.","Moriarty bent and looked at Poona with wonder. He then looked at Noah for a long time across the snow as he also sensed the somber gazes of many others, with other Immense ones showing hungry and interested looks by the dozens!","So he raised his voice, and spoke to the whole Plain.","\"THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity,\" Moriarty said, \" has never named a Son. Not once, since Lucy founded it. She left directions that if and when the time came when the nights grew long and all doors closed, someone would have to be named THE Legacy’s Son. Someone who may be able to gaze past the treachery of the long cold and ensure the Legacy shines bright...till the doors are open once more!\"","HUUM!","His crimson eyes stayed on Noah. \" Before this winter grows any longer, I would like to propose THE Legacy’s Son.\"","...!","THE Legacy’s Son!","Nobody on the Plain spoke.","At its edge, THE Thinker at the End of Existence knelt in the snow with his beads still, and smiled his fierce almost-smile, and said nothing at all.","The snow fell on the Plain of Accord, heavier than before. It fell on the empty thrones and the gathered Legacy, on a small bright slime blinking in the hollow, on a Legacy beginning to prepare for the long winter ahead.","And it fell on the man its oldest scholar had just proposed to name THE Legacy’s Son as he was feeling his rising dream after doing the unthinkable!"]},{"number":5829,"title":"Chapter 5829: Chapter 5828: Order! I","paragraphs":["The silence on the Plain of Accord lasted until Moriarty’s Immensity pulsed.","His voice carried to every one of them. They were to return to their mountains. The Immense Ones of the Legacy would hold a council, and what came next would be decided there.","The crowd broke apart at once, and Achilles lifted a hand to Noah across the snow before leading Rose away. Overhead, the thrones began to fill!","Poona looked at him before the eyes of other Immense Ones as she said...","\"I have to thank someone for my return! No worries, I will keep him safe.\"","Her golden brilliance flared and wrapped around her and Noah as they both disappeared, seemingly to Poona’s Existential Immense Domain.","But that was not the case!","—","THE Existential Dreaming Origin Domain had kept growing since the evolution. New ridges, new valleys, Gigaparsecs of golden blue brilliance.","On a hill above the river, Ruination’s and THE Infiniverse’s cocoons still glowed, still closed.","Noah gazed at Poona on the grass.","She had shrunk into a little golden slime, round and bubbly, flecked with every color. She wobbled a few times to find her balance, then bowed so deeply her eye nearly touched the ground, and thanked him for resuscitating her dream.","She had saved him a few days ago, she pointed out, and now he had saved her, and held her Immensity in his hands besides. As his senior, no less!","\"Now I feel like a baby Immense One again, wow!\" she added, mostly to herself.","Noah let her bounce for a moment.","Then he sat down cross-legged in front of her and started asking questions!","He had plenty. A whole Legacy of Immense Ones had just fought a small war, and he understood almost nothing about what they actually were. Poona was the first of them who looked happy to explain.","First, he asked her how Immense Ones differed from one another.","According to Poona, they differed in almost every way that mattered. Immensity took the shape of whatever a being had been carrying when it went through the door.","Next, he asked her how to measure them. His gold eyes could look down into an Immense One, but past a certain point, they simply found no bottom.","Poona told him the Immense had a word for that: Profundity. How far down a being’s Immensity went, rather than how high it had climbed, and how much it had carried through the Ages to get there. She explained it in her own cheerful, rambling way as...she loved talking a bit too much.","As she talked, Noah’s eyes worked. He laid her words over everything he had seen in the Thinker’s cavern, every Immense One he had read, every bottom he had failed to find.","And his existence answered with prompts that simplified her convoluted explanations!","| Profundity of Immensity.|","|The measure of what an Immense One has carried, and how far down its Immensity reaches.|","|Newly Risen. Immensity freshly established. Shallow, loud, and still learning its own shape. A Newly Risen One can be read to the bottom by a keen enough eye.|","|Known to you: Ling, THE Dancer in the Boundless Dream. Poona, reborn.|","|Established. Immensity that has carried Ages. Its bottom can be glimpsed, but lies far below. Most who sit on thrones are Established.|","|Known to you: THE Gilt Heir. THE Hound of Thresholds. Many of the Legacy’s thrones.|","|Ancient. Immensity that has carried more Ages than most lifeforms can imagine. Its bottom cannot be seen. Its presence alone changes existence nearby.|","|Known to you: Sir Moriarty. THE Sleepless Fiend. THE Thinker at the End of Existence. THE Verdant Regard. THE Rusted Matriarch.|","|Unfathomable. Immensity whose Profundity cannot be measured, even by the Ancient.|","|Known to you: none.|","|Beyond. ?????|","...!","Noah read the list twice.","The Thinker, who had held four Immense Ones at bay without standing up, was Ancient. The Fiend, whose single finger had nearly stolen his dream, was Ancient.","And above them sat a whole tier he had yet to meet.","Unfathomable. Then Beyond, with nothing written under it at all!","| Your own Profundity: ?????|","|Others perceive in you the Immensity of a weak Newly Risen One.|","To the Immense, he looked like a fresh, weak Immense One standing where a days-old Root should have been. Wrong, but useful. He would let them keep thinking it!","Then he asked Poona about THE Legacy’s Son.","Here she went serious, briefly.","According to her, the title was a spiritual pillar for the whole Legacy: the successor to everything Lucy had left behind. Lucy had named no one. She had left directions, sealed for Ages, about when one should be named. And whoever became THE Legacy’s Son gained access to an Immense Domain that nobody had ever entered, left by Lucy specifically for them. Even Moriarty had yet to set foot inside.","Then she squinted up at him.","\" Do I have to call you Master now, since you hold my Dream Immensity?\" Poona asked. She thought about it for exactly one heartbeat. \" Well, I don’t care! Master, then.\"","Since his power showed itself at the level of a weak Immense One when he was supposed to have only just formed his Root, she went on, most of the Legacy’s Immense would likely accept him.","\" We will see! \" she finished, and smiled brilliantly.","Noah looked at her truly.","Her Dream Immensity was shallow, a single warm layer of lamplight with only the beginnings of Profundity beneath its floor. Under it ran the faint memory of everything she had once been, Ages of old quiet Immensity, burned away and remembered. Bright threads ran from the bottom of her into his Tree.","| Poona.|","|THE Dreaming Hearth.|","|Dream Immensity. Kin.|","|Profundity: Newly Risen. It remembers being Ancient.|","...!","THE Dreaming Hearth. It suited her!","Noah stood up and looked out over his Domain as he sensed his own existence.","The gain were Sap from 14% to 38%. Two new Authorities, the Held Breath and the Unclosing Hand. One Immense grasp rebuffed outright, one held at bay. Poona revived as Kin. A proposed title.","The negatives of it all were Judgment Debt up to 3. The Fiend’s full attention. The Verdant Regard’s hatred.","And the most importantly...without the Thinker, Moriarty, and Poona, he would have been captured today. Plainly and simply captured.","He disliked that intensely!","Being saved was a fine thing when it came. Planning on it was another matter. So the answer was simple. Grow until nobody needed to protect him.","He was a dreamer, a sovereign, and a human. The sovereign in him would take this Legacy’s Son title grandly, walk into Lucy’s sealed Domain, and see exactly what she had left behind. If it could be learned, he would learn it. If it could be eaten, he would eat it.","But titles alone would leave his Tree hungry.","What had carried him to his first evolution? A dead Immense One’s corpse and an Ergosphere full of Roots. So where would he find more things like that?","The answer came at once!","THE Undersnow!","Dead Immense Ones. Kept First Lifeforms. Beings at Immensity, in abundance. A Floor already cleared, and a rift north of it standing open and unguarded, leading down into THE Evergrave. Down there were the Caretaker in her chains, the secrets of the Long Night, and things old enough to remember the First Sundering.","And, quite possibly, a great deal to eat!","He turned his gold eyes toward the far edge of his Domain, toward the cold waiting beyond it.","\" Existence is vast,\" Noah said, \" and full of terrors...\"","It truly was as to prepare, he had to properly understand himself!","So he sat down cross-legged on a hill in THE Existential Dreaming Origin Domain, with Poona bouncing on the grass beside him, and turned his gold eyes inward.","The first question was simple. Could his own Tree count what existence had given up on?","He dreamed that it could, and his existence began to buzz!","| Existence counts what it can write. Its count of you broke at nine hundred and ninety-nine.|","|Your Tree measures you differently: by how far your Dream can reach, and how much of that reach it can command.|","|These are the Orders of the Dream.|","...!","Noah leaned forward.","| Order I. Your Dream reaches across many Dimensions and facets of existence at once, and commands the power within them.|","|Order II. Your Dream can reach across the whole domain of a Legacy and Dream without other’s knowledge: countless Dimensions, and every space between them. All of Order I becomes a single grain within it.|","|Order III. Your Dream gains the capability to reach across an entire stratum of existence, Undefined Gaps, the whole of THE Infinite Carcosa, or the whole of THE Source Lands.|","|Order IV. Your Dream reaches across every stratum existence can perceive, layered together as one.|","|Order V. Your Dream reaches beneath existence: THE Undersnow, THE Evergrave, and the layers of cold beneath the cold further underneath.|","|Order VI. Your Dream reaches across every cycle of existence, back past THE First Sundering.|","|Order VII. Your Dream reaches outside existence.|","|Order ?????|","|Within each Order, the measure after the point is how fully you command it. At I.0, an attribute has only just entered the first Order. At I.9, it presses against the second. Every tenth is a true step in what you can do.|","...!"]},{"number":5830,"title":"Chapter 5830: Chapter 5829: Order! II","paragraphs":["Noah looked over everything thoroughly!","Each rung swallowed the one beneath it whole, and above all of them sat the undersides of existence, the cycles of the Ages, and the outside.","He smiled.","Then the Tree measured him.","| Noah Osmont. THE True Human Emperor. THE Osmontian, THE Dreaming Human Origin.|","| VERITAS: Order I.4. What you dream holds true across many Dimensions near you, and thins toward the far edges of your reach.|","|PROVENANCE: Order I.6. What you make of yourself draws on more than half the power your Order can command, and owes nothing for it.|","|POTENTIA: Infinite. No Order contains it.|","|PONDUS: Order I.3. Your weight bends a third of your reach around you.|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: Order I.1. Your hold on fate and narrative has barely entered the first Order.|","|Profundity: ?????|","...!","First Order, every one of them!","So where did the Immense sit on this ladder?","He looked at Poona, and his existence answered.","| Measured against the Orders: a Newly Risen Immensity commonly reaches upper bounds of Order I in its strongest attribute. The Ancient reach far higher. Their full measure lies beyond your present sight.|","\"Hmm...\" He nodddd at this.","Then he looked at everything else!","Over his existence he had gathered a great deal: Core Capabilities, Authorities, Provenances, techniques, Records, a whole system in his Tree. It worked, but it was cluttered.","He was THE Dreaming Human Origin now. Human, Dreamer, Sovereign.","So everything he had should belong to one of the three.","He reached into himself and began to sort!","It was strange work and very satsifying. Each capability, when he touched it, leaned toward one of the three parts of him as naturally as water runs downhill.","His existence logged it as he went.","| Streamlining your existence.|","|THE Human.|","|What you feel, what you speak, and whom you hold.|","|Your emotions: endless, every extreme growing without limit and feeding your power.|","|Core Capability IV: THE Living Grammar. Core Capability VIII: THE Sanguine Covenant. Egos.|","|Kin: Ling, THE Dancer in the Boundless Dream. Poona, THE Dreaming Hearth. Cocoons yet to open.|","|THE Dreaming Origin.|","|What you dream becomes true.|","|Core Capability I: THE Dream Without a Far Wall. Core Capability II: THE Sovereign of the Lived Hour. Core Capability III: THE Waking Decree. THE Gold Without Pupils. THE Endless Waking. THE Vigil That Wished to Rise.|","|THE Sovereign.|","|What you take, what you build, and what you rule.|","|Core Capability V: THE Rendered Design. Core Capability VI: THE Tide-Crowned Protagonist. Core Capability VII: THE Unkneeling Chill. THE Bow of the Ending Epoch. Authority of the Held Breath. Authority of the Unclosing Hand. Provenances of Ending, Order, and Stillness. Records of an Immense One. THE Feast That Seals: Predation, Auto-Fusion, Judgment, and the Branches of your Tree.|","|Beneath all three: THE One Foundation, Dialetheic Infinity.|","|Streamlining complete. What was many is arranged as one.|","...!","Noah let out a long breath.","Every power he owned now sat in its propper room, ready to his hand.","That left one thing unfinished.","He had given two great gifts on this road: Ling, carried through a sealed door inside his own Dream and made a Dream Immensity, and Poona, drawn out of her own corpse as a last flicker and dreamed back to life. Through all of it, THE Tide That Owes Nothing had not given.","It held weight sitting in the deepest part of THE Tide-Crowned Protagonist, waiting for him to ask.","So he asked!","| THE Tide That Owes Nothing has kept count of your giving.|","|Given: a Dream Immensity, to Ling. Given: a Dream Immensity and a second life, to Poona.|","|These were gifts no lifeform has given before. They were given with thought, at great cost, to those you hold dear.|","|THE Tide answers in full, and its answer exceeds your Order.|","...!","Exceeds his Order?","The sky of the Domain darkened, and the first one rose over the hills!","It came up slowly, as a sun comes up, vast and round and gold. As it climbed, Noah saw that it was a shell. A great hollow sphere woven of dream, thread over thread, shining blue and gold, and inside it, at its heart, something burned.","Dreams. Countless dreams, every one a light, gathered into a single blazing core: the dreams of a whole civilization, then another, then thousands, peoples across countless Dimensions all sleeping at once and dreaming into this one place. A child dreaming of the sea. A smith dreaming of the perfect blade.","A city dreaming of its own tomorrow. All of it pouring into the core, and the shell around it catching every scrap of their light and holding it, harnessing it, turning it into power.","A sun made of a civilization’s sleep, and a shell built to drink it.","| Loot obtained: THE Dreaming Shell of Countless Sleeping Peoples.|","|A sphere woven around the gathered dreams of countless civilizations, harnessing the whole of their dreaming as power.|","|Born of the dream you carried through a sealed door. What opened for one, now gathers from countless.|","|Its reach spans the whole weavings of a Legacy. It is of the second Order.|","...!","Second Order!","His whole existence leaned toward it. Every attribute he had sat on the first rung, and this reached a whole Legacy’s breadth.","The second one rose beside it.","This one rose out of warmth. Lamplight first, spilling across the river of light, gold and steady, and the smell of honey and baking bread rolling over the hills so thick that Poona’s eye went wide and wet. The lamplight gathered, and rose, and became a second sun beside the first.","But this sun was made of hearths.","Noah could see them in it, millions of them: the fire under every family’s pot, the lamp left burning in every window for someone coming late, every table where people gathered to eat and argue and be safe. All that warmth burned in a single sphere, and around it turned a shell of woven dream, keeping it.","A whole people’s dream of home, harnessed.","| Loot obtained: THE Hearth-Sun of the Kept Tables.|","|A sun formed of the warmth of every hearth across a civilization’s countless homes, and the dream of a home that waits for each who has not yet returned.|","|Born of the life you dreamed back from death. What returned to one table, now burns at a million.|","|Its reach spans the whole weavings of a Legacy. It is of the second Order.|","...!","Noah stood up.","Two Second Order suns hung over his Domain, and every star in his sky had dimmed around them.","He felt something rise in his chest.","Greed, first. Pure and bright and shameless. He wanted them! He wanted both of them, and everything like them, every sleeping people’s dreams and every hearth’s warmth in every civilization across existence!","His Tyranny and his Quintessence also rose. The core of him. They looked at the two suns and knew, plainly, that they belonged inside him.","| Greed: risen, without end.|","|Tyranny: risen, without end.|","|Quintessence: risen, without end.|","|Your emotions elevate your power.|","...!","He opened his mouth.","The blue-gold brilliance inside it looked up at the two suns, and the event horizons turned, and he pulled. The Dreaming Shell came down first, its woven threads stretching into long ribbons, the blazing dreams of countless peoples streaming after them like a river of sparks. Then the Hearth-Sun, unwinding into lamplight, the warmth of a million homes pouring down out of the sky and into him in a long gold flood.","His Tree drank!","The dreams of the sleeping peoples went into the truth of him and the weave of his fate. The hearths went into his weight and the part of him that generated from itself. His constellations blazed until they lit the whole hill, and the sky of the Domain, emptied of its two suns, burned brighter than before.","| Devoured: THE Dreaming Shell of a Thousand Sleeping Peoples.|","|Devoured: THE Hearth-Sun of the Kept Tables.|","|Second Order loot integrated by a first Order existence. Your attributes surge toward the second rung.|","|Sap risen toward the First Bough: 53%.|","|VERITAS: Order I.4 to Order I.8.|","|PROVENANCE: Order I.6 to Order I.9. Knocking on the doors of Order II|","|PONDUS: Order I.3 to Order I.8.|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: Order I.1 to Order I.5.|","|POTENTIA: Infinite.|","...!","Noah read the numbers, and laughed out loud.","Provenance at I.9, pressing against the second rung, with Veritas and Pondus close behind. He could feel the next Order above him now, close enough to touch.","He wanted it. He wanted all of it!","Poona was staring at him with her one great eye very round.","\" Master ,\" she said slowly, \" Were you a slime before? Your hunger and devouring almost seems grander than mine. We can test this by seeing who can devour Dimensions the fastest...\"","...!","She said some ridiculous things as he didn’t reply.","His existence only buzzed as he probed regarding The Judgments and the capability that called forth what looked like a tribulation from existence everytime he used it.","|A clarification, on the Branches of your Tree.|","|A Branch grows only when your Tree itself grows beyond what existence allows, and survives the Judgment for it.|","|When you stand within a Judgment for another, as for Ling’s rising or Poona’s return, the Judgment falls on you and is counted in your Debt. The growth is theirs. No Branch of yours grows from it.|","Okay! It didn’t answer too much, but okay!","He looked at the whole of himself one last time, sorted and counted.","First Order, every attribute, Potentia aside. Three umbrellas. One Tree, one ring lit, Sap at fifty-three percent, a single Branch with an Unsealing on it, and a Judgment Debt of three.","It was a beginning, and only that. The Ancient Ones he had met sat a little above. They had lived longer than him as that was fine.","That meant there was a great deal left to eat!","Noah stood and brushed the dream-grass off his knees. Beside him, Poona stopped bouncing and looked up.","Noah turned toward the far edge of his Domain, toward the threads that ran down out of him into THE Undersnow, toward the frozen dark of the Basal Floor and the rift that split it open in the north.","There was much to be done!"]},{"number":5831,"title":"Chapter 5831: Chapter 5830: Purpose!","paragraphs":["A part of Noah slipped quietly out of his Domain and into the Dream Engine.","He had no particular reason for it. Poona was busy bouncing around his hills, trying to taste the river of light. The cocoons on the hill were still closed. And the rest of him was already turning toward the Basal Floor and the rift. But somewhere between all of that, a thought had surfaced, and he had followed it.","He wanted to talk to someone!","Out of every dreamer sleeping on the golden shore, one name had come to mind.","He stepped into Bob’s dream.","—","It was full of Wheels!","Dead ones. Countless dead Wheels of Existence, hanging in a grey sky that went on forever. Every one of them was broken. Spokes snapped. Rims crakced through. Hubs crumbled to calcified dust.","And every one of them was trying to rebuild itself!","A spoke would drift back toward its hub and fit itself into place. A shard of rim would find another shard and fuse. For a moment, a Wheel would look almost whole, turning slowly, light flickering across its rim where life might once have been. Then a crack would race across it, and it would come apart again, and the pieces would drift, and begin again.","Over and over. Thousands of them, as far as the eye could see. Building, breaking, building.","Noah stood among them for a while and watched.","He knew this dream. Once, he had stood on the Calcified Wheels of the Null Cradle once, beside Thauron’s shadow, and looked down at a tentacled thing that had lost everything. He knew which Wheel had broken first for Bob.","At the center of the dream, a cocoon of hazy blue-gold light hung among the drifting spokes, glowing softly. Bob’s. Like every other Kin in the Dream Engine, still closed, still changing slowly.","Noah reached out and touched it.","He poured a little of himself into it. Just a little, enough to say: hurry up.","| Kin recognized: Bob.|","|Kin Evolution accelerated by your will.|","...!","The cocoon brightened, then shuddered, then split down its middle like a seed pod in summer!","A figure stepped out!","It was humanoid, mostly. A round bald head, silver shading into gold, smooth and gleaming like a polished pebble. A body that stood upright, broad-shouldered and easy. But where arms and legs should have been, there were tentacles, long and supple and silver-gold, curling and uncurling lazily as they found their balance. And in the round face, two eyes like singularities, dark and deep and faintly glowing, looking out at the dream with mild surprise.","Something burned in his chest. Obsidian and violet, slow and wild, the colors of a storm given shape.","| Kin Evolution: Bob has emerged first among your Kin.|","|Root formed: THE Khaotic Chorionic Gonadotropin. Root of Khaos.|","|Saturation toward Immensity: 9%. The road to his Immensity is long.|","...!","Bob flexed a tentacle. Then another. He looked down at himself, at the violet storm turning in his chest, and then up, at the man standing among his broken Wheels.","His singularity eyes squinted.","\"Now this is rare,\" Bob said. \" A visit from the big guy himself?\"","He tilted his round head. \"What brought you to my dream?\"","Noah shrugged.","\"I just felt like talking to someone,\" he said. \"And for some reason, you came to mind, Little Bobby.\"","Bob stared at him for a moment.","Then he laughed and shook his gleaming head!","Clouds began to form around them!","They came out of Noah without him asking, soft and golden, drifting up between the broken Wheels and gathering in loose piles, as clouds gather on a lazy afternoon. Noah lowered himself onto one and sat back against it, stretching out his legs, and looked up.","Above them, the grey sky of Bob’s dream began to change. Noah’s dreams leaked into it as warmth leaks into a cold room. Stars came out between the dead Wheels, blue and gold. A faint shape of a great Tree glimmered for a moment far overhead, its trunk climbing out of sight, and faded. A golden-blue panda drifted past on a cloud, yawning, and disolved into mist.","Bob watched the panda go by with one eyebrow raised, or the place an eyebrow would be.","\"Your dreams are...as grand as ever,\" he said.","\"Mmm.\"","Bob coiled himself onto a golden cloud of his own, tentacles tucked under him, and settled in. For a while, both of them stayed quiet. They simply sat there among the Wheels and the clouds, two old enemies on a quiet afternoon.","It had been weeks, Noah thought.","Or it had been Ages. Telling the difference had grown hard. Time felt different to him now. It ran in periods rather than in a line. It sat around him in periods, like rooms in a house he could walk between: the room where he had first met this creature, the room where they had fought, the room on the Middle Wheel Platform, the room where he had reached into a broken father’s life and pulled his daughter out of it. All of them were still there. All of them had led here.","Noah let the clouds drift.","When Bob spoke again, his voice had changed.","\"I...did everything I did for my daughter,\" he said. \"It was not an excuse for all the ones who died while I sought to save her. I know that. I carry that.\"","His singularity eyes stayed on the broken Wheels, building and breaking, building and breaking. \"But this is what we do. Fathers do everything they can for their children.\"","He turned his round head toward Noah.","\"You have two now,\" Bob said. \"And your Son is even messing around with my Daughter...\"","A slow smile spread across his face.","\"Hah. Is that why you came to me? Do you now consider me your in-law?\"","He laughed, delighted with himself.","\"Haha. We have come far...\"","Noah tipped his head back against the cloud and smiled at the stars.","They had. They truly had!","He remembered the old Bob. A tentacled monster following the being who had crushed his own Wheel because that was the only road left that led toward his child. He remembered looking at that monster and thinking: pitiful. Noble, tragically so, and pitiful. A man held up by a single thread of regret.","And he remembered the day he had finally reached into that thread and pulled the daughter free, and eventually brought them both home into THE Infiniverse, and set them down among his own people. He remembered Hell Terra Firma, and the Prime Flame and Wheels of Existence...he remembered too many things!","\"Everything here is yours.\" Bob waved a tentacle at the dream around them, the Wheels, the clouds, the stars.","\"I live in your Infiniverse. I sleep in your Dream Engine. My daughter eats at your table and makes eyes at your son...\"","They sat for a while longer.","A dead Wheel nearby came together almost completely, turning slowly, light flickering across its rim. Both of them watched it. It held for a long moment, longer than the others. Then a crack spread through it, and it drifted apart.","Bob sighed.","\"You know,\" he said, \"no matter how high you climb, it all comes back to the same few things.\"","Noah looked over at him.","\"Power,\" Little Bobby went on, slowly, as a man talks when he has been thinking about something for a very long time.","\"Complexity. True Sources. Lattices. Wheels. Now Roots and Immensity and whatever else you have going on. I’ve seen beings rise so high they forgot what the ground looked like. I’ve seen Wheels that held more life than anyone could count, and I’ve watched them break.\"","His tentacles curled under him. \"And at the bottom of all of it, under every power anyone has ever had, there’s the same thing.\"","He held up one tentacle and counted on it, tip by tip.","\"To love. To protect. To provide.\"","The violet storm in his chest turned slowly.","\"That’s it. That’s all of it. Whether it’s my daughter.\" He pointed the tentacle at Noah. \"Or your son and daughter. We do everything we can for them. And for ourselves, so that we’re still standing when they need us. Everything else is just...\" He waved at the broken Wheels. \"Scenery.\"","Noah closed his eyes.","He nodded, slowly, and for a long while he stayed quiet.","\"Sometimes I feel very distant from all of them,\" Noah said.","Bob turned his head.","\"I see so much now,\" Noah went on. \"Every path. Every branch. When I look at Seo-yeon, I can see a thousand versions of her growing up, all at once, all of them real. When I look at Henry, I see every choice he could make before he makes it. When I look at my mother, I see thr countless years she has left, and every way those years could go.\"","He was quiet for a moment. \"It would be easy to stand up here and watch it all happen. To see everyone I love as patterns. Beautiful patterns, and very far away.\"","The clouds drifted around them.","\"But the Human in me will not let me,\" he said. \"My evolution took it and made it infinite. Every feeling I have now, it grows. It does not fade. I worry about them, and the worry keeps going. I love them, and it keeps going. I am angry for them, and it keeps going.\"","He opened his gold eyes and looked up at the stars his own dreams had put into Bob’s sky. \"I used to wonder whether I would stop caring, someday. Whether a being like me eventually becomes too large to feel small things.\"","He smiled faintly. \"I do not think I will. I think I will feel all of it, for as long as there is a me to feel it. I think I am going to keep caring for a very, very long time.\"","Bob only listened.","\"Right now,\" Noah said, \"almost everyone I love is in a cocoon.\"","He could see them, through the threads, even from here. A hill in his Domain with two shining shapes on it. The golden shore of THE Infiniverse lined with sleepers wrapped in light.","\"Ruination. She has been with me since before I was anything. I hope she comes out of it knowing she was never just a voice in my head.\" He paused.","\"THE Infiniverse. She has carried everything I own and everyone I love on her back without once complaining. I hope she comes out of it lighter. I hope she finds out what she wants for herself.\"","\"My mother. I hope she comes out of it with nothing left to fear.\" His voice softened. \"Seo-yeon. I hope she comes out of it curious, and stays curious, and never once has to be brave as I had to be. Henry. I hope he comes out of it strong enough to protect what he loves.\"","A glance toward Bob. \"Including your daughter...\"","Bob snorted.","\"Emotive,\" Noah said. \"I hope she comes out of it with every color she has, and none of them hurting. Thalia. I hope she comes out of it and rewrites whatever she likes. Barbatos. I hope her dead stand up for her forever. Ling, Poona...\" He shook his head slowly. \"All of them. I hope they come out bigger than they were, and still themselves.\"","He let out a long breath.","\"I have been chasing power for a long time, Bob. I am still chasing it. I will chase it all the way down into where Those Who Remain have not even accessed, and eat everything I find.\"","He settled deeper into the cloud. \"But you are right. Underneath all of it, that is the reason. I want to stand high enough that nothing can ever reach down and take them from me. And then I want to sit at the table with them, and eat, and argue, and smile.\"","Bob laughed softly.","\" That ,\" Noah said, \"is the dream.\"","Above them, a dead Wheel drifted together.","Spoke by spoke, shard by shard, it came whole and began to turn, and this time, with a faint hum, Noah’s dream reached up into it, golden and patient, and held its cracks closed.","It stayed whole!","Bob watched it turn for a long moment, his singularity eyes very bright!"]},{"number":5832,"title":"Chapter 5832: Chapter 5831: No Door Was Sealed! I","paragraphs":["<THE Sealed One>","All of existence was red, and THE Sealed One stood at the center of it, smiling.","He had always liked this part. The moment before. When the crimson first poured out of him and painted everything it touched, every enemy in reach became, for one breath, a thing that belonged to his color. The obsidian foam of a dead home, the drifting snow, the rivers of ink around the woman on the air. All of it red. All of it, in a small and honest way, already his.","He let them look at it!","Across the undefinition, three figures stood in his light.","THE Creature, vast and dark, white and obsidian flames rising off him, the fractured Root of Existence glowing in the crack across his chest.","Anaximander beside him, a scholar in white robes with no authority at all, his hands clasped behind his back. And Calliope, THE Writer of Mythos, sitting on nothing with one leg crossed over the other, script crawling slowly across her skin.","Three of them. And behind him, five Immense Ones, standing in the foam like suns behind a hill, watching.","He had no need of them.","That was the point.","Calliope moved first!","She uncrossed her legs, lifted one ink-stained hand, and wrote on the air.","The words burned as she made them. Fine, dense lines of script, her own neat hand, unspooling from her fingertip in long black ribbons.","A dreamer would have recognized the shape of what she was doing; he had a Grammar of his own. But hers made stories, where his made Sentences.","\"Once,\" Calliope said lazily, writing as she spoke, \"there was a mountain that was told to kneel. And it refused. And the hand that told it to kneel broke on its peak.\"","The words left the air and became true!","A mountain rose out of the red foam between them, grey and vast and snowcapped, ancient as a myth, and it came down on THE Sealed One like a falling sky!","He lifted one hand, and caught it.","The crimson in his palm opened. It was Infinity, and something older under it, braided together into a single bright substance, and it drank. The mountain met his palm and began to come apart, stone by stone, myth by myth, each piece sliding into the red light of his hand and vanishing. He was eating it, eating her story.","Then he chewed, thoughtfully.","\"Good,\" he said. \"A little dry.\"","Calliope’s dark eyes narrowed, and the script on her skin quickened.","She wrote faster!","A tide came next, a flood from some story about the drowning of the first Dimension, roaring across the foam in a wall of black water full of drowned bells. A spear followed it, written out of a legend about a hunter who threw his weapon at the sun and pinned it to the sky. Then a crowd of shining soldiers out of a war that existed only in her hand, marching in perfect order, every one of them a myth of a hero who did not fall.","THE Sealed One met all of them.","He drank the flood. The spear he caught between two fingers, tasted, and let crumble. The soldiers reached him in their thousands, and he walked through them as through a field of tall grass, his crimson eating each one as it touched him, and with every myth he devoured, he shone a little brighter.","And THE Creature moved!","Instead of attacking, he did something worse. The foam around THE Sealed One stopped being foam. The red light, the drifting snow, the air between them, the very ground beneath the Sealed One’s feet: all of it became THE Creature. His Pantheon of All Existence had no shape. It became the surroundings, and now THE Sealed One stood inside him.","The space closed in!","Existence itself pressed down on THE Sealed One from every side, weight upon weight, the burden of eras pressing inward, and his feet sank. For a moment, the crimson around him flickered.","\"Ah,\" THE Sealed One said softly. \"This...is you Existence?\"","He pushed outward.","Crimson tore through THE Creature’s Pantheon like light through cloth. The red brilliance poured out of him in every direction at once, Infinity and the old thing beneath it, and wherever it struck, THE Creature’s existence was eaten. Eaten, rather than broken. A chunk of his Pantheon simply ceased to be his and became a little more of THE Sealed One.","THE Creature grunted!","Then THE MAW opened!","It opened in the dark above THE Sealed One, vast and lightless, and it came down to swallow the crimson whole, one devourer meeting another. For an instant, the two appetites ground against each other, the MAW eating crimson, the crimson eating MAW, and the whole undefinition shook with the sound of it.","\"Interesting,\" THE Sealed One murmured, and for the first time, he took a step back.","And a few strides away, Anaximander watched all of it with his hands clasped behind his back, and sweated.","His fight looked nothing like the others’. He had no authority to fight with. Every scrap of power in this place belonged to someone else: THE Creature’s existence, Calliope’s myths, the crimson of the man across from him.","All he had was himself.","THE Sealed One noticed him at last. He looked across the foam at the scholar in white, and something in his face brightened with real curiosity.","\"You,\" he said. \"I have seen many anomalies but...what exactly are you?\"","WAA!","He flicked his fingers.","A lance of crimson tore across the undefinition toward Anaximander, Infinity and the source braided together, bright enough to unmake clusters of Dimensions.","Anaximander looked at it.","\"No,\" he said. \"That won’t reach me.\"","The lance stopped!","It hung in the air an arm’s length from his chest, crimson and blazing and perfectly still, straining forward with all the power of a fused Infinity behind it, and pressed no farther. Existence had heard the man in white robes speak, and existence agreed with him.","The lance faded.","THE Sealed One’s eyebrows rose.","He sent another. A storm of them this time, hundreds of crimson lances from every direction at once.","\"You won’t hit her,\" Anaximander said, not even looking, and every lance curving toward Calliope bent away. \"Or him.\"","The ones aimed at THE Creature broke apart!","\"And you are not as fast as you think you are.\"","THE Sealed One, who had already crossed half the distance between them in the space of a thought, found himself somehow still standing where he had started.","He stopped!","For a long moment, he simply looked at Anaximander. At the sweat on the scholar’s brow. At the hollow in his chest shaped like a Root, filled with nothing but existence’s agreement.","Then THE Sealed One laughed!","It was a genuine laugh, bright and astonished.","\"You,\" he said, \"are the strongest one here.\"","He turned his whole attention onto the scholar, and his voice softened into something almost affectionate.","\"The Creature commands existence. The Writer makes it. But you simply say what is true, and existence nods along. No authority. No Root of your own.\" He tilted his head. \"Do you know how many things I have eaten, trying to understand how something like you happens? And here you are, sweating in the snow.\"","\"It’s quite warm,\" Anaximander said mildly, \"under all this red.\"","THE Sealed One stood still for a long time after that.","Behind him, the five Immense Ones watched without moving. Across from him, three enemies drew breath: THE Creature with a hole eaten in his Pantheon, Calliope with her script running thin across her skin, Anaximander with sweat on his brow and his hands still clasped behind him.","They had held him. All three together, they had held him.","He found that he was very pleased.","\"Do you know what I am?\" he asked them, quietly. \"Most do not. They call me a thief. A genocidal maniac who ate his own disciples. A devourer. A vessel-wearer. They are not wrong. But they miss the point.\"","He spread his pale hands.","\"Every being in existence is born with a little. A Root, if they are lucky. A Source. A gift from some framework they did not build. And they spend their whole lives guarding that little, and dying with it.\"","He smiled. \"I chose differently. I took many things. And most recently...every Root I ever devoured, I kept. Every Gu. Every Infinity Eater. Every story I have ever tasted. Nothing I have taken has ever been wasted.\"","The crimson around him dimmed.","And behind him, something began to rise.","Roots.","They bloomed out of the dark at his back one after another, illusory and enormous, each one a diffrent color. A Root of green fire. A Root of grey stone. A Root of gold, a Root of bone, a Root that sang. Dozens. Hundreds. Every Root he had ever devoured, from every Provenance Lifeform and Progeny THE Keepers of Existence had ever fed him, rising behind him in a vast and terrible crown.","Then they began to merge!","They grew into one another, Root into Root, colors bleeding together, stems twisting and fusing, until behind THE Sealed One stood a single towering shape, a crown braided from a few hundred stolen Roots . And from that braid, a weight poured out.","It was beyond him. Beyond anything a being who held a Root should be able to carry.","It was Immensity!","HUUM!"]},{"number":5833,"title":"Chapter 5833: Chapter 5832: No Door Was Sealed! II","paragraphs":["It was...stitched and grafted. Assembled out of a thousand pieces that had each been reaching for the door when he ate them. But Immensity, all the same, finished and heavy and real, pressing down on the undefinition from behind him.","The five Immense Ones at his back stirred, for the first time.","\"My Chorus,\" THE Sealed One said fondly. \"Every one of them died wanting to be Immense. So I let them be Immense together. Inside me.\"","He lifted his hand.","The Chorus moved with him.","It came down on THE Creature first. Crimson and a thousand braided colors, the full weight of stolen potential Immensity, crashing into the vast dark shape and driving it into the foam. White and obsidian flames guttered. The fractured Root in THE Creature’s chest flared, and cracked further, a new line of light splitting across it.","It came down on Calliope next. Her myths rose to meet it, mountains and floods and armies and suns, written faster than any hand should write, and the Chorus ate them all. Then it reached her. The script on her skin smeared and ran like ink in rain. She cried out once, sharp and furious, and fell from the air into the red foam.","And then it came for Anaximander.","\"That won’t-\" Anaximander began.","The Chorus spoke over him. A thousand stolen Roots, all at once, a single voice made of the voices of the dead:","|It will.|","And existence, for the first time, hesitated over whom to agree with.","That hesitation was enough. The weight came down. Anaximander was thrown across the undefinition, his white robes torn, blood at his mouth, and he lay where he fell, breathing hard, his eyes still open and still curious.","The crimson faded.","The Chorus settled behind THE Sealed One, quiet and enormous.","Three enemies lay broken in the foam of a dead home!","—","THE Sealed One stood over them, and smoothed down the front of his dark coat.","\"I defeated you fairly,\" he said. \"One against three. No help from behind me. You saw them. They did not move.\"","He glanced back at the five Immense Ones. \"Fair and square.\"","He looked down at the three of them, and smiled.","\"But will you play fair?\"","He lifted his eyes.","Past the foam, past the red, past the edge of the undefinition, there was a place that only a very few beings could see. A vast and quiet brilliance, standing among shelves that climbed out of sight. Ink and parchment and patience.","THE MATRIARCH OF INK, watching over her fallen daughter.","THE Sealed One looked straight at her.","\"I defeated your daughter,\" he said. \"She is my spoil now. That is how these things go.\" His gold eyes glittered. \"So. Will you be fair, Matriarch?\"","He took a step toward Calliope.","\"Or will you intervene?\"","He took a second step!","And THE MATRIARCH OF INK’s power came down.","It spilled out of the hidden brilliance like a sea of ink pouring off a shelf, black and endless and furious, every drop of it a word, every word a law, falling on the undefinition from above. Its pressure crushed the foam flat. Its edges wrote themselves across the red sky in letters too vast to read.","| You will not touch my child.|","THE Sealed One laughed!","He threw back his head and laughed with real joy.","\"There it is! Hypocrisy!\"","Behind him, the five Immense Ones moved at last.","They rose out of the foam like five suns coming up at once, and their Immensity met the falling ink in the air above the undefinition, and the whole sky cracked.","\"Remember!\" THE Sealed One called up to them, still laughing. \"You all played unfairly first!\"","|Unfair is a word for the losing side,| one of the five answered, its voice like a bell rung underwater.","|Hold her,| said another, cold and flat. |Let the boy collect.|","The five of them pushed. The sea of ink pushed back. Above the undefinition, Immensity ground against Immensity in a storm of black and gold, and THE Matriarch’s brilliance strained against five at once, and slowly, slowly, was forced back toward her shelves.","And THE Sealed One walked toward his spoils.","He walked past THE Creature, groaning in the foam. Past Anaximander, propped on one elbow, watching him go with a calm that had blood on it. He walked to where Calliope lay with her script smeared and her eyes half open, and he crouched beside her, and reached out one pale hand.","Then the snow stopped falling!","Every flake hung in the air, perfectly still. The red light dimmed. The storm above them, five Immense Ones and one Matriarch locked together, slowed and grew quiet, as though the whole undefinition had stepped inside a house where someone was in mourning.","Frost spread across the foam!","It came in a slow, silver tide, ticking softly as it went, and where it passed, everything grew very cold and very calm. Out of it, walking without hurry, came a woman.","She was tall and pale, dressed in layers of grey like the light of a winter morning, her hair now bound up with silver pins. Her face held no anger. It held something older and heavier than anger, a grief kept so long and so carefully that it had become a kind of composure.","THE REMINISCING WIDOW!","Behind her, faint and flickering, stood a second figure. A man, translucent and illusory, sharp-faced and somber, with eyes far too bright for a ghost. He held a quill. Ancient, plain, its nib dark with something deeper than ink. It hummed in his illusory hand with a sound like a clock ticking very far away.","The Quill of Chronos!","THE Sealed One went still!","The Widow kept her gaze above him. She looked up, past the five Immense Ones, past the storm, toward the hidden shelves and the brilliance straining among them.","|Matriarch,| she said. Her voice was perfectly calm. |You will want to write with something.|","The illusory man behind her flicked his wrist.","The Quill of Chronos left his illusory fingers and flew upward, through the storm, past the five Immense Ones, straight into the hidden brilliance among the shelves.","THE MATRIARCH OF INK caught it!","For one long moment, the undefinition held its breath. Then, from the hidden place, came a sound that every being in the undefinition felt in their bones: an intake of breath. Shock. Disbelief.","|This is...|","Her power exploded upward!","The sea of ink became an ocean. It rose out of the hidden shelves in a single vast column and tore through the storm, and the five Immense Ones were flung back across the sky like leaves. The ink was words, and now it was time as well. Every letter now carried a tick of the Quill, every law a moment written and fixed, and where it fell, things that had happened began to be written differently.","The smears on Calliope’s skin began, slowly, to run backward.","THE Sealed One rose from his crouch, and looked at the Widow, and at the somber ghost behind her, and at the column of ink and time blazing up from the hidden shelves.","Then, quite deliberately, he sat down.","He sat on the frozen foam with one knee drawn up and his arm resting across it, in the middle of the undefinition, ringed by Immensity on every side.","Five Immense Ones regrouping above him. A Matriarch with a weapon of time in her hand. A Widow whose cold could still a storm. His Chorus of stolen Roots towering silent at his back.","And he looked entirely at ease.","\"Everyone thinks the door is sealed,\" THE Sealed One said.","His voice was calm.","\"The Long Night closed it. The First Frost swore it. The Counting presses on every Root in existence, and every Immense One I have ever met stands in front of that door and weeps, or waits, or schemes. They think it is the shape of everything. The great wall at the end of everything.\"","He tipped his head back and looked up at the red sky.","\"I have watched them. A great many of them, through a great many eyes. Every one of them sees the door, and sees themselves, and sees nothing else. That is the trouble with being born whole. You spend your whole existence trying to stay that way.\"","He smiled.","\"I was never whole. I was riven. Torn into pieces and scattered across more vessels than I can count. And when you are already in pieces, there is nothing a door can keep out of you. You simply go around it. You go through the walls. You eat whatever stands on the other side.\"","The Chorus behind him hummed.","\"No door,\" THE Sealed One said softly, \"was ever sealed for me.\"","He looked across the undefinition, at the Widow, at the ghost, at the blazing column of ink and time, and his gold eyes shone with something very old and very hungry.","\" After all ,\" he said, \"I have access to IT.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5834,"title":"Chapter 5834: Chapter 5833: Those Who Remain!","paragraphs":["<THE True Human Emperor>","The dead Wheel was still turning above them, whole and humming, when Poona’s voice arrived in Noah’s head.","It came bright and quick down the thread that bound her to his Tree, and it was very excited.","Moriarty had reached out to her, she told him.","The Council of Immense Ones of THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity had reached a conclusion regarding his distinction as THE Legacy’s Son. They wanted her to bring him to Lucy’s Lecture Hall. Now, if possible. Preferably sooner.","Noah opened his eyes!","Bob was watching him from his golden cloud, singularity eyes narrowed.","\"Duty?\" Bob asked.","\"Something like that.\"","\"Go on, then.\" Bob waved a tentacle at him.","\"I’ll be here...\"","Noah stood, brushed off his cloud, and stepped out of the dream.","—","Poona was waiting for him at the edge of his Domain, bouncing so hard her golden body kept leaving the grss.","\"Hold on to me, Master,\" she said. \"The Lecture Hall can’t be reached by just anyone. Only a recognized Immensity of the Legacy can find the way. Even Progeny who have lived on the mountains for Ages have never seen it.\"","Noah laid a hand on her small round back.","She took them through!","It felt very different from stepping through a dream. Poona’s Dream Immensity opened, warm and smelling faintly of honey, and pulled them sideways out of the Domain and into the weavings of existence itself.","Noah felt them pass between threads hidden from him until now, strands of Lucy’s old work running through the Legacy like hidden corridors behind the walls of a great house. Some of the threads were older than anything he had ever touched. Some of them hummed when Poona passed, and let her through, as a door knows its own key.","Whatever Lucy had built, it still recognized its people.","Then the threads opened, and they stepped out into light!","They stood at the center of a ring!","It was obsidian, veined with bright gold, laid flat beneath their feet like the floor of a stage. Around it ran another ring, wider, and around that another, and another, each one rising a little higher than the last, ring after ring after ring of obsidian and gold stretching out and up and away until their end lay beyond his sight. They simply kept going, climbing into a distance that had no ceiling.","An amphitheater. The largest one he had ever seen, or would likely ever see.","And on every ring, there were thrones!","Some were carved from stone and some grown from living wood. Some were made of light, or water, or bone, or things he had no name for. They stood on the tiers in a great curving sweep, and on them, or standing beside them, or drifting above them, were the Immense Ones of THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity.","More than a hundred of them!","Noah’s gold eyes moved across them.","Most of them sat Established, their Profundity deep but readable, their bottoms glimpsed far below. Some sat Ancient, so deep his eyes slid off them. A handful, newly risen in the last few Ages, still burned bright and loud.","He recognized a few from the war on the Thinker’s mountain: THE Ashen Cantor with his cinders, THE Keeper of the Unbroken Vow with his chain of oaths, THE Lantern of the Last Shore with his lamp. The rest were strangers.","A woman made of still grey water, her throne a lake standing on its end. A tall thing of rust-red feathers, every feather a tongue of quiet flame. An old man whose beard was a watterfall of tiny written letters, scrolling slowly down to the floor. A pair of twins joined at the shoulder, one laughing, one weeping, sharing a single throne carved with a single word.","Every one of them was looking at him!","The pressure of it was enormous. More than a hundred Immensities, all turned on one man standing at the bottom of their bowl. Noah let it press, and stood straight under it.","Then he looked at the center.","The innermost tiers held the oldest thrones, plain and close to the floor, and one of them was taken by Sir Moriarty, his spectacles mended, his long coat finally clean of green, his tentacles resting on the arms of his chair.","Beside him, on a throne of dark stone that seemed to be part of a mountain, knelt THE Thinker at the End of Existence, his beads clicking slowly through his great fingers.","And beside the Thinker, perched on the arm of his throne with her legs swinging, sat Ling.","She caught Noah’s eye and grinned!","At the very front of the amphitheater, facing all of it, stood a lectern. Plain, worn, carved of pale wood gone dark with handling. Behind it hung a broad dark board of obsidian, and across that board, in faded gold, ran lines of writing too old for Noah to read. A lesson, left half-written. The last line trailed off in the middle of a word!","The lectern stood empty.","In front of it, set a little apart from all the others on the innermost ring, sat a single empty chair.","Noah looked at that chair for a long moment.","Then Moriarty rose!","He stayed beside his own throne, away from the lectern, an old octopus in a long coat, and looked down at Noah with his crimson eyes, and the whole amphitheater went quiet.","\"Do you know what we are called?\" Moriarty asked.","His voice was mild. It carried to every ring without effort.","\" Those Who Remain . Many of us do not like the name. Many of us would rather not think about it. But it is the truth, and we are scholars here, so we will start with the truth.\"","He looked up at the rings above him, at the hundred thrones.","\"Existence is very old, Osmont. Older than any of us. It has turned over more times than any of us can count. Cycles upon cycles. Ages upon Ages. And in every one of those turnings, countless beings rose, and reached, and tried to pass through the doors that would carry them further.\"","His tentacles shifted on the arms of his throne. \"Most of them failed to make it. They went on, or they ended, or they became something we could no longer see. But we did not go on. We did not end. We stayed.\"","He turned his crimson eyes back to Noah.","\"We remained. That is what the name means. We are the ones who were left behind.\"","Somewhere high in the rings, the weeping twin made a small sound.","\"Consider how strange that is,\" Moriarty went on, and now there was something almost like wonder in his voice.","\" Every particle in us...in you, every thread of your existence, was made from something that came before. Old weavings, broken down and built again. You are the ash of older authorities and Dimensionalities. So are we all . And we who remain have watched it happen. We have watched whole cycles of existence rise and fall and rise again. We have stood on the shore and watched everything we knew wash out and come back changed.\"","He was quiet for a moment.","\"We have lived a very long time. And we know, better than anyone, the ones who did not remain. We remember their names. Some of them were our teachers. Some of them were our friends.\"","His eyes went, very briefly, to the empty chair before the lectern. \"Some of them simply had a quality the rest of us lacked. Something in them that the doors recognized, and we have never understood.\"","He spread his tentacles.","\"Every one of us here is still fighting. Every being in this hall is still reaching. Still studying. Still trying. But we know, too, that the doors are nearly impossible for us. We have tried. Ages upon Ages, we have tried, and here we sit.\"","He let out a slow breath.","\"Lucy knew that. Before she left, she left us directions. And she left us something more than directions. She left us hope.\" His voice softened","\"Her words were simple. Sometimes, existence only needs the right key, to open a certain door.\"","The amphitheater was utterly silent.","\"You may be that key,\" Moriarty said. \"You may not be. None of us can say. Not even him.\"","He nodded toward the Thinker, who kept his eyes on his beads. \"But we know our own Legacy. We know what Lucy built, and what she asked of us. And so we take the gamble, whether right or wrong.\"","He straightened.","\"THE Council of Immense Ones of THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity has decided. We enact you, Noah Osmont, as THE Legacy’s Son.\"","A murmur ran through the rings, low and heavy!","\"We ask nothing of you,\" Moriarty said. \"Only this. Keep the hope alive across this winter. The hope that one day, we will be more than Those Who Remain.\"","He looked up, at the endless rings, at every throne, at every Immense One sitting on them. \" In all our existences, we do not only want to remain.\"","...!","—","The board behind the lectern began to glow!","Its faded gold writing brightened, line by line, and from the center of the half-written lesson, something bloomed.","An orb!","It swelled out of the obsidian board like a drop of ink gathering on the tip of a pen, slowly, the gold writing peeling off the board and drawing inward as it formed. It grew round and dark and perfectly smooth, obsidian clear enough to look into, and inside it, the gold writing kept moving.","Lines of Lucy’s script turned within the orb in slow rings, ring inside ring, every word glowing as it passed, circling and circling like the tiers of the very amphitheater it had been born in. Faint gold veins ran across its surface and pulsed, as though something beneath them breathed.","At its very center, cradled by all those turning rings, hung a tiny door. No larger than a thumbnail. Turning slowly in place.","The orb came free of the board and floated down through the air of the amphitheater, past the rings, past the thrones, down toward the center of the bowl, toward Noah.","It stopped in front of him, at the height of his heart, humming.","\"Lucy left this behind,\" Moriarty said quietly, \"for the one who would inherit the distinction of THE Legacy’s Son. None of us have ever held it. None of us were meant to.\"","His crimson eyes met Noah’s. \"Will you take it on?\"","Noah looked at the orb.","He looked past it, at the empty chair. At the half-written lesson. At a hundred Immense Ones who had sat in this bowl for longer than his whole species had existed, waiting for someone they had yet to name.","Then he reached out, and took it!","The orb settled into his palm as though it had always been his! Its gold veins flared bright, and the rings of Lucy’s script inside it spun faster, then all at once fell still. And the tiny door at its center stopped turning, and faced him.","| Relic grasped: THE Orb of Immensity.|","|Left by Lucy, THE Acharya of Immensity, for THE Legacy’s Son.|","|The Legacy’s woven Immensity recognizes its bearer as its own.|","|Where the bearer walks within THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity, the Legacy will answer.|","|The writing within the orb is Lucy’s last weavings.|","|The door at its heart has been waiting.|","...!","The tiny door at the heart of the orb swung open!","Light poured out of it, obsidian and gold, and spilled down onto the floor of the amphitheater in front of Noah, and grew. It rose up out of the light in a single smooth motion, taller than a man, taller than a throne, a great doorway of obsidian veined with gold, standing alone at the center of the bowl with nothing behind it but more amphitheater.","Through it, Noah could see only a soft, endless brightness.","|A doorway has formed.|","|Beyond it lies the Domain that Lucy left behind for THE Legacy’s Son.|","|No Immense One of this Legacy has entered it.|","...!","Every throne in the amphitheater stirred!","Noah stood before the doorway with the orb in his hand, and turned, and looked up at them all. At Moriarty, his tentacles very still. At the Thinker, whose beads had stopped. At Ling, who had stopped swinging her legs. At a hundred Immense Ones, all of them leaning forward on their thrones.","\"Existence is vast,\" Noah said.","\"Nothing in it can be promised. Not by me. Not by any of you. I have seen enough of it now to know that much.\" He looked at the empty chair before the lectern. \"But I... do not plan to remain.\"","The words went up through the rings like a stone dropped into a still pool.","\"And existence is cause and effect,\" Noah said. \"Everything that happens to me happens because of what came before. Those who help me...will be helped in turn. Cause...and effect. If I no longer remain, then neither will you.\"","He turned back to the doorway.","\" So I will not remain.\"","...!","He stepped toward the obsidian doorway with Lucy’s orb in his hand.","And on every throne in Lucy’s Lecture Hall, a hundred Immense Ones held their breath, and watched, and waited.","What had Lucy left behind?!"]},{"number":5835,"title":"Chapter 5835: Chapter 5834: I Am Sorry!","paragraphs":["Noah stepped through the doorway, and the brightness closed behind him.","He braced for something grand! A vault of Immensity, perhaps. A library of lost Ages. Maybe a throne waiting at the end of a long hall, or some last weapon left by the founder of a Legacy for the one who would inherit it.","Instead, he smelled grass!","He stood at the edge of a farm!","A small one. A low wooden fence ran along a dirt path, its rails grey and soft with weather. Beyond it lay a vegetable garden in neat rows: beans climbing poles, squash sprawled under broad leaves, a line of something leafy and green gone a little wild at the end where no one had weeded it.","A field of wheat swayed gold under a pale blue sky, and past the wheat, an orchard of six apple trees, the fruit red and heavy. A single cloud drifted overhead, unhurried.","Only a mild breeze, and birdsong somewhere off in the hedges, and an absence of snow and cold and Counting so complete it felt like holding his breath.","Noah stood very still and looked at it all with his gold eyes.","Here, as far as he could feel, was simply a farm. The Gold Without Pupils went down into the soil and found soil. Into the trees and found wood and sap and apples. Into the sky and found sky, ordinary and quiet, hiding nothing at all.","So he walked!","He opened the gate, and it creaked. He walked along the dirt path between the garden rows. A hoe leaned against the fence where someone had set it down, its handle worn smooth and dark where hands had held it for a very long time. A wooden bucket sat beside a stone wel, half full of water so clear he could see the pebbles at the bottom. In the middle of the wheat stood a scarecrow with its arms out, wearing a battered straw hat and a coat patched at both elbows.","He touched the scarecrow’s sleeve as he passed. Old cloth. Real cloth. Only that.","Strange!","He had expected Lucy, THE Acharya of Immensity, founder of a Legacy where a hundred Immense Ones sat waiting for her return, to leave behind something terrible and vast. And she had left him a garden.","At the end of the path stood a hut!","It was small and plain, built of timber and stone, with a thatched roof and a crooked chimney and a single window with a flower box beneath it. Herbs grew in the flower box. Someone had planted them in careful rows.","Noah opened the door and stepped inside.","One room. A narrow bed against the wall, its blanket squared at the foot. A wooden table with two chairs. Over a hearth swept clean, a kettle hung above the cold ashes. Shelves with jars of dried beans and preserved fruit, every jar labled in a small neat hand. A pair of muddy boots by the door.","And on the table, a piece of paper!","It was gold. Thin gold, creased once, lying flat beside an empty cup. And across its face ran words in obsidian ink, small and close and slanting, written by a hand that had taken its time.","A letter!","Noah picked it up!","The moment his fingers touched it, the words began to shine!","| To the one my children chose,|","|If you are reading this, then they have named you the Legacy’s Son, and you have come through the door I left, expecting a great deal. I am sorry. There is only a farm here. I grew up on one very much like it, a long time ago, before any of the rest of it. Before Immensity, before Legacies, before any of my students learned to call me THE Acharya. I wanted whoever found this to see where I came from. I wanted them to know that I began small. Everyone does.|","|Sit down, if you like. The chair by the window is the comfortable one. This will take a while.|","|Long ago, existence turned in good order. Its cycles came and went as seasons come and go on a farm: the planting, the growing, the harvest, the long rest of winter, and then the planting again. Each cycle had its nights, and its nights were cold, but they ended. Every being that rose within a cycle could climb. There were doors above us, one after another, and a path that ran up through them, higher than any of us had ever seen. The path was hard. Most who walked it failed. But it was there, and everyone knew it was there, and that knowing was a kind of light.|","|We climbed. My friends and I. My brothers and sisters of the long road, my teachers, my students. Ages upon Ages we climbed, until we came to a place on the path that no one could pass. We called it the Narrows. A junction of existence where the path above us thinned to nothing, too fine to stand on, too high to reach. Every being who had ever reached the Narrows had stopped there, and either turned back, or remained. It was the edge of everything.|","|And beneath the Narrows, holding the whole path together, there was IT.|","|I will not tell you exactly what IT was. Partly because the words would cost you more than you can yet afford to know. And partly because I am ashamed. IT was never meant for us. IT was the thing that held the path in place, as a keystone holds an arch. IT was what let existence climb from one cycle to the next without falling apart. Nobody was meant to touch IT. Nobody was meant to use IT.|","|We used IT.|","|There were a few of us. I will not write their names, because they do not deserve to be remembered for this, and neither do I. We were the oldest, the deepest, the most certain. We had stood at the Narrows longer than anyone, and we had grown tired of standing. One of us found a way to reach beneath the path and take hold of IT. And we told each other it would only be for a moment. Just long enough to cross. Just long enough to see what lay above. We would let go on the other side, and everything would be as it was.|","|We crossed.|","|And the moment we crossed, the path broke behind us.|","|I have spent a very long time trying to describe what happened next, and I have never found the right words. IT was not made to carry anyone. When we leaned our whole weight on IT, IT split. IT sundered. IT broke apart into pieces, and the pieces were flung out across existence in every direction, far and wide and deep, into places none of us could follow. And without IT holding the path together, the path itself came apart. The Narrows collapsed. The doors above them shattered, one after another, all the way up. Everything that had held existence’s cycles in good order came loose at once.|","| That was THE First Sundering. Not a war. Not a monster. Not a curse laid on existence by some enemy. It was us. Many of us, reaching for what was not ours, and breaking everything to have it.|","|We left. We crossed over, and we went on, and the road we came by closed behind us forever.|","|And everyone else stayed.|","|My friends who had not yet reached the Narrows. My students, who had been climbing behind me their whole lives, trusting the path to be there when they arrived. My brothers and sisters who were only a few steps short. All of them stayed, because there was no longer anywhere to go. We made them what they are. We made them Those Who Remain. They did not fail. We failed them. We took the path away and left them standing on a broken stair.|","|It cannot be fixed.|","|Not by any of them, and not by you. Not even if someone gathered every piece of IT from every corner of existence and put them all back together. What broke is not only IT. What broke is the path, and the doors, and the order of existence itself. You cannot unbreak a stair by finding the stones. The shape it held is gone.|","|And existence remembers what we did to it.|","|Since the First Sundering, the cycles have turned without order. Existence is hurt, and like anything that is hurt, it is trying to heal, and its healing is not gentle. It seeks to right the wrongs done to it. Its nights will grow longer and colder and stranger than any night before. It will close what we left open. It will count what we left uncounted. It will judge anything that reaches upward, because the last ones who reached upward broke everything. I have seen the first of these nights from the other side, and I tell you plainly, worse ones are coming. The Long Night is only the beginning of its anger.|","|No doors will open. The doors were shattered so that we could leave. There is no path above. There is no sky. For those I left behind, there is no hope of going where I went.|","|You will hear prophecies. You will hear of Auguries, of keys and of those who will open the way, of signs in the snow and promises in the dark. Many of them were left behind by those of us who felt guilty. We wanted to give the ones we abandoned something to hold. Some of us whispered hopes into the cracks as we crossed. Some of us left riddles, believing that a riddle was kinder than the truth. I did it too. I left my children a chair and a cup of tea and a promise that the right key might one day open a certain door. Forgive me. It was the only kindness I knew how to leave that was not a lie, and it is very nearly one.|","|If there is anything at all to be done, it is this. The pieces of IT still lie scattered across existence. Whoever gathered them might, perhaps, do what we did once. Not repair the path. Nothing will repair the path. But cross, as we crossed, by some other way that none of us could see. Maybe. I do not know. Maybe.|","|I am not leaving any trace of myself here. No echo of my mind, no piece of my consciousness for you to question. I could have. I chose not to. I do not deserve to sit in this room and be forgiven by whoever walks in. All I can leave is this letter, and this farm, and the truth.|","|Please look after them. All of them. They stayed because of me. Let them at least have someone who chose to stay with them.|","|I am so sorry.|","|Lucy.|","...!","The last word faded into the gold.","Noah stood in the small, plain hut with the letter in his hand, and for a long moment he stood perfectly still.","Outside, the breeze stirred the wheat. A bird sang in the hedges. The scarecrow stood in its field with its arms out, wearing its patched coat, as it had stood for Ages.","Multiple beings had reached beneath the path and taken hold of IT. And in reaching, they had shattered every door above existence, broken the order of its cycles, and left everyone else behind to freeze.","The Long Night, The Sealed Door, the Counting, the Judgment that had come down on him three times now, crying How dare you. All of it, every cold and closing and cruel thing he had fought since he crossed into the winter, was existence hurting. Existence trying to heal. Existence remembering what had been done to it.","And the pieces of IT were still out there!","Scattered across existence. Waiting!","Noah’s hand tightened on Lucy’s letter until the gold paper creaked!"]},{"number":5836,"title":"Chapter 5836: Chapter 5835: Keystone!","paragraphs":["Noah set the letter down on the table, beside the empty cup, exactly where he had found it.","Then he went outside.","The breeze was still blowing. The wheat still swayed. Somewhere in the hedges, the same bird was still singing, as though beings breaking the path above existence and leaving countless to freeze were a story about somewhere else. This little farm had kept on being a farm through all of it.","He stood on the doorstep for a while and looked at the garden.","The row at the end had gone wild. Weeds had crept in among the greens, tall and tangled, as weeds always do when a garden is left alone. The beans had climbed past the tops of their poles and were waving loose in the air. A few apples had fallen in the orchard and lay in the grass, going soft.","Noah walked down the path to the fence, picked up the old hoe leaning against it, and turned it over in his hands.","Smooth wood. Dark where hands had held it. Heavier than it looked.","He smiled a little.","It was a silly thing to want, for a being like him. He had evolved. He had eaten a dead Immense One and an Ergosphere full of Roots and two suns made of civilizations. And for all of that, one of the grandest dreams he had ever carried was this: a farm. A small one. Somewhere quiet, when everything was over and done, with a garden to tend and a family to feed and nothing more urgent anywhere than whether the beans needed tying.","He rolled up imaginary sleeves, and went to work!","He started with the weeds, kneeling in the wild row and pulling them one by one, roots and all, shaking the dirt off and tossing them in a pile at the end of the path. The soil was cool and dark and smelled of rian. Next, he tied the beans back to their poles with lengths of twine he found hanging on a nail by the hut door.","He gathered the fallen apples into the wooden bukcet and set them by the well. Last, he drew water and carried it down the rows and poured it at the roots of every plant, slowly, watching the soil drink.","His stellar dark gold hands got dirty.","Then he took the hoe to the last row.","It was hard ground, packed down from Ages without a turning, and he worked it. Lift, drop, pull. Lift, drop, pull. The blade bit into the earth and turned it over, dark and crumbling, and the smell of it rose up around him.","It was cathartic.","On the seventh stroke, the blade caught on something.","Paper!","A little scrap of it, crumpled into a ball, half buried in the soil where the hoe had turned it up. Gold, like the letter. Old, and creased, and very small.","Noah crouched and picked it up.","It was heavy. Far too heavy for a scrap of paper. His hand dipped under the weight of it, as though he had picked up a stone pretending to be a leaf. He stared at it for a moment.","Then he smoothed it open on his palm!","BOOM!","Something sat in the creases of the paper. A shard. Tiny, no larger than a grain of sand, obsidian and gold, catching the mild farm light and throwing it back as a deep, impossible gleam. And the moment the paper opened and the shard touched open air, its weight came down.","All of it!","Noah’s arm dropped. His knees drove into the soft dirt of the garden row. The grain of obsidian and gold sat on his open palm and pressed down on him with a heaviness beyond anything in his life. Heavier than the stone he had carried on his back in the obsidian sands. Heavier than the Warden’s gaze. Heavier than the Hound’s closing hand, or the Fiend’s finger, or any Judgment existence had ever dropped on him. It was so heavy that the farm itself seemed to lean toward it, the wheat bowing, the apple trees creaking, the single cloud overhead drifting slowly down.","On the inside of the paper, in small slanting obsidian ink, there were words.","|It seems you are a decent being. You did not destroy everything in rage, and you even began taking care of my farm. So here is a little fragment I managed to hold, and keep down here. I doubt it will help much, or change much. But it is something.|","BOOM!","The prompts came, and they were short.","|Obtained: an Infinitesimally Small Shard of IT.|","|Details: ?????|","|Details: ?????|","|Details: ?????|","...!","Noah stared at the shard in his palm.","A piece of IT!","A grain of the thing that had once held the whole path of existence together, before beings leaned their weight on it and broke it apart. Lucy had kept this. Hidden it in the dirt of her own garden, under her own scarecrow, where only someone willing to kneel in the soil and pull weeds would ever find it.","His existence pulsed!","It pulsed hard, once, all the way through, as though every part of him had just heard its own name called. The Tree in his chest flared. And his eyes, his pure gold pupil-less eyes, burned. Bright. Brighter!","Blazing with something between hunger and defiance, both at once, a gold fire so fierce it lit the garden row around him.","He could barely hold the shard up. His arm shook under it. His fingers trembled.","And something in him said: eat it.","Fucking it eat bro!","It skipped every step of thought. His existence wanted it, completely and instinctively, as a starving thing wants bread. So he lifted his trembling hand to his mouth.","And brought his jaws down.","It went into him like a mountain falling into a well.","The weight that had driven him to his knees was suddenly inside him, and his whole existence buckled around it. He felt it drop through him, past his tongue, past his throat, down into the heart of everything he was, and land at the base of his Tree like an anvil dropped from the sky.","BOOM!","His body shook!","His skin stretched. All over, at once, the night-dark surface of him bulged outward in a hundred places, as though spears were trying to push their way out of him from the inside. His constellations blazed and scattered. His horns of radiance flickered wildly.","The halo of time behind his shoulders spun so fast it shrieked. He could feel cracks running through his existence, fine and many, the whole of him straining to hold something far beyond what it had been built to hold.","He sat down!","Right there in the garden, in the dirt between the bean rows, cross-legged, hands on his knees. He closed his gold eyes and turned everything he had inward. His Dream. The Tree where his Root had been. The Human and the Dreamer and the Sovereign in him, all at once.","Then the Dreaming Human Origin went to work on what he had swallowed.","Instead of fighting it, he dreamed around it. He wrapped it in Dream, layer upon layer, and began, slowly, to break it down, as he had broken down the corpse of an Immense One and an Ergosphere full of Roots.","But this was different. This held. This was the oldest, densest, most fundamental thing he had ever touched, and his Dream could only wear at it, grain by grain, as a river wears at a mountain.","So he let time pass.","He let a great deal of it pass!","And as it passed, he saw himself.","He saw himself young. A boy, thin and quick, holding a hoe too big for him in the school garden and laughing at something just out of sight.","He saw himself as he was when everything first broke, frightened and furious, throwing fire with shaking hands. He saw himself crushed under a stone in the obsidian sands. Kneeling over a corpse on a frozen plain. Standing on a cloud while a door slammed in a young woman’s face.","He saw himself now, sitting in the dirt.","And he saw himself old.","Old, as he had always refused to imagine being. Grey at the temples. Lined at the eyes. Sitting on a porch very much like the one behind him, watching a garden grow, with children’s voices somewhere out in the wheat, and a cup of tea going cold in his hand. Content!","And then he saw more. Lives still unlived, that he might yet live. A thousand Noahs, a million, branching away in every direction through the long dream, each one living out a whole existence in the space of a breath.","One who ruled. One who wandered. One who farmed. One who died young and one who lived forever. He lived them all. Every year of them. Every season. It felt like a very long time, and also no time at all, as a whole life feels at the end of it.","All of it, every life and every year, went into the shard, and wore at it, and wore at it.","And the shard, very slowly, gave.","—","His body settled!","The spears beneath his skin sank back. The cracks in his existence sealed, one after another, and where each one closed, something new and dense and gold remained behind. His constellations drifted back into place under his skin. The halo behind his shoulders slowed, and steadied, and when it settled, there were two rings turning there, one inside the other.","Noah opened his eyes!","In the gold of them, very faint, a fleck of obsidian now drifted.","| Devoured: an Infinitesimally Small Shard of IT.|","|What you devoured cannot be fully understood. Your existence has taken from it only what it can hold.|","|Your Tree has drunk deeply.|","|Sap risen: 100%. Your Tree has grown its First Bough.|","|A great limb spreads from your trunk, and your existence spreads with it.|","|Second Ring lit. Ring by ring, your trunk will burn brighter, until one day it blazes from root to crown.|","|Sap risen toward the Second Bough: 90%.|","...!","| Attributes, measured anew.|","|VERITAS: Order I.8 to Order II.6.|","|PROVENANCE: Order I.9 to Order II.7.|","|PONDUS: Order I.8 to Order II.3.|","|OSMONTIAN MOIRAI: Order I.5 to Order II.0.|","|POTENTIA: Infinite.|","|Every attribute has entered the second Order. Your Dream now reaches across the whole domain of a Legacy.|","...!","| Predation: from the Shard of IT, your Tree has drawn a capability.|","|Formed: THE Keystone Dream.|","|Every structure has a stone that holds it: a being, a power, a Domain, a seal, a curse, a Legacy. You see that stone. You may dream it loose, and let all it held come apart. Or you may dream it held, and let nothing break it.|","|Your reach follows your Order. Keystones set deeper than your Profundity lie below your sight.|","|IT was a keystone once. You now carry a grain of it, and you will never look at anything the same way again.|","...!","|Auto-Fusion: THE Keystone Dream + THE First Unsealing: THE Door of Immensity.|","|THE First Unsealing has deepened. It is now THE Unsealing of Doors. Every door has a keystone. What is closed against those you lift, you may find the stone of, and open; what is sealed against yourself, you may find the stone of, and seek a way through.|","...!","|Kin: your Tree has risen. Those bound to it rise with it.|","|Ling, Poona, and Bob have deepened. The cocoons of your Kin brighten.|","...!","|Your Gold Without Pupils has been refined. You may now perceive the weavings of IT.|","|Sensed, faintly: Shards of IT, resonating with the one you devoured.|","|Several lie within THE Undersnow.|","|Others are stretched across existence, beyond your present reach. Some may rest in the hands of Legacies.|","...!","|This Domain lies beyond the sight of existence. No Judgment reaches here.|","|For now.|","...!","Noah sat in the dirt between the bean rows for a long time after the prompts stopped.","He could feel them. The Shards! Faint, very faint, like the warmth of distant fires felt through a closed door. Several of them below, deep in THE Undersnow, down past the Basal Floor, past the rift, somewhere in the frozen dark of the Evergrave and beyond. Others farther. Much farther. Scattered across existence, some of them humming in places beyond his sight, some of them, he was almost sure, held tight in the grip of someone very old.","Lucy’s letter said it was beyond fixing. Lucy’s letter said there was no path, and no sky, and no hope for Those Who Remain. Lucy had been there. Lucy knew more than anyone alive about what had broken, and how badly.","Noah looked down at his dirty hands.","\"Nothing is impossible,\" he said quietly, to himself, to the farm, to the scarecrow in the wheat.","The breeze moved through the beans.","\"Whether the path is fully closed or not,\" Noah said , \"I will decide that. Not her. Not existence. Me.\"","He picked up the hoe again, and stood, and looked out over the half-tended garden and the gold wheat and the six apple trees, and felt the faint warmth of the Shards far below, calling.","\" IT ,\" he said, \" is a good place to start.\"","...!"]},{"number":5837,"title":"Chapter 5837: Chapter 5836: Order II","paragraphs":["Noah set the hoe back against the fence where he had found it.","He looked at the garden one last time. Weeds lay piled at the end of the path, the beans stood tied to their poles, and the apples sat in the bucket by the well. It was unfinished. A farm always was.","He walked back to the doorway at the edge of the fields and stopped.","A hundred Immense Ones were waiting on the other side of it. He could feel their attention pressing faintly against the door like a crowd against a window. The moment he stepped through, they would want answers.","He wanted a few of his own first.","So he lifted THE Orb of Immensity and asked it, plainly, for somewhere quiet.","The Orb answered!","Lucy’s script turned inside it in slow gold rings, and the tiny door at its heart swung to face a different way. When Noah stepped through the brightness, he stood on the shoulder of a lonley mountain at the far edge of the Legacy, snow up to his knees, wind howling across bare rock. An old shrine sat half buried in the drifts. Below it, a frozen pond lay cracked straight across from the war.","The Legacy had heard its Son, and sent him where nobody would be watching!","Noah sat down in the snow, crossed his legs, and closed his gold eyes.","Then he let his Dream go as he wanted to test out his existence...at Order II.","It went out of him like breath on a cold morning, and it kept going.","Over the shrine. Over the cracked pond. Down the mountain’s side and across the valley below, over the purple-gold rivers running dark between the peaks, up the next mountain and the next. His Dream spread across the snow like a tide coming in over a beach, soft and wide and quiet, and everything it touched became something he could feel.","He felt the Keepers’ Roads winding between the mountains, every stone of them. He felt the Existential Conduits rising out of the rivers, every thread of light in their columns. Then came the thousand Elsedimension Mountains, one after another after another, and then, as his Dream sank into them, he felt what lay inside.","Dimensions!","Every mountain held them. Some held one, vast and quiet. Some held dozens, stacked inside the stone like rooms in a great house. And inside those Dimensions, Observable Existences, turning slowly in their own skies, each one full of light and motion and life.","Domains, Wheels, Frequencies, Cosmos, Galaxies, Seas. Forests under strange suns. Peoples living out their lives inside the mountains of a Legacy they would only ever know from within.","His Dream passed through all of it, and all of it began, very faintly, to dream.","He felt the lives in them, all at once rather than one at a time. Countless points of light scattered through the Legacy like stars through a night sky, each one a life, each one going about its day.","A child running down a street in a city inside a mountain; a farmer in a field under a sky with three moons; a Progeny meditating on a monastary terrace, a Root humming in her chest; a Keeper sweeping snow off the steps of a throne.","He felt the Immense Ones!","They burned among the lesser lights like suns. These were apart from the hundred in Lucy’s Lecture Hall; that place sat apart from everything else, a bright sealed knot in the weavings of the Legacy, too tightly woven for his Dream to enter. These were the others.","The Immense who kept to their own mountains. Dozens of them, scattered across the Legacy, each one deep, each one different. One sat alone on a peak of red stone, unmoving, its Profundity going down past his sight.","Another drifted through a Dimension of endless water, singing to itself. A third walked the Keepers’ Roads in the shape of an old woman with a basket, and the snow fell differently around her.","Every one of them went on, unaware of him!","His Dream lay over the whole Legacy, touching every one of them, and every head stayed exactly where it was. The old woman with the basket walked on, the singer in the water kept singing, and the Immense One on the red peak sat as still as it had sat for Ages.","His dreaming slid past their senses entirely!","Noah sat very still in the snow on his lonely mountain, and let that settle.","He went deeper!","Beneath the mountains, beneath the purple-gold rivers, beneath the snow-buried floor of the whole Legacy, his Dream found something unexpected.","Domains!","Existential Immense Domains, sunk into the foundations of the Legacy like vaults beneath a palace. Dozens of them. Sealed, silent, dark. His Dream slipped into the first one, and found it full of stone.","Statues!","They stood in rows in the dark, vast and still. Statues of Immense Ones, every one of them different. One the shape of a great Sphinx with antlers like the branches of a winter forest.","Another, a woman made of interlocking rings. A tower with eyes. A beast so large its head was lost in the dark above. Some as small as a man. Some larger than the Domain that held them, somehow, their edges trailing away into a scale his Dream could barely hold.","And every one of them was sleeping!","He could feel it. Under the stone, something breathed. Slowly. Once an Age, perhaps. A Profundity in every statue, deep and quiet and enormous, curled up in the dark like a seed in winter ground.","He moved to the next Domain. Statues. The next. Statues. Dozens of Domains, hundreds of statues, all of them Immense, all of them asleep, all of them hidden beneath a Legacy whose living Immense Ones walked over their heads every day and kept every word about them to themselves.","| Sensed: Existential Immense Domains beneath THE Legacy of THE Acharya of Immensity.|","|Within them: Immense Ones, in the form of statues, sleeping.|","|Their nature: ?????|","...!","Noah’s breath went out of him, slowly.","Who were they? Lucy’s students, who had remained and found it too much to bear? Companions of the leavers, put to sleep before the crossing? Something the Legacy had chosen to forget? Did Moriarty know? Did the Thinker?","The answers lay beyond him, for now. He held the questions, and kept going.","There was more to learn, and he learned it fast.","Each of those countless lights scattered across the Legacy, every Progeny, every Provenance Lifeform, every being with a Root humming in its chest, lay inside his Dream. He could feel their Roots. He could feel the edges of them.","And he understood, with a cold and perfect clarity, what that meant.","If he wished it, he could end them. From here. A Root-holder on a mountain at the other end of the Legacy, meditating peacefully on a terrace, would simply stop. He could dream their end as he had dreamed the Guards’ ends on the Basal Floor, and its source would stay hidden from them forever. Or he could open his mouth on this lonely mountain, and their Roots would come to him across the whole Legacy and go down into his Tree.","He could be anywhere! He reached out to the monastery terrace, and his Dream gathered there, and for a moment he was standing beside the meditating Progeny, close enough to see the snow on her eyelashes. She kept her eyes closed.","He reached to the water Dimension and stood beside the singing Immense One, close enough to hear the words of its song. It sang on.","He could stand beside a Newly Risen Immense One in its own Domain, and strike, and it would feel only the blow, after it had already landed.","All of it was his to do. Across the whole breadth of a Legacy!","This was his power! His Infinite Dream!","Noah opened his eyes.","The snow fell on his lonely mountain. Far below, the cracked pond lay quiet.","He thought, calmly, that this was what it was to be a dreamer at Order II. To lie over a whole Legacy like the night lies over a sleeping town, seeing every window, every lamp, every life, and to be seen by none of them. Every one of those lights was a choice he could make. End it. Keep it. Eat it. Leave it alone. Watching them from here, he could see every way each of them might go, every branch, every future, all of it laid out like the lines on an open palm.","It would have been very easy to stop seeing them as people.","He refused to let himself. He looked at the child running down the street inside the mountain, and made himself see a child. And on the terrace, the Progeny: he saw the snow on her eyelashes.","Then he let his Dream draw back, slowly, from all of them.","Power like this was a grand thing. He would carry it as he carried everything else, and use it when he chose.","At the very edge of his withdrawing Dream, in the bright sealed knot of the Lecture Hall, something clicked.","A single bead, sliding along a string.","Noah went still!","He waited. Silence followed: one click, faint as a pin dropped in snow, and then stillness.","Perhaps it was nothing.","He doubted it.","—","He tested the rest quickly.","THE Keystone Dream first. He looked at the old shrine’s ward, a faint skin of protection laid down over its stones by some Progeny long ago, and the ward lit in his sight like a web of frost, every strand leading inward to a single rune cut into the lintel. He dreamed it loose, and the ward came apart in silence, falling away like frost melting off glass. Then he dreamed it held, and the ward knit itself back together, good as new.","Then he tried the Legacy itself, out of pure curiosity.","He followed Lucy’s weavings inward, every river and Conduit and mountain bound together in threads so old they had hardened into something like stone. He followed them down toward the place where they all had to meet.","And lost them!","They went down past his sight, into a Profundity his gold eyes were unable to follow. Lucy’s keystone lay below him. Far below. So did his own; when he turned THE Keystone Dream inward, it found only the endless trunk of his Tree going down past anything he could see.","Last, the edge of his reach. He pushed his Dream out past the farthest mountain of the Legacy, toward the cracked sky at its border, and tried to dream a single snowflake beyond the border into a Dimension.","The dream thinned as it went, stretching like honey pulled too far, until at the Legacy’s edge it simply stopped. Inside the border, a Dimension bloomed in the air, blue-gold, and drifted down into the drifts as a snowflake was made into a Dimension. Beyond it, the snowflake stayed a snowflake.","Order II: a Legacy’s whole breadth, everything inside it!","| Order II, measured.|","|Your Dream covers the whole domain of a Legacy. Within it, you perceive every Dimension, every Observable Existence, every Root, and every Immensity, and none perceive your dreaming.|","|Within it, you may stand anywhere as though dreaming there, and impose your power wherever you wish.|","|Within it, those who hold only Roots are yours to end, or to devour.|","|Within it, a Newly Risen Immensity will sense you only when your blow has landed.|","|Established and Ancient Immensities will sense you when you act near or upon them.|","...!","|A notice, on your progress.|","|The Sap thickens as it nears a Bough.|","|You rose swiftly, carried by a Shard of IT. That was a gift, and gifts of that kind are rare. From here, your Tree grows at its true pace.|","|The final stretch toward the Second Bough will demand far more than the first. Ordinary loot will barely stir the Sap. Only grand loot will move it: the corpses of the Immense, the Ergospheres of Roots, and more.|","|Sap risen toward the Second Bough: 90%.|","...!","Noah read it twice, and almost laughed out loud!","Ten percent. And those ten percent would cost him more than the ninety before them.","Okay!","But he learned a great deal.","A Dream that covered a whole Legacy, unseen. Every Root inside it his to end or eat. Newly Risen Immense, open to him before they knew he was there. THE Keystone Dream, proven. A secret beneath the Legacy that its own Immense Ones had kept silent about.","He was stronger than he had ever been. And somewhere under the Legacy, a few hundred Immense Ones were sleeping in stone.","He turned his face toward the floor of everything.","Beneath the Legacy, beneath the snow, beneath the frozen dark of the Basal Floor, he could feel them now that he was quiet: several warmths, faint and far down, calling to the grain of IT in him like coals answering a spark.","Shards below. Unclaimed!","When he went down into THE Evergrave, he would let his Dream go there too to learn.","Noah lifted the Orb. The tiny door at its heart turned back toward the Lecture Hall, and opened.","He stepped through, and came out at the bottom of a bowl of obsidian and gold, where more than a hundred Immense Ones were still sitting exactly where he had left them, leaning forward on their thrones.","And on the innermost ring, the Thinker’s beads clicked once, slowly, as he passed."]},{"number":5838,"title":"Chapter 5838: Chapter 5837: THE Evergrave! I","paragraphs":["Every gaze in Lucy’s Lecture Hall landed on him at once.","More than a hundred Immensities, each one a weight, each one a question, and all of them looking at his eyes. Gold, as before, pupil-less and bright. And drifting in the gold, a fleck of obsidian, new since he left.","Moriarty rose halfway from his throne. \"THE Legacy’s Son,\" he said. \"What did you find?\"","Noah had pondered on this question.","The farm, the letter, the garden, the hoe, the grain of something unbearably heavy turned up in the soil: all of it was his now, and he had already decided how much of it this hall would know.","He would keep many things to himself as there were too many monsters in Existence, and he was just up and coming!","\"Lucy left behind a legacy,\" he said. \"A way of...seeing.\"","A murmur ran through the rings!","\"It lets me see possible paths.\" He looked up at the endless tiers. \"That path lies with IT as many here already knew.\"","\"IT is no longer whole,\" Noah went on. \"IT was shattered, long ago, and its pieces were stretched out across existence. Scattered. Lost. Any mention of Immense Ones holding it is merely false, as what they hold at most is... a piece of IT.\"","He opened his hand. \"What Lucy left behind has let me sense where some of those pieces may be.\"","His existence hummed as he said this!","\"If we gather the pieces of IT,\" he said, \"all of them...\"","He let the words hang, and looked around the bowl at every one of them. \"I can use the methodology Lucy left behind to potentially open up a pathway. There... may no longer be Those Who Remain!\"","WAA!","The hall went utterly silent!","He bullshitted them so calmly as his existence didnt even flutter!","Moriarty took off his spectacles. He sat with them in one tentacle, looking at Noah for a very long moment, and something in his crimson eyes cracked open.","\"Where...can we find them?\"","\"Some of them are close,\" Noah said. \"Others are far. I can feel them as you feel a fire through a closed door. Warmth, and a direction. Across existence, and in... THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering too.\"","Discussion bloomed as many talked amongst themselves, but Noah had laid the seeds to send others looking, and to use Immense Ones as his own personal valets to get what he wanted!","Moriarty put his spectacles back on and rose fully.","\"We will need to move,\" he said. \"All of us. Soon!\"","The hall agreed with him in a long, low rumble!","What came next took a while.","Discussions on where The Immense Ones of The Legacy would go based on where Noah felt a Shard of IT might be!","Moriarty laid out the dangers plainly. THE Keepers of Existence had come into this Legacy for Noah, and THE Sealed One had apparently been given or claimed access to IT as he may have a shard.","There wers other Legacies too as Existence was vast and filled with boundless terrors. Established Immense Ones were abundant. Ancient Immensities were abundant, and there were likely those above lying in wait for when any answers provided themselves!","Noah even wondered where someone like Vakochev stood as he had to at least be Ancient, right?","\"Everywhere we go,\" Moriarty said, \"assume other Legacies are already there. Assume others are ahead.\"","That sobered the hall more than anything else that day!","Then Moriarty turned back to him.","\"And THE Legacy’s Son,\" he said. \"Where will you go?\"","Noah smiled!","\"Where it is coldest.\" he said.","The hall quieted.","He didn’t say anything else as only THE THINKER and Ling truly knew what he meant with this!","The Thinker spoke quietly to him at this time.","|\"Immense Ones who go into THE Undersnow,\"| he said mildly, |\"tend not to come back. You can be considered an Immense One now as you may face a heavier rejection, will things be okay?\"|","His own back, where the frost-wound leaked, he left unremarked.","\"I know,\" Noah sent back mentally. \"That is why I am going alone. You may need to take Ling looking elsewhere. Take Poona as well and see if you can grasp any of the Shards in THE Chrysalis!\"","...!","Ling, on the arm of her father’s throne, seemed to almost hear being talked about as she frowned.","But Noah had decided!","Information was shared and given in a limited fashion as many Immensities began to move!","The Council broke near what felt a few hours.","Achilles was waiting on the Plain of Accord, Rose wrapped in his cloak.","Among The Immense Ones setting off...many would take their Progeny and those with Roots to search across Existence as Achilles would be among many who would search across Existence.","The Shards of IT had been stretched out across existence for ages and had not been found. Being Immense did not matter as something not Immense could find it...so long as they were looking in the right place.","Like this...an entire Legacy was slowly mobilized!","—","Noah’s existence remained steadfast as he stretched himself out in multiple areas.","The Basal Floor was quiet without anyone beside him!","Noah crossed it alone. Ling and Poona were on their way to THE Chrysalis of THE First Sundering with the Thinker. Ruination and THE Infiniverse still slept in their cocoons. For the first time since he had come into this winter, nobody walked at his side, and nobody’s voice was in his head. Even Atlas had gone quiet!","He found he liked it.","As for this first region of THE Undersnow...half the floor was gone. The great frozen plain where the Warden had sat for Ages had broken into a thousand drifting pieces when Ling kicked him off his ring, and those pieces still turned slowly through the dark like the wreck of a sunken fleet. Slabs of ice the size of mountains. Pillars of frost with frozen challengers still locked inside them, faces pressed to the glass. Torn Dimensions hanging between it all, their skies gone black.","He walked on the empty air between them, and the cold came up to meet him.","It was a different cold. Up here, it had only pressed. Down there, past the north, it pulled. It caught at every part of him and tugged, patient and steady, downward. The Long Night’s cold that had lived in him since the frozen underworld stirred in answer, eager, as if it knew the way home.","He let it pull!","The rift split the dark from top to bottom.","He stood at its edge and looked down. Blue ice, glitering with frost so old it had turned to glass, falling away into a blue so deep it swallowed his sight. Somewhere far below lay THE Evergrave of THE Unthawed Ages.","He stepped off the edge!","The walls rushed past in great blue sheets, and things lay inside them. Bones first, whole skeletons curled up as if they had lain down to sleep and stayed asleep. Then bigger shapes. A hand the size of a Dimension pressed flat against the inside of the wall, fingers spread, as if something had tried to push its way out and frozen in the trying. An eye a mile across, wide open. A mouth.","They were all looking up!","Noah looked back at them as he fell, and felt, under the cold, something older. A pressure on the back of his neck. Faint, for now.","He hit the bottom!","The gate filled the floor of the rift from wall to wall.","It was a ribcage. Each rib a curving pillar of white bone thicker than a city wall, rising out of the ice and arching inward to meet its twin along a spine far overhead. Something enormous had died here, long before the First Sundering, and its chest had become a door. A skin of frost lay over the whole of it, thick and old, put there by something that wanted the living kept out.","Noah looked at it with THE Keystone Dream.","The seal lit up in his sight, a web of frost across every rib, so dense and tangled that for a moment he saw only more of it. He followed the strands inward. They ran up the ribs and along the spine, thousands of them, all leaning toward one point at the very top of the arch, where a single small bone glowed.","That one!","He reached for it with his Dream. It fought him, cold and stubborn, the weight of something very old refusing something young. He leaned in. The grain of IT in his chest pulsed once, deep and sure, and the fleck of obsidian in his gold eyes brightened.","CRACK!","The little bone slid out of its place and drifted up off the spine. Every strand of the seal let go at once, falling away from the top down like snow shaken off a branch.","The gate stood open!","He walked through. Behind him, he dreamed the bone back into its place, and the frost closed over the ribs again.","—","The first thing he saw was the sun!","It hung high in a sky of deep frozen blue, round and white and perfectly bright. A dead star. It shone on everything and warmed nothing, and its light on his face felt like snowmelt.","Beneath it lay the Evergrave.","A Dimension, or the bones of one. Light years of distance of Streets of black ice ran out from the gate in straight lines wider than rivers, so smooth they held the dead sun’s reflection. Towers and halls and houses lined them, built for bodies other than human, dead so long their shapes had stopped making sense. A few windows glowed a faint blue. Shapes moved slowly behind some of them, as if every step cost them something.","And over all of it, the anger!","It came down on him the moment he passed the gate. Heavy, and constant, and old. It settled on the back of his neck like a hand and stayed there. The anger soaked the ice under his feet and the dead sun overhead and every stone of every frozen house. It had been here so long that it had stopped being a feeling and become the weather.","And it looked at him. The only living thing in its home.","| You have entered the place where existence keeps its anger.|","|It will press on you.|","|It will remember you.|","...!","Noah rolled his shoulders under the weight, and smiled.","Across the street, a door creaked open.","A dead thing stood in it, weaker than anything with a Root. Tall, thin, wrapped in rags stiff with frost, its face a grey shape with dark hollows where its eyes had been. It had come to the door slowly, drawn by something it had no name for.","Then it felt him!","It flinched back so hard it hit the doorframe. Its hands came up in front of its face as if he were a fire roaring in its doorway. A sound came out of it, thin and cracked, a word in some language older than any he knew. Noah understood it anyway.","Warm.","It said the word as a man alone in the dark might say knife.","Then it was gone, the door slamming, its footsteps scraping away inside. Up and down the street, the blue windows went dark one after another.","Noah watched them go out.","He had walked into many places in his life. This was the first where warmth was the thing people hid from.","Night Lifeforms here were interesting!","None antagonized him so far, so he didn’t rush out to be a genocidal maniac just yet.","He sat down on the black ice, crossed his legs, closed his gold eyes, and let his Dream go.","It went out over the Evergrave soft and wide and silent, as it had gone over the Legacy, rolling down the streets and in through the dark windows and out across the frozen land beyond. The Evergrave was bigger than any Legacy. His Dream covered only part of it before it thinned and stopped. Maybe a tenth.","He felt the dead. Thousands upon thosuands of them, in the city light years vast, alone, kept awake in the cold. Every one of them went on, unaware of him passing.","He felt them gathered in families. Clans and Provenance Lineages. Each one held a stretch of the city or the frozen land beyond it, with high walls of ice, banners of stitched skin, and a strong one at the center. The clan heads burned among the lesser Night Lifeforms like cold suns, deep and dangerous, every one of them Immense. Newly Risen, and even Established!","He felt the clans at work!","On a long street near the city’s edge, a column of weak dead stood chained together, and tall figures in grey robes walked the line with glass needles. Wherever a needle went in, something pale and gold drifted out of the dead and up into glass jars. The dead in that line went dimmer every time. Warm memories, he understood: a fire, a hand, a summer day. They were draining the last warmth out of the weakest dead and keeping it in jars.","Beyond the city, he felt fields where the dimmest of all had been planted upright in the ice, row on row, and set alight. They burned slowly, with a pale fire that gave no heat, and their light was carried away in lanterns to light the clans’ halls.","He felt four things that were bigger than the Provenance Lineages. Much bigger!","A king of frost on a throne of bone at the city’s heart, thin as a starved man, wearing a crown made of finger-bones; a cathedral shaped like a woman, with a choir inside her singing something that sounded like an apology; a giant drowned and frozen under a sea of black ice, screaming without a sound; and far off, at the very edge of his reach, something armored and old and utterly still, sitting before a gate.","Established , all four. Their Profundity went down past anything he could see. Four lords over all the Night Provenance Lineages!","And past the armored thing, past the gate, at the very center of the Evergrave, beyond the reach of his Dream, something pulsed against the grain of IT in his chest so hard it ached.","A Shard!","Noah drew his Dream back slowly, and opened his eyes.","A city of the dead, cold and awake. Clans of Immense dead, feeding on the weak. Four lords above the clans. And at the center of it all, behind every one of them, a single Shard of IT.","One Shard. Four Established Immense Ones. A great many lifeforms in the way. And his Sap needed feeding anyway.","He found he was looking forward to it!","Noah stood and brushed the frost off his knees.","Far down the street, at the edge of what he could see, something howled. Long and high and hungry, the sound of a hunting horn blown through a throat. Another howl answered it. Then another.","A dozen shapes came over the rooftops in a running pack, low and fast, their eyes cold points of blue. At their head ran something taller.","It was sniffing!","And then it turned, all at once, and looked straight down the long black street at the only warm thing in the Evergrave.","Towards him, and the glorious weavings of an Infinite Dream beginning to spill out of him!"]},{"number":5839,"title":"Chapter 5839: Chapter 5838: THE Evergrave! II","paragraphs":["They caught him on a frozen plain!","Noah let them as he had seen the pack turn toward him down the long black street, so he walked out to meet them, past the last frozen houses and onto a white plain so wide it could have held an Observable Existence, and he waited there with his hands at his sides while the pack poured in from every direction at once.","There were twelve of them.","Night Lifeforms. Each one was a monstrosity the size of a mountain range, built like a man stretched and starved and frozen until it was more bone than flesh. They moved on all fours across the ice, their spines rising in long ridges, their ribs open down their fronts like the doors of empty barns.","Their faces were long and eyeless. Their mouths opened from chin to chest. Where they ran, the frozen space of the Evergrave split around them and closed again behind, and the Dimensionality pouring off their bodies came down on the plain like a storm of black hail.","They were fucking ugly!","Each one held a Root, cold and huge, burning in its open chest like a dying Dimension.","They spread out around him in a ring that reached the horizon, and stopped, and lowered their long faces toward the small warm thing standing alone in the middle of them, and breathed him in.","Their leader came last.","It was larger than the rest by half. It walked upright, its head scraping the frozen sky, wrapped in a cloak stitched from the skins of dead Dimensions, their stars still frozen into the hide. Around its neck hung a chain of hearts. Warm things it had caught and eaten, frozen solid, each one the size of a city. Some of them were very small.","Its Root was stronger than theirs. A scion of its Lineage, then. Close to Immense, and very proud of it. Its face was a long grey blade of bone, and its eyes were two cold points of blue, each one wider than a sea.","It looked Noah up and down.","Then it laughed!","The sound of it rolled across the plain like an avalanche. \"Look at this,\" it said. \"A warm thing in the endless cold...\"","It walked a slow circle around him, each step cracking the ice for miles.","\"No Lineage. No lord. No banner. Walking our home like it owns them.\"","Its cold blue eyes narrowed. \"They told me a warm thing came through the gate. I laughed at them. Warm things don’t come to the Evergrave.\"","It bent down, and its long face filled the sky over him, its mouth opening to show teeth like frozen towers. \"And the ones that do don’t last.\"","The pack laughed with it, a dozen dry roars that shook the frozen sun.","The scion lowered its face further.","\"I haven’t tasted anything warm in Ages,\" it said softly. \" I’m going to take my time with you.\"","Noah looked at it.","He looked at the frozen hearts on their chain. Then at the twelve Night Lifeforms in their ring, their Roots stirring with hunger.","THE THINKER had tried to delve into the source of THE Long Night and was almost killed when he came down to THE Undersnow. It showed that anyone with Immensity who didn’t belong got an extremely heavy reaction.","Noah so far...everything had been mild for him as he may just be able to uncover and understand more! He stretched his neck as his voice boomed out.","\"Leave,\" Noah said. \"Find something else to hunt, and leave me alone.\"","The plain went quiet!","Then the scion laughed again, louder, and the pack laughed with it, and the scion lifted one vast hand, and the cold of its Root began to gather.","Fine!","Noah looked at the twelve for but an instant.","An Instant!","And...","They stopped!","All of them, at once, in the middle of their laughter. Their mouths stayed open. Their teeth stayed bared. Their Roots, those huge cold stars burning in their open chests, simply went out, like twelve candles pinched between finger and thumb.","And the twelve monstrosities, one by one, sank down onto the ice and lay still, each one landing with a sound like a mountain falling, until the whole plain shook with it.","It took less than a breath!","The scion’s laugh died in its throat!","It stood over him with its hand still raised, staring at the twelve fallen giants around it, and for the first time, its cold blue eyes showed fear instead of hunger.","Then it struck!","Its Root blazed. The cold of the Chase came out of it, the hunting cold of its whole Lineage, a cold that had run down and frozen prey across a hundred Dimensions. It came down on Noah from every side at once in a storm of frozen Dimensionality, spears of black ice each long enough to pin a Dimension to the sky, the space around him clenching shut like a fist to hold him still for the killing.","Noah stood in the middle of it, and dreamed.","The storm reached him, and turned into a dream.","Every spear of black ice softened as it came, blurring at the edges, and passed through him like a memory of rain, and was gone. The fist of frozen space closed around him and closed on empty air. The cold of the Chase, the cold that had hunted down a hundred Dimensions, touched his night-dark skin, and his skin stayed exactly as warm as it had been.","He stood exactly where he had been. Every constellation under his skin burned steady.","\"What... are you?\" the scion hissed.","It struck again, and again, backing away across the plain, each blow vaster than the last, tearing the frozen land open around them in canyons that ran to the horizon. Noah walked through all of it. The canyons healed behind him as he passed, the ice dreaming itself whole again under his feet.","Then he was in front of it!","\"Get back!\" It brought both of its enormous hands down on him at once, with the whole weight of its body and its Root behind them, enough force to crack a Dimension in half.","Noah looked up at the hands, and dreamed them still.","They stopped in the air above him, frozen in place, trembling. The scion strained against its own arms with everything it had, and they stayed exactly where he had dreamed them.","\"You should have left,\" Noah said.","He closed his hand.","The scion came apart!","It happened from the inside. Every joint of its huge frozen body opened at once, every limb tearing loose along every seam, its ribs splitting outward, its long bone face cracking from the crown down. Its Root guttered, flared once like a star about to go out, and went dark. What was left of it came down across the plain in pieces the size of mountains, and the chain of frozen hearts broke and scattered across the ice.","The plain was silent!","Thirteen giants lay broken across the frozen plain under a dead sun, and Noah stood among them, small and warm, without a single mark on him, breathing slowly.","It should have been over.","He looked at them for a long moment.","Twelve hunters and their scion. Kept awake in the cold for Ages, hunting the weak for scraps of warmth, wearing the hearts of children as trophies. He had ended them without a second thought, and he would do it again.","And yet...","Something about how they lay on the ice made him think of a great white panda, sitting on a frozen ring at the bottom of the Basal Floor for Ages, holding the door shut, wishing with every part of itself that it could stand up and walk away.","THE Vigil That Wished to Rise.","He had taken that dream from the Warden when he killed him. He had kept it. It had sat inside him ever since, quiet and patient, a dream that only ever wanted one thing.","Here, in a place full of dead stuck forever in place, he could feel it stirring.","Noah closed his gold eyes and reached for it.","The dream came up out of him slow and heavy, blue and gold and very old, and as it came, it spread out across the whole frozen plain and settled over the thirteen fallen giants like a blanket of light. He could feel each of them under it. Their Roots were out. Their bodies were broken. But somewhere far down in each of them, under the cold and the hunger and the long, long Ages of being kept, there was something left. A wish. The oldest wish any of the dead in this place had. A Dream!","To move again. To get up.","To rise!","Noah opened his eyes.","\" Dream ,\" he said.","HUUM!","The bodies shuddered!","One by one, across the frozen plain, the giants moved. A hand the size of a city flexed. A long bone face lifted from the ice. They pushed themselves up on shaking arms, slowly, as a man gets up after a very long sickness, and the whole plain trembled as they stood. Twelve monstrosities, their ribs open, the cold stars in their chests turned to faint lights of blue and gold. And their scion, whole again, rising last and largest, the chain of hearts gone from its neck.","Their eyes had changed. In place of the cold blue points burned the color of Noah’s own dreaming.","They turned, all thirteen of them, to face him.","And they knelt!","The plain cracked under their knees for miles in every direction.","| THE Vigil That Wished to Rise has woken in the Evergrave.|","|Here, among the dead who cannot move on, the dream of the one who wished to stand becomes yours to give.|","|Those you kill, you may raise. They rise bound to your Dream, and loyal to it.|","|The Risen Dreams keep their skills and their memories, and a part of their strength. Never all of it. A risen thing is less than it was, but it can dream to be grander under you. Due to this being the first time, the corpses of these Risen Dreams and weavings were sacrificed for their emergence.|","|Each risen thing rests on your Dream. The more you raise, the heavier it grows.|","|Risen Dreams: 14.|","...!","Noah read the prompts, then looked up at the thirteen giants kneeling around him, and the massive shadow of the golden fat panda behind them!","The scion lowered its great face until it hung in the air just above him.","\"I can move,\" it said slowly. It looked at its own enormous hands. \"I... can move.\"","It flexed its fingers, one by one, each one a mountain.","Then, very quietly: \"Thank you.\"","Noah looked at them and nodded. Down here, nothing short of an Immensity could even touch him.","\"Get up,\" Noah told them.","They got up!","He looked toward the city’s heart, where a king of frost sat on a throne of bone, and beyond it, toward the center of everything, where the Shard of IT pulsed against his chest.","\"We’re going that way,\" he said. \"Follow me.\"","Fourteen giants fell in behind him, the ice shaking under every step!","Far away, beyond a hundred frozen streets, in a stronghold of ice the size of an Observable Existence, hung with banners stitched from the skins of dead Dimensions, The Night Provenance Lineage of The Chase felt its hunting party go silent.","Every hunter. All at once!","In the stronghold’s high hall, something that had been sitting very still for a long time rose from a seat of antlers. Skinless and vast, its muscles bare and frozen and gleeming, its body taller than the hall that held it, it rose until its flayed head broke through the roof and the cold of its Immensity spilled out over the Evergrave like a winter storm.","It walked out to where a horse of bare bones the size of a mountain range stood waiting in the snow.","The head of The Lineage of the Chase, a Newly Risen Immense One, swung up into its saddle, lifted its flayed face to the wind, and rode out to see what had killed its Hunters!"]},{"number":5840,"title":"Chapter 5840: Chapter 5839: First One Down!","paragraphs":["By the time Noah stopped, his Dream had already spread across the whole region.","It hung over the outer city like a low, soft cloud, blue and gold, drifting through the frozen streets and down into the dark windows and out across the white plains beyond. Everything under it went on, unaware. And everything the cloud touched, Noah knew.","His Risen Dreams moved around him on a frozen plain, fourteen giants sitting in the snow, the golden shadow of the panda lying at the back of them with its great head on its paws.","The prompts came quietly.","| Your Dream has settled over this region.|","|Observed: the Draining. Lines of the weakest dead, chained in their thousands. Their last warm memories drawn out of them by the Regent’s wardens, and carried away in jars.|","|The warmth flows inward, street by street, hall by hall towards a powerful Immense One- toward the throne of THE Gaunt Regent at the city’s heart.|","|From the Regent, it flows further inward still. Toward the center of the Evergrave.|","|Toward the Shard potential shard you have been feeling the pull of.|","...!","Noah eyes pulsed as he obtained more information about this place and its workings, but he would not be given any rest as he sensed a heavy brilliance coming straight at him!","It came from the north, from beyond the edge of his Dream, and it came fast as a sea of its Immensity barreled down!","The cold arrived before the thing that carried it. It fell across the plain in one long sweep, and where it passed, his Risen Dreams ended. Three giants, standing in the snow, simply stopped. Their bodies went grey from the inside, their blue-gold light going out like lamps at the end of their oil, and they crumbled into frozen dust where they sat.","Then the hunter came over the horizon!","| THE Flayed Huntsman- Newly Risen Immense One|","It was skinless, its whole body bare frozen muscle, red-black and glistning, larger than a mountain range, riding a horse of white bones that was larger still. Its head was a flayed skull with two cold blue lights burning deep in the sockets. And rolling ahead of it across the plain like a storm front came its Immensity.","An Immensity of Ending!","Noah had eaten a Provenance of Ending once, torn out of the Judgment that came for his evolution. He knew its taste. This was that same taste grown wild and vast and ancient, held by a hunter who had spent Ages learning to aim it. Snow ended where it passed. Ice ended. Air ended, leaving holes of nothing that the Evergrave rushed in to fill.","The Huntsman rode as its Immensity crashed through his army, and his Risen Dreams went grey and crumbled one after another. His scion, his first, roared and threw itself in the hunter’s path, and ended in the middle of its roar. At the back of the plain, the golden shadow of the panda stood up, looked at the hunter, and faded slowly into the snow.","All fourteen. In the space of a few breaths!","| Your Risen Dreams have been ended.|","|They are kept. What you have raised once, your Provenance remembers.|","|Whenever you wish, you may dream them risen again as they should be stronger to not die to the same thing again.|","...!","Noah stood up, alone on the plain, and looked at the hunter.","An Immense One who had frost and Immensity raging down from it as it looked ancient and aged, its voice echoing out.","|\" Those that don’t belong always make the biggest messes. Things that have lived since before The First Sundering, enjoying the long night, now ended by you...must you all always be so cruel? You...don’t even know what Ending truly is.\"|","HUUM!","The Huntsman came down off its horse, and the Evergrave began to end!","It aimed at everything around Noah first. Its Immensity poured out of it in a tide of cold so vast that the plain vanished under it in an instant, and then the frozen hills beyond the plain, and then the city’s outer streets, and then the sky over all of it. The tide rolled outward for light years!","Whole regions of the Evergrave simply stopped being. Mountains ended at their roots and toppled into nothing. Frozen rivers ended mid-flow. Towers of the dead ended with the dead still in them, their faces at the windows going grey and bloing away like ash.","It was clearing a hunting ground. Making a place where nothing existed but the hunter and its prey!","Was this the same fucker just admonishing Noah for Ending Night Lifeforms?!","Noah’s Dream moved!","It spread out of him behind the Ending, soft and patient, and wherever the hunter’s cold had erased something, his Dream found the shape of what had been there and laid it back down. Hills rose back out of the nothing, the snow settling on them as if it had been there all along. Streets ran back into place, house by house. The frozen rivers took up their flow again mid-ripple. It happened quietly, almost gently, as new skin closes over a cut, the whole broken region stitching itself back together light year by light year as fast as the Huntsman could tear it open.","The Huntsman saw it, and stopped!","Its cold blue lights fixed on him.","\"I can sense your existence looking for something. There are...no answers for you here. No recompense. Nothing that will satisfy you. Only...ENDINGS!\"","HUUM!","It came for him!","All of its Immensity, all at once, turned onto one small warm thing standing in the snow.","Ending fell on Noah like a sky collapsing!","And he was expectant to see how a Newly Risen Immensity would now fare against his Order II power!","It came from every direction, from above and below and from inside the air itself, and it was looking for a way in. It pressed against his skin, against his constellations, against the Tree in his chest, against the Dream that made him what he was, searching for any crack, any gap, any single place where it could get inside him and stop him as it had stopped everything else.","And it found layers!","Dream after dream after dream, wrapped around his body like the rings of a tree, every one of them deeper than the last. The Ending tore through the first layer, and found a second. It ended the second, and found a third already dreamed back over it.","It clawed at him with the full weight of Ages, and every layer it ended was dreamed whole again before it could reach the next, and underneath all of them, untouched, at the center of an ocean of dreams, stood Noah.","The way in stayed hidden from it.","Even the door stayed hidden!","Noah watched it search for a long moment. Then he took a step forward into it, and another, and he was through its storm and standing inches from its Immensity!","Oh!","It felt like standing before a cold furnace, but he was doing it! How unthinkable was it to even stand before a glimmer of Immensity days ago, but he was now standing unfettered with a full raging Immensity inches away?!","He looked up at it.","He hit it!","His fist went into the Huntsman’s shin, and the bare frozen muscle burst around his knuckles. Black-red blood sprayed out in a frozen fan that hung in the air and went on falling for miles. The hunter roared and brought a hand down on him with enough force to end Dimensions, and Noah caught it, and tore two of its fingers away, and climbed.","He went up its body with his hands. Into the muscle of its thigh. Into the cage of its ribs. Every handhold he took, he poured his Dream into it, straight from his palms into the hunter’s flesh, and every place his Dream went in, the hunter’s body began to change.","He was altering its Immensity!","Frozen muscle went soft and dreaming. Blood that had been ice for Ages thawed and ran. The hunter clawed at him, tore at him, ended layer after layer of the dreams around him, and he kept climbing, and kept pouring.","He reached its chest, drove both hands in to the wrist, and let everything go!","His Dream went into THE Flayed Huntsman like a flood into a cracked dam.","And he saw it!","All of it, at once, as he had seen the whole Legacy from a lonely mountain. The hunter’s Immensity of Ending lay open in front of him, every part of it, and he could see exactly what it was made of.","He saw the first thing it ever chased, Ages ago: a small warm creature running across the snow in some cycle long since gone, and the moment it caught it, and the moment that warmth went out under its hand. That was the root of it. Every Ending since had grown from that one.","He saw the Ages layered on top of that first kill like rings in a frozen trunk. Every hunt it had ever run, every Lineage brother it had hung in its antler trees, every fleeing thing it had stopped. Each one had added a layer of cold, and each layer had made the Ending sharper, and narrower, and hungrier.","He saw the shape of the Immensity itself. A long, thin thread of stopping, wound around and around a single wish, so tight that the hunter had forgotten the wish was there.","The wish was simple.","It wanted things to hold still. It wanted, more than anything, for the running to stop.","Noah understood it then, completely, from the inside, as only someone who has eaten Ending could. And understanding it, he knew exactly where to press.","He saw the Keystone of its Dream.","He closed his hands!","His Dream closed with them, around that one thin thread of stopping, around Ages of cold and the first kill at the bottom of it all, and he crushed it.","HUUUM!","The Ending broke!","It broke from the center outward. The Huntsman’s Immensity, Ages deep, came apart in Noah’s hands like ice under a hammer, and the cold went out of it all at once. The storm across the plain stopped, and blue-gold light filled the holes it had torn in the air.","Far away, across light years, the last regions it had ended stitched themselves back together under Noah’s Dream, and the dead in their towers blinked, and found themselves back at their windows.","|\"OOOOOH!\"|","The Huntsman screamed one last time. It came out of it as a long, thin, broken sound, and it went on for a long time, and then it stopped.","Noah pulled his hands free.","The hunter swayed, its skinless chest torn open, its blue lights flickering. It looked down at him one last time.","Then it fell!","It came down across the plain like a mountain range collapsing. Its vast body struck the ice so hard the whole region shook, and black-red blood spread out from it across the snow in a frozen sea. Snow went up in a wall that hid the dead sun. The ground cracked for miles in every direction, and the sound of it rolled out across the Evergrave and kept on rolling, down every street of the city of the dead, until every dead thing in every dark window had heard it.","Then, slowly, the snow came down.","Noah stood on the hunter’s chest!","He stood there in the falling snow, small and warm and untouched, the hunter’s frozen blood drying on his hands and arms to the shoulder. His gold eyes burned.","His Dream rolled off him in slow blue-gold tides across the broken plain, stitching the last of the cracks closed behind it. Under his feet, the head of the Night Provenance Lineage of the Chase lay still, its Immensity crushed, its blue lights out.","Across the plain, from the edges of the city, the dead had come to their windows. Hundreds of them. Thousands. Grey faces pressed to frozen glass, staring at the warm thing standing on the body of an Immense One.","Every one of them stayed silent!","Noah looked out over the plain at all of them.","His first Immense One in the Evergrave.","He found he wanted more! More, more, more!"]}]);
